      ],
      "children": [
        {
          "id": "/page/4/SectionHeader/0",
          "block_type": "SectionHeader",
          "html": "<h1><b>Preface</b></h1>",
          "polygon": [
            [
              128.6455078125,
              164.935546875
            ],
            [
              212.9150390625,
              164.935546875
            ],
            [
              212.9150390625,
              191.0
            ],
            [
              128.6455078125,
              191.0
            ]
          ],
          "children": null,
          "section_hierarchy": {
            "1": "/page/4/SectionHeader/0",
            "3": "/page/4/SectionHeader/1"
          },
          "images": {}
        },
        {
          "id": "/page/4/SectionHeader/1",
          "block_type": "SectionHeader",
          "html": "<h3><b>The strange history of this book</b></h3>",
          "polygon": [
            [
              128.86962890625,
              237.4453125
            ],
            [
              340.365234375,
              237.4453125
            ],
            [
              340.365234375,
              254.0
            ],
            [
              128.86962890625,
              254.0
            ]
          ],
          "children": null,
          "section_hierarchy": {
            "1": "/page/4/SectionHeader/0",
            "3": "/page/4/SectionHeader/1"
          },
          "images": {}
        },
        {
          "id": "/page/4/Text/2",
          "block_type": "Text",
          "html": "<p>In January 1999 I was preparing to teach an introductory programming class in Java. I had taught it three times and I was getting frustrated. The failure rate in the class was too high and, even for students who succeeded, the overall level of achievement was too low.</p>",
          "polygon": [
            [
              128.6455078125,
              263.162109375
            ],
            [
              527.73046875,
              263.162109375
            ],
            [
              527.73046875,
              299.126953125
            ],
            [
              128.6455078125,
              299.126953125
            ]
          ],
          "children": null,
          "section_hierarchy": {
            "1": "/page/4/SectionHeader/0",
            "3": "/page/4/SectionHeader/1"
          },
          "images": {}
        },
        {
          "id": "/page/4/Text/3",
          "block_type": "Text",
          "html": "<p>One of the problems I saw was the books. They were too big, with too much unnecessary detail about Java, and not enough high-level guidance about how to program. And they all suffered from the trap door effect: they would start out easy, proceed gradually, and then somewhere around Chapter 5 the bottom would fall out. The students would get too much new material, too fast, and I would spend the rest of the semester picking up the pieces.</p>",
          "polygon": [
            [
              128.9443359375,
              307.0546875
            ],
            [
              527.73046875,
              307.0546875
            ],
            [
              527.73046875,
              367.0
            ],
            [
              128.9443359375,
              367.0
            ]
          ],
          "children": null,
          "section_hierarchy": {
            "1": "/page/4/SectionHeader/0",
            "3": "/page/4/SectionHeader/1"
          },
          "images": {}
        },
        {
          "id": "/page/4/Text/4",
          "block_type": "Text",
          "html": "<p>Two weeks before the first day of classes, I decided to write my own book. My goals were:</p>",
          "polygon": [
            [
              128.49609375,
              374.73046875
            ],
            [
              527.1328125,
              374.73046875
            ],
            [
              527.1328125,
              386.0
            ],
            [
              128.49609375,
              386.0
            ]
          ],
          "children": null,
          "section_hierarchy": {
            "1": "/page/4/SectionHeader/0",
            "3": "/page/4/SectionHeader/1"
          },
          "images": {}
        },
        {
          "id": "/page/4/ListGroup/109",
          "block_type": "ListGroup",
          "html": "<p><ul><content-ref src='/page/4/ListItem/5'></content-ref><content-ref src='/page/4/ListItem/6'></content-ref><content-ref src='/page/4/ListItem/7'></content-ref><content-ref src='/page/4/ListItem/8'></content-ref></ul></p>",
          "polygon": [
            [
              143.0,
              397.16015625
            ],
            [
              527.73046875,
              397.16015625
            ],
            [
              527.73046875,
              504.0
            ],
            [
              143.0,
              504.0
            ]
          ],
          "children": [
            {
              "id": "/page/4/ListItem/5",
              "block_type": "ListItem",
              "html": "<li> Keep it short. It is better for students to read 10 pages than not read 50 pages.</li>",
              "polygon": [
                [
                  143.0,
                  397.16015625
                ],
                [
                  494.560546875,
                  397.16015625
                ],
                [
                  494.560546875,
                  409.0
                ],
                [
                  143.0,
                  409.0
                ]
              ],
              "children": null,
              "section_hierarchy": {
                "1": "/page/4/SectionHeader/0",
                "3": "/page/4/SectionHeader/1"
              },
              "images": {}
            },
            {
              "id": "/page/4/ListItem/6",
              "block_type": "ListItem",
              "html": "<li> Be careful with vocabulary. I tried to minimize the jargon and define each term at first use.</li>",
              "polygon": [
                [
                  143.0,
                  417.65625
                ],
                [
                  527.73046875,
                  417.65625
                ],
                [
                  527.73046875,
                  441.0
                ],
                [
                  143.0,
                  441.0
                ]
              ],
              "children": null,
              "section_hierarchy": {
                "1": "/page/4/SectionHeader/0",
                "3": "/page/4/SectionHeader/1"
              },
              "images": {}
            },
            {
              "id": "/page/4/ListItem/7",
              "block_type": "ListItem",
              "html": "<li> Build gradually. To avoid trap doors, I took the most difficult topics and split them into a series of small steps.</li>",
              "polygon": [
                [
                  143.0,
                  448.59375
                ],
                [
                  527.431640625,
                  448.59375
                ],
                [
                  527.431640625,
                  472.0
                ],
                [
                  143.0,
                  472.0
                ]
              ],
              "children": null,
              "section_hierarchy": {
                "1": "/page/4/SectionHeader/0",
                "3": "/page/4/SectionHeader/1"
              },
              "images": {}
            },
            {
              "id": "/page/4/ListItem/8",
              "block_type": "ListItem",
              "html": "<li> Focus on programming, not the programming language. I included the minimum useful subset of Java and left out the rest.</li>",
              "polygon": [
                [
                  143.0,
                  480.69140625
                ],
                [
                  527.73046875,
                  480.69140625
                ],
                [
                  527.73046875,
                  504.0
                ],
                [
                  143.0,
                  504.0
                ]
              ],
              "children": null,
              "section_hierarchy": {
                "1": "/page/4/SectionHeader/0",
                "3": "/page/4/SectionHeader/1"
              },
              "images": {}
            }
          ],
          "section_hierarchy": {
            "1": "/page/4/SectionHeader/0",
            "3": "/page/4/SectionHeader/1"
          },
          "images": null
        },
        {
          "id": "/page/4/Text/9",
          "block_type": "Text",
          "html": "<p>I needed a title, so on a whim I chose <i>How to Think Like a Computer Scientist</i>.</p>",
          "polygon": [
            [
              128.6455078125,
              517.0
            ],
            [
              460.1953125,
              517.0
            ],
            [
              460.1953125,
              527.09765625
            ],
            [
              128.6455078125,
              527.09765625
            ]
          ],
          "children": null,
          "section_hierarchy": {
            "1": "/page/4/SectionHeader/0",
            "3": "/page/4/SectionHeader/1"
          },
          "images": {}
        },
        {
          "id": "/page/4/Text/10",
          "block_type": "Text",
          "html": "<p>My first version was rough, but it worked. Students did the reading, and they understood enough that I could spend class time on the hard topics, the interesting topics and (most important) letting the students practice.</p>",
          "polygon": [
            [
              128.9443359375,
              535.9921875
            ],
            [
              527.73046875,
              535.9921875
            ],
            [
              527.73046875,
              570.796875
            ],
            [
              128.9443359375,
              570.796875
            ]
          ],
          "children": null,
          "section_hierarchy": {
            "1": "/page/4/SectionHeader/0",
            "3": "/page/4/SectionHeader/1"
          },
          "images": {}
        },
        {
          "id": "/page/4/Text/11",
          "block_type": "Text",
          "html": "<p>I released the book under the GNU Free Documentation License, which allows users to copy, modify, and distribute the book.</p>",
          "polygon": [
            [
              128.794921875,
              579.3046875
            ],
            [
              528.029296875,
              579.3046875
            ],
            [
              528.029296875,
              602.0
            ],
            [
              128.794921875,
              602.0
            ]
          ],
          "children": null,
          "section_hierarchy": {
            "1": "/page/4/SectionHeader/0",
            "3": "/page/4/SectionHeader/1"
          },
          "images": {}
        },
        {
          "id": "/page/4/Text/12",
          "block_type": "Text",
          "html": "<p>What happened next is the cool part. Jeff Elkner, a high school teacher in Virginia, adopted my book and translated it into Python. He sent me a copy of his translation, and I had the unusual experience of learning Python by reading my own book. As Green Tea Press, I published the first Python version in 2001.</p>",
          "polygon": [
            [
              128.9443359375,
              610.62890625
            ],
            [
              527.73046875,
              610.62890625
            ],
            [
              527.73046875,
              657.03515625
            ],
            [
              128.9443359375,
              657.03515625
            ]
          ],
          "children": null,
          "section_hierarchy": {
