        },
        {
          "id": "/page/24/SectionHeader/1",
          "block_type": "SectionHeader",
          "html": "<h3><b>1.2 What is a program?</b></h3>",
          "polygon": [
            [
              127.30078125,
              85.8515625
            ],
            [
              288.966796875,
              84.3046875
            ],
            [
              288.966796875,
              100.0
            ],
            [
              127.30078125,
              100.93359375
            ]
          ],
          "children": null,
          "section_hierarchy": {
            "1": "/page/22/SectionHeader/1",
            "3": "/page/24/SectionHeader/1"
          },
          "images": {}
        },
        {
          "id": "/page/24/Text/2",
          "block_type": "Text",
          "html": "<p>A <b>program</b> is a sequence of instructions that specifies how to perform a computation. The computation might be something mathematical, such as solving a system of equations or finding the roots of a polynomial, but it can also be a symbolic computation, such as searching and replacing text in a document or (strangely enough) compiling a program.</p>",
          "polygon": [
            [
              128.9443359375,
              112.341796875
            ],
            [
              526.0,
              112.341796875
            ],
            [
              526.0,
              160.0
            ],
            [
              128.9443359375,
              160.0
            ]
          ],
          "children": null,
          "section_hierarchy": {
            "1": "/page/22/SectionHeader/1",
            "3": "/page/24/SectionHeader/1"
          },
          "images": {}
        },
        {
          "id": "/page/24/Text/3",
          "block_type": "Text",
          "html": "<p>The details look different in different languages, but a few basic instructions appear in just about every language:</p>",
          "polygon": [
            [
              128.9443359375,
              169.76953125
            ],
            [
              526.53515625,
              169.76953125
            ],
            [
              526.53515625,
              193.0
            ],
            [
              128.9443359375,
              193.0
            ]
          ],
          "children": null,
          "section_hierarchy": {
            "1": "/page/22/SectionHeader/1",
            "3": "/page/24/SectionHeader/1"
          },
          "images": {}
        },
        {
          "id": "/page/24/Text/4",
          "block_type": "Text",
          "html": "<p><b>input:</b> Get data from the keyboard, a file, or some other device.</p>",
          "polygon": [
            [
              128.42138671875,
              206.89453125
            ],
            [
              410.291015625,
              206.89453125
            ],
            [
              410.291015625,
              218.0
            ],
            [
              128.42138671875,
              218.0
            ]
          ],
          "children": null,
          "section_hierarchy": {
            "1": "/page/22/SectionHeader/1",
            "3": "/page/24/SectionHeader/1"
          },
          "images": {}
        },
        {
          "id": "/page/24/Text/5",
          "block_type": "Text",
          "html": "<p><b>output:</b> Display data on the screen or send data to a file or other device.</p>",
          "polygon": [
            [
              128.794921875,
              227.583984375
            ],
            [
              447.943359375,
              227.583984375
            ],
            [
              447.943359375,
              239.0
            ],
            [
              128.794921875,
              239.0
            ]
          ],
          "children": null,
          "section_hierarchy": {
            "1": "/page/22/SectionHeader/1",
            "3": "/page/24/SectionHeader/1"
          },
          "images": {}
        },
        {
          "id": "/page/24/Text/6",
          "block_type": "Text",
          "html": "<p><b>math:</b> Perform basic mathematical operations like addition and multiplication.</p>",
          "polygon": [
            [
              128.49609375,
              248.466796875
            ],
            [
              478.423828125,
              248.466796875
            ],
            [
              478.423828125,
              260.0
            ],
            [
              128.49609375,
              260.0
            ]
          ],
          "children": null,
          "section_hierarchy": {
            "1": "/page/22/SectionHeader/1",
            "3": "/page/24/SectionHeader/1"
          },
          "images": {}
        },
        {
          "id": "/page/24/Text/7",
          "block_type": "Text",
          "html": "<p><b>conditional execution:</b> Check for certain conditions and execute the appropriate code.</p>",
          "polygon": [
            [
              129.09375,
              270.509765625
            ],
            [
              512.19140625,
              270.509765625
            ],
            [
              512.19140625,
              281.724609375
            ],
            [
              129.09375,
              281.724609375
            ]
          ],
          "children": null,
          "section_hierarchy": {
            "1": "/page/22/SectionHeader/1",
            "3": "/page/24/SectionHeader/1"
          },
          "images": {}
        },
        {
          "id": "/page/24/Text/8",
          "block_type": "Text",
          "html": "<p><b>repetition:</b> Perform some action repeatedly, usually with some variation.</p>",
          "polygon": [
            [
              128.6455078125,
              291.005859375
            ],
            [
              453.0234375,
              291.005859375
            ],
            [
              453.0234375,
              302.0
            ],
            [
              128.6455078125,
              302.0
            ]
          ],
          "children": null,
          "section_hierarchy": {
            "1": "/page/22/SectionHeader/1",
            "3": "/page/24/SectionHeader/1"
          },
          "images": {}
        },
        {
          "id": "/page/24/Text/9",
          "block_type": "Text",
          "html": "<p>Believe it or not, that's pretty much all there is to it. Every program you've ever used, no matter how complicated, is made up of instructions that look pretty much like these. So you can think of programming as the process of breaking a large, complex task into smaller and smaller subtasks until the subtasks are simple enough to be performed with one of these basic instructions.</p>",
          "polygon": [
            [
              128.49609375,
              314.595703125
            ],
            [
              527.73046875,
              314.595703125
            ],
            [
              527.73046875,
              376.0
            ],
            [
              128.49609375,
              376.0
            ]
          ],
          "children": null,
          "section_hierarchy": {
            "1": "/page/22/SectionHeader/1",
            "3": "/page/24/SectionHeader/1"
          },
          "images": {}
        },
        {
          "id": "/page/24/Text/10",
          "block_type": "Text",
          "html": "<p>That may be a little vague, but we will come back to this topic when we talk about <b>algo</b><b>rithms</b>.</p>",
          "polygon": [
            [
              129.2431640625,
              385.55859375
            ],
            [
              527.73046875,
              385.55859375
            ],
            [
              527.73046875,
              408.76171875
            ],
            [
              129.2431640625,
              408.76171875
            ]
          ],
          "children": null,
          "section_hierarchy": {
            "1": "/page/22/SectionHeader/1",
            "3": "/page/24/SectionHeader/11"
          },
          "images": {}
        },
        {
          "id": "/page/24/SectionHeader/11",
          "block_type": "SectionHeader",
          "html": "<h3><b>1.3 What is debugging?</b></h3>",
          "polygon": [
            [
              128.72021484375,
              437.37890625
            ],
            [
              293.150390625,
              437.37890625
            ],
            [
              293.150390625,
              454.0
            ],
            [
              128.72021484375,
              454.0
            ]
          ],
          "children": null,
          "section_hierarchy": {
            "1": "/page/22/SectionHeader/1",
            "3": "/page/24/SectionHeader/11"
          },
          "images": {}
        },
        {
          "id": "/page/24/Text/12",
          "block_type": "Text",
          "html": "<p>Programming is error-prone. For whimsical reasons, programming errors are called <b>bugs</b> and the process of tracking them down is called <b>debugging</b>.</p>",
          "polygon": [
            [
              128.3466796875,
              465.22265625
            ],
            [
              527.73046875,
              465.22265625
            ],
            [
              527.73046875,
              489.0
            ],
            [
              128.3466796875,
              489.0
            ]
          ],
          "children": null,
          "section_hierarchy": {
            "1": "/page/22/SectionHeader/1",
            "3": "/page/24/SectionHeader/11"
          },
          "images": {}
        },
        {
          "id": "/page/24/Text/13",
          "block_type": "Text",
          "html": "<p>Three kinds of errors can occur in a program: syntax errors, runtime errors, and semantic errors. It is useful to distinguish between them in order to track them down more quickly.</p>",
          "polygon": [
            [
              128.197265625,
              497.70703125
            ],
            [
              527.431640625,
              497.70703125
            ],
            [
              527.431640625,
              522.0
            ],
            [
              128.197265625,
              522.0
            ]
          ],
          "children": null,
          "section_hierarchy": {
            "1": "/page/22/SectionHeader/1",
            "3": "/page/24/SectionHeader/11",
            "4": "/page/24/SectionHeader/14"
          },
          "images": {}
        },
        {
          "id": "/page/24/SectionHeader/14",
          "block_type": "SectionHeader",
          "html": "<h4><b>1.3.1 Syntax errors</b></h4>",
          "polygon": [
            [
              128.794921875,
              547.98046875
            ],
            [
              238.0,
              547.98046875
            ],
            [
              238.0,
              561.0
            ],
            [
              128.794921875,
              561.0
            ]
          ],
          "children": null,
          "section_hierarchy": {
            "1": "/page/22/SectionHeader/1",
            "3": "/page/24/SectionHeader/11",
            "4": "/page/24/SectionHeader/14"
          },
          "images": {}
        },
        {
          "id": "/page/24/Text/15",
          "block_type": "Text",
          "html": "<p>Python can only execute a program if the syntax is correct; otherwise, the interpreter displays an error message. <b>Syntax</b> refers to the structure of a program and the rules about that structure. For example, parentheses have to come in matching pairs, so (1 + 2) is legal, but 8) is a <b>syntax error</b>.</p>",
          "polygon": [
            [
              128.49609375,
              571.18359375
            ],
            [
              527.1328125,
              571.18359375
            ],
            [
              527.1328125,
              619.91015625
            ],
            [
              128.49609375,
              619.91015625
            ]
          ],
          "children": null,
          "section_hierarchy": {
            "1": "/page/22/SectionHeader/1",
            "3": "/page/24/SectionHeader/11",
            "4": "/page/24/SectionHeader/14"
          },
          "images": {}
        },
        {
          "id": "/page/24/Text/16",
          "block_type": "Text",
          "html": "<p>In English, readers can tolerate most syntax errors, which is why we can read the poetry of e. e. cummings without spewing error messages. Python is not so forgiving. If there is a single syntax error anywhere in your program, Python will display an error message and quit, and you will not be able to run your program. During the first few weeks of your programming career, you will probably spend a lot of time tracking down syntax errors. As you gain experience, you will make fewer errors and find them faster.</p>",
          "polygon": [
            [
              128.3466796875,
              629.19140625
            ],
            [
              526.53515625,
              629.19140625
            ],
            [
              526.53515625,
              701.12109375
            ],
            [
              128.3466796875,
              701.12109375
            ]
          ],
          "children": null,
          "section_hierarchy": {
