        },
        {
          "id": "/page/33/Text/5",
          "block_type": "Text",
          "html": "<p>Well, that's not what we expected at all! Python interprets 1,000,000 as a commaseparated sequence of integers. This is the first example we have seen of a semantic error: the code runs without producing an error message, but it doesn't do the \"right\" thing.</p>",
          "polygon": [
            [
              85.6142578125,
              208.44140625
            ],
            [
              482.90625,
              208.44140625
            ],
            [
              482.90625,
              244.40625
            ],
            [
              85.6142578125,
              244.40625
