          "children": null,
          "section_hierarchy": {
            "1": "/page/32/SectionHeader/1",
            "3": "/page/33/SectionHeader/14"
          },
          "images": {}
        },
        {
          "id": "/page/34/Text/2",
          "block_type": "Text",
          "html": "<p>If you give a variable an illegal name, you get a syntax error: ''</p>",
          "polygon": [
            [
              127.37548828125,
              120.849609375
            ],
            [
              396.24609375,
              120.849609375
            ],
            [
              396.24609375,
              133.0
            ],
            [
              127.37548828125,
              133.0
            ]
          ],
          "children": null,
          "section_hierarchy": {
            "1": "/page/32/SectionHeader/1",
            "3": "/page/33/SectionHeader/14"
          },
          "images": {}
        },
        {
          "id": "/page/34/Code/3",
          "block_type": "Code",
          "html": "<pre>&gt;&gt;&gt; 76trombones = big parade\n                               \nSyntaxError: invalid syntax\n&gt;&gt;&gt; more@ = 1000000\nSyntaxError: invalid syntax\n&gt;&gt;&gt; class = 'Advanced Theoretical Zymurgy'\n                                            \nSyntaxError: invalid syntax</pre>",
          "polygon": [
            [
              128.197265625,
              136.0
            ],
            [
              350.0,
              136.0
            ],
            [
              350.0,
              208.634765625
            ],
            [
              128.197265625,
              208.634765625
            ]
          ],
          "children": null,
          "section_hierarchy": {
            "1": "/page/32/SectionHeader/1",
            "3": "/page/33/SectionHeader/14"
          },
          "images": {}
        },
        {
          "id": "/page/34/Text/4",
          "block_type": "Text",
          "html": "<p>76trombones is illegal because it does not begin with a letter. more@ is illegal because it contains an illegal character, @. But what's wrong with class?</p>",
          "polygon": [
            [
              129.392578125,
              212.30859375
            ],
            [
              526.236328125,
              212.30859375
            ],
            [
              526.236328125,
              235.0
            ],
            [
              129.392578125,
              235.0
            ]
          ],
          "children": null,
          "section_hierarchy": {
            "1": "/page/32/SectionHeader/1",
            "3": "/page/33/SectionHeader/14"
          },
          "images": {}
        },
        {
          "id": "/page/34/Text/5",
          "block_type": "Text",
          "html": "<p>It turns out that class is one of Python's <b>keywords</b>. The interpreter uses keywords to recognize the structure of the program, and they cannot be used as variable names.</p>",
          "polygon": [
            [
              129.2431640625,
              244.212890625
            ],
            [
              526.53515625,
              244.212890625
            ],
            [
              526.53515625,
              267.0
            ],
            [
              129.2431640625,
              267.0
            ]
          ],
          "children": null,
          "section_hierarchy": {
            "1": "/page/32/SectionHeader/1",
            "3": "/page/33/SectionHeader/14"
          },
          "images": {}
        },
        {
          "id": "/page/34/Text/6",
          "block_type": "Text",
          "html": "<p>Python 2 has 31 keywords:</p>",
          "polygon": [
            [
              128.3466796875,
              275.537109375
            ],
            [
              248.0,
              275.537109375
            ],
            [
              248.0,
              287.0
            ],
            [
              128.3466796875,
              287.0
            ]
          ],
          "children": null,
          "section_hierarchy": {
            "1": "/page/32/SectionHeader/1",
            "3": "/page/33/SectionHeader/14"
          },
          "images": {}
        },
        {
          "id": "/page/34/Table/7",
          "block_type": "Table",
          "html": "<table>\n<thead>\n<tr><th>and     </th><th>del    </th><th>from  </th><th>not   </th><th>while  </th></tr>\n</thead>\n<tbody>\n<tr><td>as      </td><td>elif   </td><td>global</td><td>or    </td><td>with   </td></tr>\n<tr><td>assert  </td><td>else   </td><td>if    </td><td>pass  </td><td>yield  </td></tr>\n<tr><td>break   </td><td>except </td><td>import</td><td>print </td><td> </td></tr>\n<tr><td>class   </td><td>exec   </td><td>in    </td><td>raise </td><td> </td></tr>\n<tr><td>continue</td><td>finally</td><td>is    </td><td>return</td><td> </td></tr>\n<tr><td>def     </td><td>for    </td><td>lambda</td><td>try   </td><td> </td></tr>\n</tbody>\n</table>",
          "polygon": [
            [
              127.7490234375,
              291.19921875
            ],
            [
              367.55859375,
              289.65234375
            ],
            [
