        {
          "id": "/page/35/Text/9",
          "block_type": "Text",
          "html": "<p>A <b>statement</b> is a unit of code that the Python interpreter can execute. We have seen two kinds of statement: print and assignment.</p>",
          "polygon": [
            [
              85.46484375,
              305.701171875
            ],
            [
              483.50390625,
              305.701171875
            ],
            [
              483.50390625,
              328.904296875
            ],
            [
              85.46484375,
              328.904296875
            ]
          ],
          "children": null,
          "section_hierarchy": {
            "1": "/page/32/SectionHeader/1",
            "3": "/page/35/SectionHeader/4"
          },
          "images": {}
        },
        {
          "id": "/page/35/Text/10",
          "block_type": "Text",
          "html": "<p>Technically an expression is also a statement, but it is probably simpler to think of them as different things. The important difference is that an expression has a value; a statement does not.</p>",
          "polygon": [
            [
              85.46484375,
              337.21875
            ],
            [
              483.802734375,
              337.21875
            ],
            [
              483.802734375,
              372.0
            ],
            [
              85.46484375,
              372.0
            ]
          ],
          "children": null,
          "section_hierarchy": {
            "1": "/page/32/SectionHeader/1",
            "3": "/page/35/SectionHeader/11"
          },
          "images": {}
        },
        {
          "id": "/page/35/SectionHeader/11",
          "block_type": "SectionHeader",
          "html": "<h3><b>2.6 Interactive mode and script mode</b></h3>",
          "polygon": [
            [
              85.68896484375,
              399.8671875
            ],
            [
              339.46875,
              399.8671875
            ],
            [
              339.46875,
              415.0
            ],
            [
              85.68896484375,
              415.0
            ]
          ],
          "children": null,
          "section_hierarchy": {
            "1": "/page/32/SectionHeader/1",
            "3": "/page/35/SectionHeader/11"
          },
          "images": {}
        },
        {
          "id": "/page/35/Text/12",
          "block_type": "Text",
          "html": "<p>One of the benefits of working with an interpreted language is that you can test bits of code in interactive mode before you put them in a script. But there are differences between interactive mode and script mode that can be confusing.</p>",
          "polygon": [
            [
              85.46484375,
              426.55078125
            ],
            [
              483.802734375,
              426.55078125
            ],
            [
              483.802734375,
              462.12890625
            ],
            [
              85.46484375,
              462.12890625
            ]
          ],
          "children": null,
          "section_hierarchy": {
            "1": "/page/32/SectionHeader/1",
            "3": "/page/35/SectionHeader/11"
          },
          "images": {}
        },
        {
          "id": "/page/35/Text/13",
          "block_type": "Text",
          "html": "<p>For example, if you are using Python as a calculator, you might type</p>",
          "polygon": [
            [
              85.39013671875,
              471.0
            ],
            [
              387.87890625,
              471.0
            ],
            [
              387.87890625,
              481.8515625
            ],
            [
              85.39013671875,
              481.8515625
            ]
          ],
          "children": null,
          "section_hierarchy": {
            "1": "/page/32/SectionHeader/1",
            "3": "/page/35/SectionHeader/11"
          },
          "images": {}
        },
        {
          "id": "/page/35/Code/14",
          "block_type": "Code",
          "html": "<pre>&gt;&gt;&gt; miles = 26.2\n&gt;&gt;&gt; miles * 1.61\n42.182</pre>",
          "polygon": [
            [
              85.39013671875,
              486.4921875
            ],
            [
              170.33203125,
              486.4921875
            ],
            [
              170.33203125,
              521.296875
            ],
            [
              85.39013671875,
              521.296875
            ]
          ],
          "children": null,
          "section_hierarchy": {
            "1": "/page/32/SectionHeader/1",
            "3": "/page/35/SectionHeader/11"
          },
          "images": {}
        },
        {
          "id": "/page/35/Text/15",
          "block_type": "Text",
          "html": "<p>The first line assigns a value to miles, but it has no visible effect. The second line is an expression, so the interpreter evaluates it and displays the result. So we learn that a marathon is about 42 kilometers.</p>",
          "polygon": [
            [
              85.46484375,
              526.32421875
            ],
            [
              482.607421875,
              526.32421875
            ],
            [
              482.607421875,
              562.0
            ],
            [
              85.46484375,
              562.0
            ]
          ],
          "children": null,
          "section_hierarchy": {
            "1": "/page/32/SectionHeader/1",
            "3": "/page/35/SectionHeader/11"
          },
          "images": {}
        },
        {
          "id": "/page/35/Text/16",
          "block_type": "Text",
          "html": "<p>But if you type the same code into a script and run it, you get no output at all. In script mode an expression, all by itself, has no visible effect. Python actually evaluates the expression, but it doesn't display the value unless you tell it to:</p>",
          "polygon": [
            [
              85.46484375,
              570.0234375
            ],
            [
              483.205078125,
              570.0234375
            ],
            [
              483.205078125,
              606.0
            ],
            [
              85.46484375,
              606.0
            ]
          ],
          "children": null,
          "section_hierarchy": {
            "1": "/page/32/SectionHeader/1",
            "3": "/page/35/SectionHeader/11"
          },
          "images": {}
        },
        {
          "id": "/page/35/Code/17",
          "block_type": "Code",
          "html": "<pre>miles = 26.2\nprint miles * 1.61</pre>",
          "polygon": [
            [
              83.74658203125,
              611.0
            ],
            [
              255.796875,
              611.0
            ],
            [
              255.796875,
              640.01953125
