        },
        {
          "id": "/page/38/PageHeader/22",
          "block_type": "PageHeader",
          "html": "<p></p>",
          "polygon": [
            [
              515.478515625,
              61.9716796875
            ],
            [
              525.638671875,
              61.9716796875
            ],
            [
              525.638671875,
              70.4794921875
            ],
            [
              515.478515625,
              70.4794921875
            ]
          ],
          "children": null,
          "section_hierarchy": {
            "1": "/page/32/SectionHeader/1",
            "3": "/page/37/SectionHeader/19"
          },
          "images": {}
        },
        {
          "id": "/page/38/Text/1",
          "block_type": "Text",
          "html": "<p>If you put a space in a variable name, Python thinks it is two operands without an operator:</p>",
          "polygon": [
            [
              128.3466796875,
              89.0
            ],
            [
              526.0,
              89.0
            ],
            [
              526.0,
              99.0
            ],
            [
              128.3466796875,
              99.0
            ]
          ],
          "children": null,
          "section_hierarchy": {
            "1": "/page/32/SectionHeader/1",
            "3": "/page/37/SectionHeader/19"
          },
          "images": {}
        },
        {
          "id": "/page/38/Text/2",
          "block_type": "Text",
          "html": "<p>&gt;&gt;&gt; bad name = 5 SyntaxError: invalid syntax</p>",
          "polygon": [
            [
              129.09375,
              105.0
            ],
            [
              271.037109375,
              105.0
            ],
            [
              271.037109375,
              127.0
            ],
            [
              129.09375,
              127.0
            ]
          ],
          "children": null,
          "section_hierarchy": {
            "1": "/page/32/SectionHeader/1",
            "3": "/page/37/SectionHeader/19"
          },
          "images": {}
        },
        {
          "id": "/page/38/Text/3",
          "block_type": "Text",
          "html": "<p>For syntax errors, the error messages don't help much. The most common messages are SyntaxError: invalid syntax and SyntaxError: invalid token, neither of which is very informative.</p>",
          "polygon": [
            [
              128.794921875,
              133.611328125
            ],
            [
              526.0,
              133.611328125
            ],
            [
              526.0,
              168.0
            ],
            [
              128.794921875,
              168.0
            ]
          ],
          "children": null,
          "section_hierarchy": {
            "1": "/page/32/SectionHeader/1",
            "3": "/page/37/SectionHeader/19"
          },
          "images": {}
        },
        {
          "id": "/page/38/Text/4",
          "block_type": "Text",
          "html": "<p>The runtime error you are most likely to make is a \"use before def;\" that is, trying to use a variable before you have assigned a value. This can happen if you spell a variable name wrong:</p>",
          "polygon": [
            [
              128.794921875,
              178.0
            ],
            [
              526.0,
              178.0
            ],
            [
              526.0,
              213.0
            ],
            [
              128.794921875,
              213.0
            ]
          ],
          "children": null,
          "section_hierarchy": {
            "1": "/page/32/SectionHeader/1",
            "3": "/page/37/SectionHeader/19"
          },
          "images": {}
        },
        {
          "id": "/page/38/Code/5",
          "block_type": "Code",
          "html": "<pre>&gt;&gt;&gt; principal = 327.68\n&gt;&gt;&gt; interest = principle * rate\nNameError: name 'principle' is not defined</pre>",
          "polygon": [
            [
              128.9443359375,
              219.0
            ],
            [
              349.03125,
              219.0
            ],
            [
              349.03125,
              253.0
            ],
            [
              128.9443359375,
              253.0
            ]
          ],
          "children": null,
          "section_hierarchy": {
            "1": "/page/32/SectionHeader/1",
            "3": "/page/37/SectionHeader/19"
          },
          "images": {}
        },
        {
          "id": "/page/38/Text/6",
          "block_type": "Text",
          "html": "<p>Variables names are case sensitive, so LaTeX is not the same as latex.</p>",
          "polygon": [
            [
              129.31787109375,
              260.0
            ],
            [
              433.30078125,
              260.0
            ],
            [
              433.30078125,
              270.0
            ],
            [
              129.31787109375,
              270.0
            ]
          ],
          "children": null,
          "section_hierarchy": {
            "1": "/page/32/SectionHeader/1",
            "3": "/page/37/SectionHeader/19"
          },
          "images": {}
        },
        {
          "id": "/page/38/Text/7",
          "block_type": "Text",
          "html": "<p>At this point the most likely cause of a semantic error is the order of operations. For example, to evaluate 1 2π , you might be tempted to write</p>",
          "polygon": [
            [
              129.2431640625,
              279.59765625
            ],
            [
              526.53515625,
              279.59765625
            ],
            [
              526.53515625,
              306.0
            ],
            [
              129.2431640625,
              306.0
            ]
          ],
          "children": null,
          "section_hierarchy": {
            "1": "/page/32/SectionHeader/1",
            "3": "/page/37/SectionHeader/19"
          },
          "images": {}
        },
        {
          "id": "/page/38/TextInlineMath/8",
          "block_type": "TextInlineMath",
          "html": "<p>&gt;&gt;&gt; 1.0 / 2.0 * pi</p>",
          "polygon": [
            [
              129.09375,
              308.794921875
            ],
            [
              224.0,
              308.794921875
            ],
            [
              224.0,
              319.0
            ],
            [
              129.09375,
              319.0
            ]
          ],
          "children": null,
          "section_hierarchy": {
            "1": "/page/32/SectionHeader/1",
            "3": "/page/37/SectionHeader/19"
          },
          "images": {}
        },
        {
          "id": "/page/38/Text/9",
          "block_type": "Text",
          "html": "<p>But the division happens first, so you would get π/2, which is not the same thing! There is no way for Python to know what you meant to write, so in this case you don't get an error message; you just get the wrong answer.</p>",
          "polygon": [
            [
              128.3466796875,
              323.68359375
            ],
            [
              526.0,
              323.68359375
            ],
            [
              526.0,
              359.26171875
            ],
            [
              128.3466796875,
              359.26171875
            ]
          ],
          "children": null,
          "section_hierarchy": {
            "1": "/page/32/SectionHeader/1",
            "3": "/page/38/SectionHeader/10"
          },
          "images": {}
        },
