          "images": {}
        },
        {
          "id": "/page/41/Code/1",
          "block_type": "Code",
          "html": "<pre>&gt;&gt;&gt; float(32)\n32.0\n&gt;&gt;&gt; float('3.14159')\n3.14159\nFinally, str converts its argument to a string:\n&gt;&gt;&gt; str(32)\n'32'\n    \n&gt;&gt;&gt; str(3.14159)\n'3.14159'</pre>",
          "polygon": [
            [
              85.763671875,
              89.0
            ],
            [
              284.0,
              88.171875
            ],
            [
              284.0,
              203.0
            ],
            [
              85.763671875,
              203.607421875
            ]
          ],
          "children": null,
          "section_hierarchy": {
            "1": "/page/40/SectionHeader/1",
            "3": "/page/41/SectionHeader/2"
          },
          "images": {}
        },
        {
          "id": "/page/41/SectionHeader/2",
          "block_type": "SectionHeader",
          "html": "<h3><b>3.3 Math functions</b></h3>",
          "polygon": [
            [
              85.3154296875,
              231.2578125
            ],
            [
              219.9375,
              229.7109375
            ],
            [
              219.9375,
              247.0
            ],
            [
              85.3154296875,
              247.11328125
            ]
          ],
          "children": null,
          "section_hierarchy": {
            "1": "/page/40/SectionHeader/1",
            "3": "/page/41/SectionHeader/2"
          },
          "images": {}
        },
        {
          "id": "/page/41/Text/3",
          "block_type": "Text",
          "html": "<p>Python has a math module that provides most of the familiar mathematical functions. A <b>module</b> is a file that contains a collection of related functions.</p>",
          "polygon": [
            [
              86.0,
              258.0
            ],
            [
              482.30859375,
              256.587890625
            ],
            [
              482.30859375,
              281.0
            ],
            [
              86.0,
              281.0
            ]
          ],
          "children": null,
          "section_hierarchy": {
            "1": "/page/40/SectionHeader/1",
            "3": "/page/41/SectionHeader/2"
          },
          "images": {}
        },
        {
          "id": "/page/41/Text/4",
          "block_type": "Text",
          "html": "<p>Before we can use the module, we have to import it:</p>",
          "polygon": [
            [
              85.46484375,
              290.0
            ],
            [
              315.861328125,
              288.685546875
            ],
            [
              315.861328125,
              300.0
            ],
            [
              85.46484375,
              300.673828125
            ]
          ],
          "children": null,
          "section_hierarchy": {
            "1": "/page/40/SectionHeader/1",
            "3": "/page/41/SectionHeader/2"
          },
          "images": {}
        },
        {
          "id": "/page/41/Text/5",
          "block_type": "Text",
          "html": "<p>&gt;&gt;&gt; import math</p>",
          "polygon": [
            [
              85.46484375,
              305.5078125
            ],
            [
              165.55078125,
              305.5078125
            ],
            [
              165.55078125,
              316.0
            ],
            [
              85.46484375,
              316.0
            ]
          ],
          "children": null,
          "section_hierarchy": {
            "1": "/page/40/SectionHeader/1",
            "3": "/page/41/SectionHeader/2"
          },
          "images": {}
        },
        {
          "id": "/page/41/Text/6",
          "block_type": "Text",
          "html": "<p>This statement creates a <b>module object</b> named math. If you print the module object, you get some information about it:</p>",
          "polygon": [
            [
              85.6142578125,
              320.9765625
            ],
            [
              483.50390625,
              320.9765625
            ],
            [
              483.50390625,
              344.1796875
            ],
            [
              85.6142578125,
              344.1796875
            ]
          ],
          "children": null,
          "section_hierarchy": {
            "1": "/page/40/SectionHeader/1",
            "3": "/page/41/SectionHeader/2"
          },
          "images": {}
        },
        {
          "id": "/page/41/Text/7",
          "block_type": "Text",
          "html": "<p>&gt;&gt;&gt; print math &lt;module 'math'(built-in)&gt;</p>",
          "polygon": [
            [
              84.568359375,
              348.0
            ],
            [
              224.12109375,
              348.0
            ],
            [
              224.12109375,
              372.0
            ],
            [
              84.568359375,
              372.0
            ]
          ],
          "children": null,
          "section_hierarchy": {
            "1": "/page/40/SectionHeader/1",
            "3": "/page/41/SectionHeader/2"
          },
          "images": {}
        },
        {
          "id": "/page/41/Text/8",
          "block_type": "Text",
          "html": "<p>The module object contains the functions and variables defined in the module. To access one of the functions, you have to specify the name of the module and the name of the function, separated by a dot (also known as a period). This format is called <b>dot notation</b>.</p>",
          "polygon": [
            [
              85.46484375,
              375.50390625
            ],
            [
              484.1015625,
              375.50390625
            ],
            [
              484.1015625,
              412.0
            ],
            [
              85.46484375,
              412.0
            ]
          ],
          "children": null,
          "section_hierarchy": {
            "1": "/page/40/SectionHeader/1",
            "3": "/page/41/SectionHeader/2"
          },
          "images": {}
        },
        {
          "id": "/page/41/Code/9",
          "block_type": "Code",
          "html": "<pre>&gt;&gt;&gt; ratio = signal_power / noise_power\n&gt;&gt;&gt; decibels = 10 * math.log10(ratio)\n&gt;&gt;&gt; radians = 0.7\n&gt;&gt;&gt; height = math.sin(radians)</pre>",
          "polygon": [
            [
              85.6142578125,
              418.0
            ],
            [
              285.0,
              418.0
            ],
            [
              285.0,
              476.0
            ],
            [
              85.6142578125,
              476.0
            ]
          ],
          "children": null,
          "section_hierarchy": {
            "1": "/page/40/SectionHeader/1",
            "3": "/page/41/SectionHeader/2"
          },
          "images": {}
        },
        {
          "id": "/page/41/Text/10",
          "block_type": "Text",
          "html": "<p>The first example uses log10 to compute a signal-to-noise ratio in decibels (assuming that signal_power and noise_power are defined). The math module also provides log, which computes logarithms base e.</p>",
          "polygon": [
            [
              86.0,
              478.37109375
            ],
            [
              483.50390625,
              478.37109375
            ],
            [
              482.30859375,
              517.0
            ],
            [
              85.3154296875,
              517.0
            ]
          ],
          "children": null,
          "section_hierarchy": {
            "1": "/page/40/SectionHeader/1",
            "3": "/page/41/SectionHeader/2"
          },
          "images": {}
        },
        {
          "id": "/page/41/Text/11",
          "block_type": "Text",
          "html": "<p>The second example finds the sine of radians. The name of the variable is a hint that sin and the other trigonometric functions (cos, tan, etc.) take arguments in radians. To convert from degrees to radians, divide by 360 and multiply by 2π:</p>",
          "polygon": [
            [
              86.0,
              524.00390625
            ],
            [
              482.90625,
              524.00390625
            ],
            [
              482.90625,
              562.0
            ],
            [
              86.0,
              562.0
            ]
          ],
          "children": null,
          "section_hierarchy": {
            "1": "/page/40/SectionHeader/1",
            "3": "/page/41/SectionHeader/2"
          },
          "images": {}
        },
        {
          "id": "/page/41/Code/12",
          "block_type": "Code",
          "html": "<pre>&gt;&gt;&gt; degrees = 45\n&gt;&gt;&gt; radians = degrees / 360.0 * 2 * math.pi\n&gt;&gt;&gt; math.sin(radians)\n0.707106781187</pre>",
          "polygon": [
            [
              85.24072265625,
              564.99609375
            ],
            [
              312.275390625,
              564.99609375
            ],
            [
              311.080078125,
              613.0
            ],
            [
              84.04541015625,
              613.0
            ]
          ],
          "children": null,
          "section_hierarchy": {
            "1": "/page/40/SectionHeader/1",
            "3": "/page/41/SectionHeader/2"
          },
          "images": {}
        },
        {
          "id": "/page/41/Text/13",
          "block_type": "Text",
          "html": "<p>The expression math.pi gets the variable pi from the math module. The value of this variable is an approximation of π, accurate to about 15 digits.</p>",
          "polygon": [
            [
              85.763671875,
              617.58984375
            ],
            [
              482.607421875,
              617.58984375
            ],
            [
              482.607421875,
              642.0
            ],
            [
              85.763671875,
              642.0
            ]
          ],
          "children": null,
          "section_hierarchy": {
            "1": "/page/40/SectionHeader/1",
            "3": "/page/41/SectionHeader/2"
          },
          "images": {}
        },
        {
          "id": "/page/41/Text/14",
          "block_type": "Text",
          "html": "<p>If you know your trigonometry, you can check the previous result by comparing it to the square root of two divided by two:</p>",
          "polygon": [
            [
              85.6142578125,
              648.52734375
            ],
            [
              483.50390625,
              648.52734375
            ],
            [
              483.50390625,
              673.0
            ],
            [
              85.6142578125,
              673.0
            ]
          ],
          "children": null,
          "section_hierarchy": {
            "1": "/page/40/SectionHeader/1",
            "3": "/page/41/SectionHeader/2"
          },
          "images": {}
        },
        {
          "id": "/page/41/Code/15",
          "block_type": "Code",
          "html": "<pre>&gt;&gt;&gt; math.sqrt(2) / 2.0\n0.707106781187</pre>",
          "polygon": [
            [
              85.9130859375,
              673.6640625
            ],
            [
              205.7431640625,
              673.6640625
            ],
            [
              205.7431640625,
              701.0
            ],
            [
              85.9130859375,
              701.0
            ]
          ],
          "children": null,
          "section_hierarchy": {
            "1": "/page/40/SectionHeader/1",
            "3": "/page/41/SectionHeader/2"
          },
          "images": {}
        }
      ],
      "section_hierarchy": {
        "1": "/page/40/SectionHeader/1",
