        {
          "id": "/page/47/SectionHeader/17",
          "block_type": "SectionHeader",
          "html": "<h3><b>3.12 Why functions?</b></h3>",
          "polygon": [
            [
              85.9130859375,
              584.71875
            ],
            [
              229.0,
              584.71875
            ],
            [
              229.0,
              599.4140625
            ],
            [
              85.9130859375,
              599.4140625
            ]
          ],
          "children": null,
          "section_hierarchy": {
            "1": "/page/40/SectionHeader/1",
            "3": "/page/47/SectionHeader/17"
          },
          "images": {}
        },
        {
          "id": "/page/47/Text/18",
          "block_type": "Text",
          "html": "<p>It may not be clear why it is worth the trouble to divide a program into functions. There are several reasons:</p>",
          "polygon": [
            [
              85.46484375,
              611.0
            ],
            [
              482.009765625,
              611.0
            ],
            [
              482.009765625,
              634.0
            ],
            [
              85.46484375,
              634.0
            ]
          ],
          "children": null,
          "section_hierarchy": {
            "1": "/page/40/SectionHeader/1",
            "3": "/page/47/SectionHeader/17"
          },
          "images": {}
        },
        {
          "id": "/page/47/ListGroup/182",
          "block_type": "ListGroup",
          "html": "<p><ul><content-ref src='/page/47/ListItem/19'></content-ref><content-ref src='/page/47/ListItem/20'></content-ref></ul></p>",
          "polygon": [
            [
              99.80859375,
              645.8203125
            ],
            [
              482.90625,
              645.8203125
            ],
            [
              482.90625,
              701.0
            ],
            [
              99.80859375,
              701.0
            ]
          ],
          "children": [
            {
              "id": "/page/47/ListItem/19",
              "block_type": "ListItem",
              "html": "<li> Creating a new function gives you an opportunity to name a group of statements, which makes your program easier to read and debug.</li>",
              "polygon": [
                [
                  99.80859375,
                  645.8203125
                ],
                [
                  482.607421875,
                  645.8203125
                ],
                [
                  482.607421875,
                  669.0
                ],
                [
                  99.80859375,
                  669.0
                ]
              ],
              "children": null,
              "section_hierarchy": {
                "1": "/page/40/SectionHeader/1",
                "3": "/page/47/SectionHeader/17"
              },
              "images": {}
            },
            {
              "id": "/page/47/ListItem/20",
              "block_type": "ListItem",
              "html": "<li> Functions can make a program smaller by eliminating repetitive code. Later, if you make a change, you only have to make it in one place.</li>",
              "polygon": [
                [
                  100.0,
                  677.14453125
                ],
                [
                  482.90625,
                  677.14453125
                ],
                [
                  482.90625,
