          "images": {}
        },
        {
          "id": "/page/53/PageHeader/16",
          "block_type": "PageHeader",
          "html": "<p></p>",
          "polygon": [
            [
              85.68896484375,
              60.0380859375
            ],
            [
              96.59619140625,
              60.0380859375
            ],
            [
              96.59619140625,
              69.802734375
            ],
            [
              85.68896484375,
              69.802734375
            ]
          ],
          "children": null,
          "section_hierarchy": {
            "1": "/page/52/SectionHeader/1",
            "3": "/page/52/SectionHeader/3"
          },
          "images": {}
        },
        {
          "id": "/page/53/Text/1",
          "block_type": "Text",
          "html": "<p>The first line imports everything from the TurtleWorld module in the swampy package.</p>",
          "polygon": [
            [
              85.6142578125,
              88.02685546875
            ],
            [
              469.16015625,
              88.02685546875
            ],
            [
              469.16015625,
              99.4833984375
            ],
            [
              85.6142578125,
              99.4833984375
            ]
          ],
          "children": null,
          "section_hierarchy": {
            "1": "/page/52/SectionHeader/1",
            "3": "/page/52/SectionHeader/3"
          },
          "images": {}
        },
        {
          "id": "/page/53/Text/2",
          "block_type": "Text",
          "html": "<p>The next lines create a TurtleWorld assigned to world and a Turtle assigned to bob. Printing bob yields something like:</p>",
          "polygon": [
            [
              85.3154296875,
              107.7978515625
            ],
            [
              484.69921875,
              107.7978515625
            ],
            [
              484.69921875,
              131.0
            ],
            [
              85.3154296875,
              131.0
            ]
          ],
          "children": null,
          "section_hierarchy": {
            "1": "/page/52/SectionHeader/1",
            "3": "/page/52/SectionHeader/3"
          },
          "images": {}
        },
        {
          "id": "/page/53/Text/3",
          "block_type": "Text",
          "html": "<p>&lt;TurtleWorld.Turtle instance at 0xb7bfbf4c&gt;</p>",
          "polygon": [
            [
              86.0,
              136.6083984375
            ],
            [
              311.0,
              136.6083984375
            ],
            [
              311.0,
              148.0
            ],
            [
              86.0,
              148.0
            ]
          ],
          "children": null,
          "section_hierarchy": {
            "1": "/page/52/SectionHeader/1",
            "3": "/page/52/SectionHeader/3"
          },
          "images": {}
        },
        {
          "id": "/page/53/Text/4",
          "block_type": "Text",
          "html": "<p>This means that bob refers to an <b>instance</b> of a Turtle as defined in module TurtleWorld. In this context, \"instance\" means a member of a set; this Turtle is one of the set of possible Turtles.</p>",
          "polygon": [
            [
              85.763671875,
              153.52734375
            ],
            [
              484.1015625,
              153.52734375
            ],
            [
              484.1015625,
              189.0
            ],
            [
              85.763671875,
              189.0
            ]
          ],
          "children": null,
          "section_hierarchy": {
            "1": "/page/52/SectionHeader/1",
            "3": "/page/52/SectionHeader/3"
          },
          "images": {}
        },
        {
          "id": "/page/53/Text/5",
          "block_type": "Text",
          "html": "<p>wait_for_user tells TurtleWorld to wait for the user to do something, although in this case there's not much for the user to do except close the window.</p>",
          "polygon": [
            [
              85.166015625,
              197.61328125
            ],
            [
              483.50390625,
              197.61328125
            ],
            [
              483.50390625,
              221.0
            ],
            [
              85.166015625,
              221.0
            ]
          ],
          "children": null,
          "section_hierarchy": {
            "1": "/page/52/SectionHeader/1",
            "3": "/page/52/SectionHeader/3"
          },
          "images": {}
        },
        {
          "id": "/page/53/Text/6",
          "block_type": "Text",
          "html": "<p>TurtleWorld provides several turtle-steering functions: fd and bk for forward and backward, and lt and rt for left and right turns. Also, each Turtle is holding a pen, which is either down or up; if the pen is down, the Turtle leaves a trail when it moves. The functions pu and pd stand for \"pen up\" and \"pen down.\"</p>",
          "polygon": [
            [
              85.3154296875,
              230.484375
            ],
            [
              483.50390625,
              230.484375
            ],
            [
              483.50390625,
              278.05078125
            ],
            [
              85.3154296875,
              278.05078125
            ]
          ],
          "children": null,
          "section_hierarchy": {
            "1": "/page/52/SectionHeader/1",
            "3": "/page/52/SectionHeader/3"
          },
          "images": {}
        },
        {
          "id": "/page/53/Text/7",
          "block_type": "Text",
          "html": "<p>To draw a right angle, add these lines to the program (after creating bob and before calling wait_for_user):</p>",
          "polygon": [
            [
              85.0166015625,
              289.0
            ],
            [
              484.1015625,
              289.0
            ],
            [
              484.1015625,
              311.0
            ],
            [
              85.0166015625,
              311.0
            ]
          ],
          "children": null,
          "section_hierarchy": {
            "1": "/page/52/SectionHeader/1",
            "3": "/page/52/SectionHeader/3"
          },
          "images": {}
        },
        {
          "id": "/page/53/TextInlineMath/8",
          "block_type": "TextInlineMath",
          "html": "<p>fd(bob, 100) lt(bob) fd(bob, 100)</p>",
          "polygon": [
            [
              85.68896484375,
              315.755859375
            ],
            [
              150.98291015625,
              315.755859375
            ],
            [
              150.98291015625,
              354.427734375
            ],
            [
              85.68896484375,
              354.427734375
            ]
          ],
          "children": null,
          "section_hierarchy": {
            "1": "/page/52/SectionHeader/1",
            "3": "/page/52/SectionHeader/3"
          },
          "images": {}
        },
        {
          "id": "/page/53/Text/9",
          "block_type": "Text",
          "html": "<p>The first line tells bob to take 100 steps forward. The second line tells him to turn left.</p>",
          "polygon": [
            [
              84.568359375,
              356.748046875
            ],
            [
              460.79296875,
              356.748046875
            ],
            [
              460.79296875,
              368.0
            ],
            [
              84.568359375,
              368.0
            ]
          ],
          "children": null,
          "section_hierarchy": {
            "1": "/page/52/SectionHeader/1",
            "3": "/page/52/SectionHeader/3"
          },
          "images": {}
        },
        {
          "id": "/page/53/Text/10",
          "block_type": "Text",
          "html": "<p>When you run this program, you should see bob move east and then north, leaving two line segments behind.</p>",
          "polygon": [
            [
              85.166015625,
              377.82421875
            ],
            [
              484.1015625,
              377.82421875
            ],
            [
              484.1015625,
              401.0
            ],
            [
              85.166015625,
              401.0
            ]
