        },
        {
          "id": "/page/55/Text/5",
          "block_type": "Text",
          "html": "<p>The first exercise asks you to put your square-drawing code into a function definition and then call the function, passing the turtle as a parameter. Here is a solution:</p>",
          "polygon": [
            [
              85.9130859375,
              251.560546875
            ],
            [
              482.30859375,
              251.560546875
            ],
            [
              482.30859375,
              274.0
            ],
            [
              85.9130859375,
              274.0
            ]
          ],
          "children": null,
          "section_hierarchy": {
            "1": "/page/52/SectionHeader/1",
            "3": "/page/55/SectionHeader/4"
          },
          "images": {}
        },
        {
          "id": "/page/55/Code/6",
          "block_type": "Code",
          "html": "<pre>def square(t):\n    for i in range(4):\n        fd(t, 100)\n        lt(t)</pre>",
          "polygon": [
            [
              85.98779296875,
              278.630859375
            ],
            [
              201.0,
              278.630859375
            ],
            [
              201.0,
              329.291015625
            ],
            [
              85.98779296875,
              329.291015625
            ]
          ],
          "children": null,
          "section_hierarchy": {
            "1": "/page/52/SectionHeader/1",
            "3": "/page/55/SectionHeader/4"
          },
          "images": {}
        },
        {
          "id": "/page/55/Text/7",
          "block_type": "Text",
          "html": "<p>square(bob)</p>",
          "polygon": [
            [
              85.39013671875,
              340.3125
