          "children": null,
          "section_hierarchy": {
            "1": "/page/52/SectionHeader/1",
            "3": "/page/55/SectionHeader/12"
          },
          "images": {}
        },
        {
          "id": "/page/56/Text/1",
          "block_type": "Text",
          "html": "<p>The next step is also a generalization. Instead of drawing squares, polygon draws regular polygons with any number of sides. Here is a solution :rule</p>",
          "polygon": [
            [
              128.6455078125,
              88.55859375
            ],
            [
              526.0,
              88.55859375
            ],
            [
              526.0,
              111.0
            ],
            [
              128.6455078125,
              111.0
            ]
          ],
          "children": null,
          "section_hierarchy": {
            "1": "/page/52/SectionHeader/1",
            "3": "/page/55/SectionHeader/12"
          },
          "images": {}
        },
        {
          "id": "/page/56/Code/2",
          "block_type": "Code",
          "html": "<pre>def polygon(t, n, length):\n    angle = 360.0 / n\n    for i in range(n):\n        fd(t, length)\n        lt(t, angle)</pre>",
          "polygon": [
            [
              128.6455078125,
              118.8193359375
            ],
            [
              266.1064453125,
              118.8193359375
            ],
            [
              266.1064453125,
              183.2080078125
            ],
            [
              128.6455078125,
              183.2080078125
            ]
          ],
          "children": null,
          "section_hierarchy": {
            "1": "/page/52/SectionHeader/1",
            "3": "/page/55/SectionHeader/12"
          },
          "images": {}
        },
        {
          "id": "/page/56/Text/3",
          "block_type": "Text",
          "html": "<p>polygon(bob, 7, 70)</p>",
          "polygon": [
            [
              126.62841796875,
              193.0
            ],
            [
              229.0,
              193.0
            ],
            [
              229.0,
              203.220703125
            ],
            [
              126.62841796875,
              203.220703125
            ]
          ],
          "children": null,
          "section_hierarchy": {
            "1": "/page/52/SectionHeader/1",
            "3": "/page/55/SectionHeader/12"
          },
          "images": {}
        },
        {
          "id": "/page/56/Text/4",
          "block_type": "Text",
          "html": "<p>This draws a 7-sided polygon with side length 70. If you have more than a few numeric arguments, it is easy to forget what they are, or what order they should be in. It is legal, and sometimes helpful, to include the names of the parameters in the argument list:</p>",
          "polygon": [
            [
              129.09375,
              212.501953125
            ],
            [
              526.0,
              212.501953125
            ],
            [
              526.0,
              247.306640625
            ],
            [
              129.09375,
              247.306640625
            ]
          ],
          "children": null,
          "section_hierarchy": {
            "1": "/page/52/SectionHeader/1",
            "3": "/page/55/SectionHeader/12"
          },
          "images": {}
        },
        {
          "id": "/page/56/TextInlineMath/5",
          "block_type": "TextInlineMath",
          "html": "<p>polygon(bob, n=7, length=70)</p>",
          "polygon": [
            [
              130.0,
              251.947265625
            ],
            [
              276.0,
              251.947265625
            ],
            [
              276.0,
              262.0
            ],
            [
              129.01904296875,
              262.0
            ]
          ],
          "children": null,
          "section_hierarchy": {
            "1": "/page/52/SectionHeader/1",
            "3": "/page/55/SectionHeader/12"
          },
          "images": {}
        },
        {
          "id": "/page/56/Text/6",
          "block_type": "Text",
          "html": "<p>These are called <b>keyword arguments</b> because they include the parameter names as \"keywords\" (not to be confused with Python keywords like while and def).</p>",
          "polygon": [
            [
              128.0478515625,
              267.609375
            ],
            [
              526.0,
              267.609375
            ],
            [
              526.0,
              290.0
            ],
            [
              128.0478515625,
              290.0
            ]
          ],
          "children": null,
          "section_hierarchy": {
            "1": "/page/52/SectionHeader/1",
            "3": "/page/55/SectionHeader/12"
          },
          "images": {}
        },
        {
          "id": "/page/56/Text/7",
          "block_type": "Text",
          "html": "<p>This syntax makes the program more readable. It is also a reminder about how arguments and parameters work: when you call a function, the arguments are assigned to the parameters.</p>",
          "polygon": [
            [
              128.6455078125,
              299.0
            ],
            [
              526.0,
              299.0
            ],
            [
              526.0,
              334.0
            ],
            [
              128.6455078125,
              334.0
            ]
          ],
          "children": null,
          "section_hierarchy": {
            "1": "/page/52/SectionHeader/1",
            "3": "/page/56/SectionHeader/8"
          },
          "images": {}
        },
        {
          "id": "/page/56/SectionHeader/8",
          "block_type": "SectionHeader",
          "html": "<h3><b>4.6 Interface design</b></h3>",
          "polygon": [
            [
              127.52490234375,
              362.0
            ],
            [
              267.0,
              362.0
            ],
            [
              267.0,
              376.857421875
            ],
            [
              127.52490234375,
              376.857421875
            ]
          ],
          "children": null,
          "section_hierarchy": {
            "1": "/page/52/SectionHeader/1",
            "3": "/page/56/SectionHeader/8"
          },
          "images": {}
        },
        {
          "id": "/page/56/Text/9",
          "block_type": "Text",
          "html": "<p>The next step is to write circle, which takes a radius, r, as a parameter. Here is a simple solution that uses polygon to draw a 50-sided polygon:</p>",
          "polygon": [
            [
              129.5419921875,
              388.0
            ],
            [
              526.0,
              388.0
            ],
            [
              526.0,
              410.0
            ],
            [
              129.5419921875,
              410.0
            ]
          ],
          "children": null,
          "section_hierarchy": {
            "1": "/page/52/SectionHeader/1",
            "3": "/page/56/SectionHeader/8"
          },
          "images": {}
        },
        {
          "id": "/page/56/Code/10",
          "block_type": "Code",
          "html": "<pre>def circle(t, r):\n    circumference = 2 * math.pi * r\n    n = 50\n    length = circumference / n\n    polygon(t, n, length)</pre>",
          "polygon": [
            [
              130.0,
              414.17578125
            ],
            [
              313.0,
              414.17578125
            ],
            [
              313.0,
              474.50390625
            ],
            [
              130.0,
              474.50390625
            ]
          ],
          "children": null,
          "section_hierarchy": {
            "1": "/page/52/SectionHeader/1",
            "3": "/page/56/SectionHeader/8"
          },
          "images": {}
        },
        {
          "id": "/page/56/Text/11",
          "block_type": "Text",
          "html": "<p>The first line computes the circumference of a circle with radius r using the formula 2πr. Since we use math.pi, we have to import math. By convention, import statements are usually at the beginning of the script.</p>",
          "polygon": [
            [
              129.09375,
              478.7578125
            ],
            [
              526.53515625,
              478.7578125
            ],
            [
              526.53515625,
              514.0
            ],
            [
              129.09375,
              514.0
            ]
          ],
          "children": null,
          "section_hierarchy": {
            "1": "/page/52/SectionHeader/1",
            "3": "/page/56/SectionHeader/8"
          },
          "images": {}
        },
        {
          "id": "/page/56/Text/12",
          "block_type": "Text",
          "html": "<p>n is the number of line segments in our approximation of a circle, so length is the length of each segment. Thus, polygon draws a 50-sides polygon that approximates a circle with radius r.</p>",
          "polygon": [
            [
              128.6455078125,
              522.45703125
            ],
            [
              527.1328125,
              522.45703125
            ],
            [
              527.1328125,
              558.0
            ],
            [
              128.6455078125,
              558.0
            ]
          ],
          "children": null,
          "section_hierarchy": {
            "1": "/page/52/SectionHeader/1",
            "3": "/page/56/SectionHeader/8"
          },
          "images": {}
        },
        {
          "id": "/page/56/Text/13",
          "block_type": "Text",
          "html": "<p>One limitation of this solution is that n is a constant, which means that for very big circles, the line segments are too long, and for small circles, we waste time drawing very small segments. One solution would be to generalize the function by taking n as a parameter. This would give the user (whoever calls circle) more control, but the interface would be less clean.</p>",
          "polygon": [
            [
              128.0478515625,
              566.54296875
            ],
            [
              526.0,
              566.54296875
            ],
            [
              526.0,
              626.0
            ],
            [
              128.0478515625,
              626.0
            ]
          ],
          "children": null,
          "section_hierarchy": {
            "1": "/page/52/SectionHeader/1",
            "3": "/page/56/SectionHeader/8"
          },
          "images": {}
        },
        {
          "id": "/page/56/Text/14",
          "block_type": "Text",
          "html": "<p>The <b>interface</b> of a function is a summary of how it is used: what are the parameters? What does the function do? And what is the return value? An interface is \"clean\" if it is \"as simple as possible, but not simpler. (Einstein)\"</p>",
          "polygon": [
            [
              128.49609375,
              634.60546875
            ],
            [
              527.1328125,
              634.60546875
            ],
            [
              527.1328125,
              669.0
            ],
            [
              128.49609375,
              669.0
            ]
          ],
          "children": null,
          "section_hierarchy": {
            "1": "/page/52/SectionHeader/1",
            "3": "/page/56/SectionHeader/8"
          },
          "images": {}
        },
        {
          "id": "/page/56/Text/15",
          "block_type": "Text",
          "html": "<p>In this example, r belongs in the interface because it specifies the circle to be drawn. n is less appropriate because it pertains to the details of how the circle should be rendered.</p>",
          "polygon": [
            [
              128.197265625,
              678.3046875
            ],
            [
              526.0,
              678.3046875
            ],
            [
              526.0,
              701.0
            ],
            [
              128.197265625,
              701.0
            ]
          ],
          "children": null,
          "section_hierarchy": {
            "1": "/page/52/SectionHeader/1",
            "3": "/page/56/SectionHeader/8"
          },
          "images": {}
        }
      ],
      "section_hierarchy": {
        "1": "/page/52/SectionHeader/1",
        "3": "/page/56/SectionHeader/8"
      },
      "images": null
    },
    {
      "id": "/page/57/Page/202",
      "block_type": "Page",
      "html": "<content-ref src='/page/57/PageHeader/0'></content-ref><content-ref src='/page/57/PageHeader/10'></content-ref><content-ref src='/page/57/Text/1'></content-ref><content-ref src='/page/57/Code/2'></content-ref><content-ref src='/page/57/Text/3'></content-ref><content-ref src='/page/57/SectionHeader/4'></content-ref><content-ref src='/page/57/Text/5'></content-ref><content-ref src='/page/57/Text/6'></content-ref><content-ref src='/page/57/Code/7'></content-ref><content-ref src='/page/57/Text/8'></content-ref><content-ref src='/page/57/Code/9'></content-ref>",
      "polygon": [
        [
          0.0,
          0.0
        ],
        [
          612.0,
          0.0
        ],
        [
          612.0,
          792.0
        ],
        [
          0.0,
          792.0
        ]
      ],
      "children": [
        {
          "id": "/page/57/PageHeader/0",
          "block_type": "PageHeader",
          "html": "<p><b>36 Chapter 4. Case study: interface design</b></p>",
          "polygon": [
            [
              86.0,
              60.95654296875
            ],
            [
              482.90625,
              60.95654296875
            ],
            [
              482.90625,
              71.0
            ],
            [
              86.0,
              71.0
            ]
          ],
          "children": null,
          "section_hierarchy": {
            "1": "/page/52/SectionHeader/1",
            "3": "/page/56/SectionHeader/8"
          },
          "images": {}
        },
        {
          "id": "/page/57/PageHeader/10",
          "block_type": "PageHeader",
          "html": "<p></p>",
          "polygon": [
            [
              85.6142578125,
              60.8115234375
            ],
            [
              97.119140625,
              60.8115234375
            ],
            [
              97.119140625,
              70.3828125
            ],
            [
              85.6142578125,
              70.3828125
            ]
          ],
          "children": null,
          "section_hierarchy": {
            "1": "/page/52/SectionHeader/1",
            "3": "/page/56/SectionHeader/8"
          },
          "images": {}
        },
        {
          "id": "/page/57/Text/1",
          "block_type": "Text",
          "html": "<p>Rather than clutter up the interface, it is better to choose an appropriate value of n depending on circumference:</p>",
          "polygon": [
            [
              84.7177734375,
              88.41357421875
            ],
            [
              482.30859375,
              88.41357421875
            ],
            [
              482.30859375,
              111.0
            ],
            [
              84.7177734375,
              111.0
            ]
          ],
          "children": null,
          "section_hierarchy": {
            "1": "/page/52/SectionHeader/1",
            "3": "/page/56/SectionHeader/8"
          },
          "images": {}
        },
        {
          "id": "/page/57/Code/2",
          "block_type": "Code",
          "html": "<pre>def circle(t, r):\n    circumference = 2 * math.pi * r\n    n = int(circumference / 3) + 1\n    length = circumference / n\n    polygon(t, n, length)</pre>",
          "polygon": [
            [
              86.0,
              115.62890625
            ],
            [
              271.93359375,
              115.62890625
            ],
            [
              271.93359375,
              177.310546875
            ],
            [
              86.0,
              177.310546875
            ]
          ],
          "children": null,
          "section_hierarchy": {
            "1": "/page/52/SectionHeader/1",
            "3": "/page/56/SectionHeader/8"
          },
          "images": {}
        },
        {
          "id": "/page/57/Text/3",
          "block_type": "Text",
          "html": "<p>Now the number of segments is (approximately) circumference/3, so the length of each segment is (approximately) 3, which is small enough that the circles look good, but big enough to be efficient, and appropriate for any size circle.</p>",
          "polygon": [
            [
              85.763671875,
              179.9208984375
            ],
            [
              482.30859375,
              179.9208984375
            ],
            [
              482.30859375,
              217.0
            ],
            [
              85.763671875,
              217.0
            ]
          ],
          "children": null,
          "section_hierarchy": {
            "1": "/page/52/SectionHeader/1",
            "3": "/page/57/SectionHeader/4"
          },
          "images": {}
        },
        {
          "id": "/page/57/SectionHeader/4",
          "block_type": "SectionHeader",
          "html": "<h3><b>4.7 Refactoring</b></h3>",
          "polygon": [
            [
              85.6142578125,
              244.599609375
            ],
            [
              195.2841796875,
              244.599609375
            ],
            [
              195.2841796875,
              260.068359375
            ],
            [
              85.6142578125,
              260.068359375
            ]
          ],
          "children": null,
          "section_hierarchy": {
            "1": "/page/52/SectionHeader/1",
            "3": "/page/57/SectionHeader/4"
          },
          "images": {}
        },
        {
          "id": "/page/57/Text/5",
          "block_type": "Text",
          "html": "<p>When I wrote circle, I was able to re-use polygon because a many-sided polygon is a good approximation of a circle. But arc is not as cooperative; we can't use polygon or circle to draw an arc.</p>",
          "polygon": [
            [
              85.6142578125,
              271.4765625
            ],
            [
              482.30859375,
              271.4765625
            ],
            [
              482.30859375,
              307.0546875
            ],
            [
              85.6142578125,
              307.0546875
            ]
          ],
          "children": null,
          "section_hierarchy": {
            "1": "/page/52/SectionHeader/1",
            "3": "/page/57/SectionHeader/4"
          },
          "images": {}
        },
        {
          "id": "/page/57/Text/6",
          "block_type": "Text",
          "html": "<p>One alternative is to start with a copy of polygon and transform it into arc. The result might look like this:</p>",
          "polygon": [
            [
              85.46484375,
              315.755859375
            ],
            [
              482.30859375,
              315.755859375
            ],
            [
              482.30859375,
              339.0
            ],
            [
              85.46484375,
              339.0
            ]
          ],
          "children": null,
          "section_hierarchy": {
            "1": "/page/52/SectionHeader/1",
            "3": "/page/57/SectionHeader/4"
          },
          "images": {}
        },
        {
          "id": "/page/57/Code/7",
          "block_type": "Code",
          "html": "<pre>def arc(t, r, angle):\n    arc_length = 2 * math.pi * r * angle / 360\n    n = int(arc_length / 3) + 1\n    step_length = arc_length / n\n    step_angle = float(angle) / n\n    for i in range(n):\n        fd(t, step_length)\n        lt(t, step_angle)</pre>",
          "polygon": [
            [
              86.0,
              343.40625
            ],
            [
              327.0,
              343.40625
            ],
            [
              327.0,
              453.0
            ],
            [
              86.0,
              453.0
            ]
          ],
          "children": null,
          "section_hierarchy": {
            "1": "/page/52/SectionHeader/1",
            "3": "/page/57/SectionHeader/4"
          },
          "images": {}
        },
        {
          "id": "/page/57/Text/8",
          "block_type": "Text",
          "html": "<p>The second half of this function looks like polygon, but we can't re-use polygon without changing the interface. We could generalize polygon to take an angle as a third argument, but then polygon would no longer be an appropriate name! Instead, let's call the more general function polyline:</p>",
          "polygon": [
            [
              85.9130859375,
              457.875
            ],
            [
              482.30859375,
              457.875
            ],
            [
              482.30859375,
              506.6015625
            ],
            [
              85.9130859375,
              506.6015625
            ]
          ],
          "children": null,
          "section_hierarchy": {
            "1": "/page/52/SectionHeader/1",
            "3": "/page/57/SectionHeader/4"
          },
          "images": {}
        },
        {
          "id": "/page/57/Code/9",
          "block_type": "Code",
          "html": "<pre>def polyline(t, n, length, angle):\n    for i in range(n):\n        fd(t, length)\n        lt(t, angle)\nNow we can rewrite polygon and arc to use polyline:\ndef polygon(t, n, length):\n    angle = 360.0 / n\n    polyline(t, n, length, angle)\ndef arc(t, r, angle):\n    arc_length = 2 * math.pi * r * angle / 360\n    n = int(arc_length / 3) + 1\n    step_length = arc_length / n\n    step_angle = float(angle) / n\n    polyline(t, n, step_length, step_angle)</pre>",
          "polygon": [
            [
              85.166015625,
              512.0
            ],
            [
              333.193359375,
              512.0
            ],
            [
              333.193359375,
              701.0
            ],
            [
              85.166015625,
              701.0
            ]
          ],
          "children": null,
          "section_hierarchy": {
            "1": "/page/52/SectionHeader/1",
            "3": "/page/57/SectionHeader/4"
          },
          "images": {}
        }
      ],
      "section_hierarchy": {
        "1": "/page/52/SectionHeader/1",
        "3": "/page/57/SectionHeader/4"
      },
      "images": null
    },
    {
      "id": "/page/58/Page/150",
      "block_type": "Page",
      "html": "<content-ref src='/page/58/PageHeader/0'></content-ref><content-ref src='/page/58/PageHeader/16'></content-ref><content-ref src='/page/58/Text/1'></content-ref><content-ref src='/page/58/TextInlineMath/2'></content-ref><content-ref src='/page/58/Text/3'></content-ref><content-ref src='/page/58/Text/4'></content-ref><content-ref src='/page/58/SectionHeader/5'></content-ref><content-ref src='/page/58/Text/6'></content-ref><content-ref src='/page/58/ListGroup/150'></content-ref><content-ref src='/page/58/Text/12'></content-ref><content-ref src='/page/58/SectionHeader/13'></content-ref><content-ref src='/page/58/Text/14'></content-ref><content-ref src='/page/58/Code/15'></content-ref>",
      "polygon": [
        [
          0.0,
          0.0
        ],
        [
          612.0,
          0.0
        ],
        [
          612.0,
          792.0
        ],
        [
          0.0,
          792.0
        ]
      ],
      "children": [
        {
          "id": "/page/58/PageHeader/0",
          "block_type": "PageHeader",
          "html": "<p><b>4.8. A development plan 37</b></p>",
          "polygon": [
            [
              127.52490234375,
              61.0
            ],
            [
              526.0,
              61.0
            ],
            [
              526.0,
              71.0
            ],
            [
              127.52490234375,
              71.0
            ]
          ],
          "children": null,
          "section_hierarchy": {
            "1": "/page/52/SectionHeader/1",
            "3": "/page/57/SectionHeader/4"
          },
          "images": {}
        },
        {
          "id": "/page/58/PageHeader/16",
          "block_type": "PageHeader",
          "html": "<p></p>",
          "polygon": [
            [
              515.478515625,
              60.6181640625
            ],
            [
              526.236328125,
              60.6181640625
            ],
            [
              526.236328125,
              70.0927734375
            ],
            [
              515.478515625,
              70.0927734375
            ]
          ],
          "children": null,
          "section_hierarchy": {
            "1": "/page/52/SectionHeader/1",
            "3": "/page/57/SectionHeader/4"
          },
          "images": {}
        },
        {
          "id": "/page/58/Text/1",
          "block_type": "Text",
          "html": "<p>Finally, we can rewrite circle to use arc:</p>",
          "polygon": [
            [
              127.599609375,
              88.55859375
            ],
            [
              313.171875,
              88.55859375
            ],
            [
              313.171875,
              99.0
            ],
            [
              127.599609375,
              99.0
            ]
          ],
          "children": null,
          "section_hierarchy": {
            "1": "/page/52/SectionHeader/1",
            "3": "/page/57/SectionHeader/4"
          },
          "images": {}
        },
        {
          "id": "/page/58/TextInlineMath/2",
          "block_type": "TextInlineMath",
          "html": "<p>def circle(t, r): arc(t, r, 360)</p>",
          "polygon": [
            [
              128.794921875,
              106.34765625
            ],
            [
              224.0,
              106.34765625
            ],
            [
              224.0,
              129.0
            ],
            [
              128.794921875,
              129.0
            ]
          ],
          "children": null,
          "section_hierarchy": {
            "1": "/page/52/SectionHeader/1",
            "3": "/page/57/SectionHeader/4"
          },
          "images": {}
        },
        {
          "id": "/page/58/Text/3",
          "block_type": "Text",
          "html": "<p>This process—rearranging a program to improve function interfaces and facilitate code reuse—is called <b>refactoring</b>. In this case, we noticed that there was similar code in arc and polygon, so we \"factored it out\" into polyline.</p>",
          "polygon": [
            [
              129.392578125,
              136.0283203125
            ],
            [
              526.0,
              136.0283203125
            ],
            [
              526.0,
              171.2197265625
            ],
            [
              129.392578125,
              171.2197265625
            ]
          ],
          "children": null,
          "section_hierarchy": {
            "1": "/page/52/SectionHeader/1",
            "3": "/page/57/SectionHeader/4"
          },
          "images": {}
        },
        {
          "id": "/page/58/Text/4",
          "block_type": "Text",
          "html": "<p>If we had planned ahead, we might have written polyline first and avoided refactoring, but often you don't know enough at the beginning of a project to design all the interfaces. Once you start coding, you understand the problem better. Sometimes refactoring is a sign that you have learned something.</p>",
          "polygon": [
            [
              128.3466796875,
              183.0
            ],
            [
              526.0,
              183.0
            ],
            [
              526.0,
              230.0
            ],
            [
              128.3466796875,
              230.0
            ]
          ],
          "children": null,
          "section_hierarchy": {
            "1": "/page/52/SectionHeader/1",
            "3": "/page/58/SectionHeader/5"
          },
          "images": {}
        },
        {
          "id": "/page/58/SectionHeader/5",
          "block_type": "SectionHeader",
          "html": "<h3><b>4.8 A development plan</b></h3>",
          "polygon": [
            [
              128.72021484375,
              264.0
            ],
            [
              296.0,
              264.0
            ],
            [
              296.0,
              279.0
            ],
            [
              128.72021484375,
              279.0
            ]
          ],
          "children": null,
          "section_hierarchy": {
            "1": "/page/52/SectionHeader/1",
            "3": "/page/58/SectionHeader/5"
          },
          "images": {}
        },
        {
          "id": "/page/58/Text/6",
          "block_type": "Text",
          "html": "<p>A <b>development plan</b> is a process for writing programs. The process we used in this case study is \"encapsulation and generalization.\" The steps of this process are:</p>",
          "polygon": [
            [
              128.794921875,
              292.939453125
            ],
            [
              526.236328125,
              292.939453125
            ],
            [
              526.236328125,
              316.0
            ],
            [
              128.794921875,
              316.0
            ]
          ],
          "children": null,
          "section_hierarchy": {
            "1": "/page/52/SectionHeader/1",
            "3": "/page/58/SectionHeader/5"
          },
          "images": {}
        },
        {
          "id": "/page/58/ListGroup/150",
          "block_type": "ListGroup",
          "html": "<p><ul><content-ref src='/page/58/ListItem/7'></content-ref><content-ref src='/page/58/ListItem/8'></content-ref><content-ref src='/page/58/ListItem/9'></content-ref><content-ref src='/page/58/ListItem/10'></content-ref><content-ref src='/page/58/ListItem/11'></content-ref></ul></p>",
          "polygon": [
            [
              141.42041015625,
              331.998046875
            ],
            [
              527.1328125,
              331.998046875
            ],
            [
              527.1328125,
              472.0
            ],
            [
              141.42041015625,
              472.0
            ]
          ],
          "children": [
            {
              "id": "/page/58/ListItem/7",
              "block_type": "ListItem",
              "html": "<li>1. Start by writing a small program with no function definitions.</li>",
              "polygon": [
                [
                  141.42041015625,
                  331.998046875
                ],
                [
                  427.025390625,
                  331.998046875
                ],
                [
                  427.025390625,
                  343.0
                ],
                [
                  141.42041015625,
                  343.0
                ]
              ],
              "children": null,
              "section_hierarchy": {
                "1": "/page/52/SectionHeader/1",
                "3": "/page/58/SectionHeader/5"
              },
              "images": {}
            },
            {
              "id": "/page/58/ListItem/8",
              "block_type": "ListItem",
              "html": "<li>2. Once you get the program working, encapsulate it in a function and give it a name.</li>",
              "polygon": [
                [
                  142.0,
                  354.814453125
                ],
                [
                  520.55859375,
                  354.814453125
                ],
                [
                  520.55859375,
                  366.0
                ],
                [
                  142.0,
                  366.0
                ]
              ],
              "children": null,
              "section_hierarchy": {
                "1": "/page/52/SectionHeader/1",
                "3": "/page/58/SectionHeader/5"
              },
              "images": {}
            },
            {
              "id": "/page/58/ListItem/9",
              "block_type": "ListItem",
              "html": "<li>3. Generalize the function by adding appropriate parameters.</li>",
              "polygon": [
                [
                  142.0,
                  378.2109375
                ],
                [
                  414.0,
                  378.2109375
                ],
                [
                  414.0,
                  389.0
                ],
                [
                  142.0,
                  389.0
                ]
              ],
              "children": null,
              "section_hierarchy": {
                "1": "/page/52/SectionHeader/1",
                "3": "/page/58/SectionHeader/5"
              },
              "images": {}
            },
            {
              "id": "/page/58/ListItem/10",
              "block_type": "ListItem",
              "html": "<li>4. Repeat steps 1–3 until you have a set of working functions. Copy and paste working code to avoid retyping (and re-debugging).</li>",
              "polygon": [
                [
                  141.64453125,
                  401.02734375
                ],
                [
                  527.1328125,
                  401.02734375
                ],
                [
                  527.1328125,
                  425.0
                ],
                [
                  141.64453125,
                  425.0
                ]
              ],
              "children": null,
              "section_hierarchy": {
                "1": "/page/52/SectionHeader/1",
                "3": "/page/58/SectionHeader/5"
              },
              "images": {}
            },
            {
              "id": "/page/58/ListItem/11",
              "block_type": "ListItem",
              "html": "<li>5. Look for opportunities to improve the program by refactoring. For example, if you have similar code in several places, consider factoring it into an appropriately general function.</li>",
              "polygon": [
                [
                  141.64453125,
                  436.9921875
                ],
                [
                  526.53515625,
                  436.9921875
                ],
                [
                  526.53515625,
                  472.0
                ],
                [
                  141.64453125,
                  472.0
                ]
              ],
              "children": null,
              "section_hierarchy": {
                "1": "/page/52/SectionHeader/1",
                "3": "/page/58/SectionHeader/5"
              },
              "images": {}
            }
          ],
          "section_hierarchy": {
            "1": "/page/52/SectionHeader/1",
            "3": "/page/58/SectionHeader/5"
          },
          "images": null
        },
        {
          "id": "/page/58/Text/12",
          "block_type": "Text",
          "html": "<p>This process has some drawbacks—we will see alternatives later—but it can be useful if you don't know ahead of time how to divide the program into functions. This approach lets you design as you go along.</p>",
          "polygon": [
            [
              128.794921875,
              488.8125
            ],
            [
              527.431640625,
              488.8125
            ],
            [
              527.431640625,
              524.0
            ],
            [
              128.794921875,
              524.0
            ]
          ],
          "children": null,
          "section_hierarchy": {
            "1": "/page/52/SectionHeader/1",
            "3": "/page/58/SectionHeader/13"
          },
          "images": {}
        },
        {
          "id": "/page/58/SectionHeader/13",
          "block_type": "SectionHeader",
          "html": "<h3><b>4.9 docstring</b></h3>",
          "polygon": [
            [
              128.42138671875,
              558.0
            ],
            [
              224.419921875,
              558.0
            ],
            [
              224.419921875,
              573.0
            ],
            [
              128.42138671875,
              573.0
            ]
          ],
          "children": null,
          "section_hierarchy": {
            "1": "/page/52/SectionHeader/1",
            "3": "/page/58/SectionHeader/13"
          },
          "images": {}
        },
        {
          "id": "/page/58/Text/14",
          "block_type": "Text",
          "html": "<p>A <b>docstring</b> is a string at the beginning of a function that explains the interface (\"doc\" is short for \"documentation\"). Here is an example:</p>",
          "polygon": [
            [
              128.3466796875,
              586.265625
            ],
            [
              526.53515625,
              586.265625
            ],
            [
              526.53515625,
              610.0
            ],
