      ],
      "children": [
        {
          "id": "/page/59/PageHeader/0",
          "block_type": "PageHeader",
          "html": "<p><b>38 Chapter 4. Case study: interface design</b></p>",
          "polygon": [
            [
              86.0,
              60.95654296875
            ],
            [
              483.50390625,
              60.95654296875
            ],
            [
              483.50390625,
              71.0
            ],
            [
              86.0,
              71.0
            ]
          ],
          "children": null,
          "section_hierarchy": {
            "1": "/page/52/SectionHeader/1",
            "3": "/page/58/SectionHeader/13"
          },
          "images": {}
        },
        {
          "id": "/page/59/PageHeader/17",
          "block_type": "PageHeader",
          "html": "<p></p>",
          "polygon": [
            [
              85.24072265625,
              60.37646484375
            ],
            [
              96.44677734375,
              60.37646484375
            ],
            [
              96.44677734375,
              70.14111328125
            ],
            [
              85.24072265625,
              70.14111328125
            ]
          ],
          "children": null,
          "section_hierarchy": {
            "1": "/page/52/SectionHeader/1",
            "3": "/page/58/SectionHeader/13"
          },
          "images": {}
        },
        {
          "id": "/page/59/Text/1",
          "block_type": "Text",
          "html": "<p>This docstring is a triple-quoted string, also known as a multiline string because the triple quotes allow the string to span more than one line.</p>",
          "polygon": [
            [
              85.9130859375,
              88.02685546875
            ],
            [
              483.50390625,
              88.02685546875
            ],
            [
              483.50390625,
              111.0
            ],
            [
              85.9130859375,
              111.0
            ]
          ],
          "children": null,
          "section_hierarchy": {
            "1": "/page/52/SectionHeader/1",
            "3": "/page/58/SectionHeader/13"
          },
          "images": {}
        },
        {
          "id": "/page/59/Text/2",
          "block_type": "Text",
          "html": "<p>It is terse, but it contains the essential information someone would need to use this function. It explains concisely what the function does (without getting into the details of how it does it). It explains what effect each parameter has on the behavior of the function and what type each parameter should be (if it is not obvious).</p>",
          "polygon": [
            [
              85.46484375,
              120.076171875
            ],
            [
              482.90625,
              120.076171875
            ],
            [
              482.90625,
              167.0
            ],
            [
              85.46484375,
              167.0
            ]
          ],
          "children": null,
          "section_hierarchy": {
            "1": "/page/52/SectionHeader/1",
            "3": "/page/58/SectionHeader/13"
          },
          "images": {}
        },
        {
          "id": "/page/59/Text/3",
          "block_type": "Text",
          "html": "<p>Writing this kind of documentation is an important part of interface design. A welldesigned interface should be simple to explain; if you are having a hard time explaining one of your functions, that might be a sign that the interface could be improved.</p>",
          "polygon": [
            [
              86.0,
              176.4404296875
            ],
            [
              483.50390625,
              176.4404296875
            ],
            [
              483.50390625,
              212.0
            ],
            [
              86.0,
              212.0
            ]
          ],
          "children": null,
          "section_hierarchy": {
            "1": "/page/52/SectionHeader/1",
            "3": "/page/59/SectionHeader/4"
          },
          "images": {}
        },
        {
          "id": "/page/59/SectionHeader/4",
          "block_type": "SectionHeader",
          "html": "<h3><b>4.10 Debugging</b></h3>",
          "polygon": [
            [
              86.0,
              240.345703125
            ],
            [
              200.3642578125,
              240.345703125
            ],
            [
              200.3642578125,
              255.0
            ],
            [
              86.0,
              255.0
            ]
          ],
          "children": null,
          "section_hierarchy": {
            "1": "/page/52/SectionHeader/1",
            "3": "/page/59/SectionHeader/4"
          },
          "images": {}
        },
        {
          "id": "/page/59/Text/5",
          "block_type": "Text",
          "html": "<p>An interface is like a contract between a function and a caller. The caller agrees to provide certain parameters and the function agrees to do certain work.</p>",
          "polygon": [
            [
              85.9130859375,
              265.095703125
            ],
            [
              482.90625,
              265.095703125
            ],
            [
              482.90625,
              289.0
            ],
            [
              85.9130859375,
              289.0
            ]
          ],
          "children": null,
          "section_hierarchy": {
            "1": "/page/52/SectionHeader/1",
            "3": "/page/59/SectionHeader/4"
          },
          "images": {}
        },
        {
          "id": "/page/59/Text/6",
          "block_type": "Text",
          "html": "<p>For example, polyline requires four arguments: t has to be a Turtle; n is the number of line segments, so it has to be an integer; length should be a positive number; and angle has to be a number, which is understood to be in degrees.</p>",
          "polygon": [
            [
              85.166015625,
              297.580078125
            ],
            [
              484.1015625,
              297.580078125
            ],
            [
              484.1015625,
              333.544921875
            ],
            [
              85.166015625,
              333.544921875
            ]
          ],
          "children": null,
          "section_hierarchy": {
            "1": "/page/52/SectionHeader/1",
            "3": "/page/59/SectionHeader/4"
          },
          "images": {}
        },
        {
          "id": "/page/59/Text/7",
          "block_type": "Text",
          "html": "<p>These requirements are called <b>preconditions</b> because they are supposed to be true before the function starts executing. Conversely, conditions at the end of the function are <b>post</b><b>conditions</b>. Postconditions include the intended effect of the function (like drawing line segments) and any side effects (like moving the Turtle or making other changes in the World).</p>",
          "polygon": [
            [
              85.46484375,
              342.052734375
            ],
            [
              484.69921875,
              342.052734375
            ],
            [
              484.69921875,
              402.1875
            ],
            [
              85.46484375,
              402.1875
            ]
          ],
          "children": null,
          "section_hierarchy": {
            "1": "/page/52/SectionHeader/1",
            "3": "/page/59/SectionHeader/4"
          },
          "images": {}
        },
        {
          "id": "/page/59/Text/8",
          "block_type": "Text",
          "html": "<p>Preconditions are the responsibility of the caller. If the caller violates a (properly documented!) precondition and the function doesn't work correctly, the bug is in the caller, not the function.</p>",
          "polygon": [
            [
              85.166015625,
              409.921875
            ],
            [
              484.69921875,
              409.921875
            ],
            [
              484.69921875,
              446.0
            ],
            [
              85.166015625,
              446.0
            ]
          ],
          "children": null,
          "section_hierarchy": {
            "1": "/page/52/SectionHeader/1",
            "3": "/page/59/SectionHeader/9"
          },
          "images": {}
        },
        {
          "id": "/page/59/SectionHeader/9",
          "block_type": "SectionHeader",
          "html": "<h3><b>4.11 Glossary</b></h3>",
          "polygon": [
