        {
          "id": "/page/67/SectionHeader/3",
          "block_type": "SectionHeader",
          "html": "<h3><b>5.10 Infinite recursion</b></h3>",
          "polygon": [
            [
              85.3154296875,
              250.787109375
            ],
            [
              239.0,
              250.787109375
            ],
            [
              239.0,
              266.0
            ],
            [
              85.3154296875,
              266.0
            ]
          ],
          "children": null,
          "section_hierarchy": {
            "1": "/page/62/SectionHeader/1",
            "3": "/page/67/SectionHeader/3"
          },
          "images": {}
        },
        {
          "id": "/page/67/Text/4",
          "block_type": "Text",
          "html": "<p>If a recursion never reaches a base case, it goes on making recursive calls forever, and the program never terminates. This is known as <b>infinite recursion</b>, and it is generally not a good idea. Here is a minimal program with an infinite recursion:</p>",
          "polygon": [
            [
              85.6142578125,
              279.2109375
            ],
            [
              482.90625,
              279.2109375
            ],
            [
              482.90625,
              314.40234375
            ],
            [
              85.6142578125,
              314.40234375
            ]
          ],
          "children": null,
          "section_hierarchy": {
            "1": "/page/62/SectionHeader/1",
            "3": "/page/67/SectionHeader/3"
          },
          "images": {}
        },
        {
          "id": "/page/67/Code/5",
          "block_type": "Code",
          "html": "<pre>def recurse():\n    recurse()</pre>",
          "polygon": [
            [
              85.68896484375,
              320.9765625
            ],
            [
              160.76953125,
              320.9765625
            ],
            [
              160.76953125,
              344.0
            ],
            [
              85.68896484375,
              344.0
            ]
          ],
          "children": null,
          "section_hierarchy": {
            "1": "/page/62/SectionHeader/1",
            "3": "/page/67/SectionHeader/3"
          },
          "images": {}
        },
        {
          "id": "/page/67/Text/6",
          "block_type": "Text",
          "html": "<p>In most programming environments, a program with infinite recursion does not really run forever. Python reports an error message when the maximum recursion depth is reached:</p>",
          "polygon": [
            [
              85.9130859375,
              350.560546875
            ],
            [
              482.90625,
              350.560546875
            ],
            [
              482.90625,
              373.0
            ],
            [
              85.9130859375,
              373.0
            ]
          ],
          "children": null,
          "section_hierarchy": {
            "1": "/page/62/SectionHeader/1",
            "3": "/page/67/SectionHeader/3"
          },
          "images": {}
        },
        {
          "id": "/page/67/Code/7",
          "block_type": "Code",
          "html": "<pre>File \"&lt;stdin&gt;\", line 2, in recurse\nFile \"&lt;stdin&gt;\", line 2, in recurse\nFile \"&lt;stdin&gt;\", line 2, in recurse\n                .\n                .\n                .\nFile \"&lt;stdin&gt;\", line 2, in recurse</pre>",
          "polygon": [
            [
              95.55029296875,
              380.337890625
            ],
            [
              281.197265625,
              380.337890625
            ],
            [
              281.197265625,
              464.44921875
            ],
            [
