          "children": null,
          "section_hierarchy": {
            "1": "/page/62/SectionHeader/1",
            "3": "/page/67/SectionHeader/10"
          },
          "images": {}
        },
        {
          "id": "/page/67/Text/11",
          "block_type": "Text",
          "html": "<p>The programs we have written so far are a bit rude in the sense that they accept no input from the user. They just do the same thing every time.</p>",
          "polygon": [
            [
              85.6142578125,
              565.76953125
            ],
            [
              482.30859375,
              565.76953125
            ],
            [
              482.30859375,
              589.0
            ],
            [
              85.6142578125,
              589.0
            ]
          ],
          "children": null,
          "section_hierarchy": {
            "1": "/page/62/SectionHeader/1",
            "3": "/page/67/SectionHeader/10"
          },
          "images": {}
        },
        {
          "id": "/page/67/Text/12",
          "block_type": "Text",
          "html": "<p>Python 2 provides a built-in function called raw_input that gets input from the keyboard. In Python 3, it is called input. When this function is called, the program stops and waits for the user to type something. When the user presses Return or Enter, the program resumes and raw_input returns what the user typed as a string.</p>",
          "polygon": [
            [
              85.46484375,
              598.640625
            ],
            [
              482.607421875,
              598.640625
            ],
            [
              482.607421875,
              647.0
            ],
            [
              85.46484375,
              647.0
            ]
          ],
          "children": null,
          "section_hierarchy": {
            "1": "/page/62/SectionHeader/1",
            "3": "/page/67/SectionHeader/10"
          },
          "images": {}
        },
        {
          "id": "/page/67/Code/13",
          "block_type": "Code",
          "html": "<pre>&gt;&gt;&gt; text = raw_input()\nWhat are you waiting for?\n&gt;&gt;&gt; print text\nWhat are you waiting for?</pre>",
          "polygon": [
            [
              84.26953125,
              653.16796875
            ],
