          "images": {}
        },
        {
          "id": "/page/70/Text/14",
          "block_type": "Text",
          "html": "<p><i>If any of the three lengths is greater than the sum of the other two, then you cannot</i> <i>form a triangle. Otherwise, you can. (If the sum of two lengths equals the third, they</i> <i>form what is called a \"degenerate\" triangle.)</i></p>",
          "polygon": [
