          },
          "images": {}
        },
        {
          "id": "/page/73/Text/1",
          "block_type": "Text",
          "html": "<p>Since these return statements are in an alternative conditional, only one will be executed.</p>",
          "polygon": [
            [
              85.763671875,
              89.0
            ],
            [
              481.11328125,
              89.0
            ],
            [
              481.11328125,
              99.580078125
            ],
            [
              85.763671875,
              99.580078125
            ]
          ],
          "children": null,
          "section_hierarchy": {
            "1": "/page/72/SectionHeader/1",
            "3": "/page/72/SectionHeader/2"
          },
          "images": {}
        },
        {
          "id": "/page/73/Text/2",
          "block_type": "Text",
          "html": "<p>As soon as a return statement executes, the function terminates without executing any subsequent statements. Code that appears after a return statement, or any other place the flow of execution can never reach, is called <b>dead code</b>.</p>",
          "polygon": [
            [
              85.9130859375,
              109.634765625
            ],
            [
              482.90625,
              109.634765625
            ],
            [
              482.90625,
              144.0
            ],
            [
              85.9130859375,
              144.0
            ]
          ],
          "children": null,
          "section_hierarchy": {
            "1": "/page/72/SectionHeader/1",
            "3": "/page/72/SectionHeader/2"
          },
          "images": {}
        },
        {
          "id": "/page/73/Text/3",
          "block_type": "Text",
          "html": "<p>In a fruitful function, it is a good idea to ensure that every possible path through the program hits a return statement. For example:</p>",
          "polygon": [
            [
              85.166015625,
              154.5908203125
            ],
            [
              482.90625,
              154.5908203125
            ],
            [
              482.90625,
              177.0
            ],
            [
              85.166015625,
              177.0
            ]
          ],
          "children": null,
          "section_hierarchy": {
            "1": "/page/72/SectionHeader/1",
            "3": "/page/72/SectionHeader/2"
          },
          "images": {}
        },
        {
          "id": "/page/73/TextInlineMath/4",
          "block_type": "TextInlineMath",
          "html": "<p>def absolute_value(x): if x &lt; 0: return -x if x &gt; 0: return x</p>",
          "polygon": [
            [
              85.83837890625,
              182.4345703125
            ],
            [
              204.3984375,
              182.4345703125
            ],
            [
              204.3984375,
              245.56640625
            ],
            [
              85.83837890625,
              245.56640625
            ]
          ],
          "children": null,
          "section_hierarchy": {
            "1": "/page/72/SectionHeader/1",
            "3": "/page/72/SectionHeader/2"
          },
          "images": {}
        },
        {
          "id": "/page/73/Text/5",
          "block_type": "Text",
          "html": "<p>This function is incorrect because if x happens to be 0, neither condition is true, and the function ends without hitting a return statement. If the flow of execution gets to the end of a function, the return value is None, which is not the absolute value of 0.</p>",
          "polygon": [
            [
              86.0,
              248.2734375
            ],
            [
              482.90625,
              248.2734375
            ],
            [
              482.90625,
              284.0
            ],
            [
              86.0,
              284.0
            ]
          ],
          "children": null,
          "section_hierarchy": {
            "1": "/page/72/SectionHeader/1",
            "3": "/page/72/SectionHeader/2"
          },
          "images": {}
        },
        {
          "id": "/page/73/Code/6",
          "block_type": "Code",
          "html": "<pre>&gt;&gt;&gt; print absolute_value(0)\nNone</pre>",
          "polygon": [
            [
              85.166015625,
              291.0
            ],
            [
              228.0,
              289.458984375
            ],
            [
              228.0,
              313.0
            ],
            [
              85.166015625,
              313.822265625
            ]
          ],
          "children": null,
          "section_hierarchy": {
            "1": "/page/72/SectionHeader/1",
            "3": "/page/72/SectionHeader/2"
          },
          "images": {}
        },
        {
          "id": "/page/73/Text/7",
          "block_type": "Text",
          "html": "<p>By the way, Python provides a built-in function called abs that computes absolute values. <b>Exercise 6.1.</b> <i>Write a</i> compare <i>function that returns</i> 1 if x &gt; y, 0 if x == y<i>, and</i> -1 if x &lt; y.</p>",
          "polygon": [
            [
              85.0166015625,
              320.0
            ],
            [
              480.515625,
              318.462890625
            ],
            [
              480.515625,
              342.0
            ],
            [
              85.0166015625,
              342.052734375
            ]
          ],
          "children": null,
          "section_hierarchy": {
            "1": "/page/72/SectionHeader/1",
            "3": "/page/73/SectionHeader/8"
          },
          "images": {}
        },
        {
          "id": "/page/73/SectionHeader/8",
          "block_type": "SectionHeader",
          "html": "<h3><b>6.2 Incremental development</b></h3>",
          "polygon": [
            [
              85.763671875,
              372.216796875
            ],
            [
              287.173828125,
              372.216796875
            ],
            [
              287.173828125,
              388.0
            ],
            [
              85.763671875,
              388.0
            ]
          ],
          "children": null,
          "section_hierarchy": {
            "1": "/page/72/SectionHeader/1",
            "3": "/page/73/SectionHeader/8"
          },
          "images": {}
        },
        {
          "id": "/page/73/Text/9",
          "block_type": "Text",
          "html": "<p>As you write larger functions, you might find yourself spending more time debugging.</p>",
          "polygon": [
            [
              85.9130859375,
              399.09375
            ],
            [
              469.16015625,
              399.09375
            ],
            [
              469.16015625,
              411.0
            ],
            [
              85.9130859375,
              411.0
            ]
          ],
          "children": null,
          "section_hierarchy": {
            "1": "/page/72/SectionHeader/1",
            "3": "/page/73/SectionHeader/8"
          },
          "images": {}
        },
        {
          "id": "/page/73/Text/10",
          "block_type": "Text",
          "html": "<p>To deal with increasingly complex programs, you might want to try a process called in<b>cremental development</b>. The goal of incremental development is to avoid long debugging sessions by adding and testing only a small amount of code at a time.</p>",
          "polygon": [
            [
              85.46484375,
              420.75
            ],
            [
              483.50390625,
              420.75
            ],
            [
              483.50390625,
              456.328125
            ],
            [
              85.46484375,
              456.328125
            ]
          ],
          "children": null,
          "section_hierarchy": {
            "1": "/page/72/SectionHeader/1",
            "3": "/page/73/SectionHeader/8"
          },
          "images": {}
        },
        {
          "id": "/page/73/Text/11",
          "block_type": "Text",
          "html": "<p>As an example, suppose you want to find the distance between two points, given by the coordinates (x1, y1) and (x2, y2). By the Pythagorean theorem, the distance is:</p>",
          "polygon": [
            [
              85.166015625,
              465.99609375
            ],
            [
              483.802734375,
              465.99609375
            ],
            [
              483.802734375,
              490.0
            ],
            [
              85.166015625,
              490.0
            ]
          ],
          "children": null,
          "section_hierarchy": {
            "1": "/page/72/SectionHeader/1",
            "3": "/page/73/SectionHeader/8"
          },
          "images": {}
        },
        {
          "id": "/page/73/Equation/12",
          "block_type": "Equation",
          "html": "\n<p><math>$${\\mathrm{distance}}={\\sqrt{(x_{2}-x_{1})^{2}+(y_{2}-y_{1})^{2}}}$$</math></p>\n",
          "polygon": [
            [
              202.7548828125,
              508.0
            ],
            [
              366.9609375,
              508.0
            ],
            [
              366.9609375,
              527.87109375
            ],
            [
              202.7548828125,
              527.87109375
            ]
          ],
          "children": null,
          "section_hierarchy": {
            "1": "/page/72/SectionHeader/1",
            "3": "/page/73/SectionHeader/8"
          },
          "images": {}
        },
        {
          "id": "/page/73/Text/13",
          "block_type": "Text",
          "html": "<p>The first step is to consider what a distance function should look like in Python. In other words, what are the inputs (parameters) and what is the output (return value)?</p>",
          "polygon": [
            [
              85.6142578125,
              532.51171875
            ],
            [
              483.50390625,
              532.51171875
            ],
            [
              483.50390625,
              556.0
            ],
            [
              85.6142578125,
              556.0
            ]
          ],
          "children": null,
          "section_hierarchy": {
            "1": "/page/72/SectionHeader/1",
            "3": "/page/73/SectionHeader/8"
          },
          "images": {}
        },
        {
          "id": "/page/73/Text/14",
          "block_type": "Text",
          "html": "<p>In this case, the inputs are two points, which you can represent using four numbers. The return value is the distance, which is a floating-point value.</p>",
          "polygon": [
            [
              85.46484375,
              565.76953125
            ],
            [
              483.50390625,
              565.76953125
            ],
            [
              483.50390625,
              589.0
            ],
            [
              85.46484375,
              589.0
            ]
          ],
          "children": null,
          "section_hierarchy": {
            "1": "/page/72/SectionHeader/1",
            "3": "/page/73/SectionHeader/8"
          },
          "images": {}
        },
        {
          "id": "/page/73/Text/15",
          "block_type": "Text",
          "html": "<p>Already you can write an outline of the function:</p>",
          "polygon": [
            [
              85.763671875,
              598.25390625
            ],
            [
              301.517578125,
              598.25390625
            ],
            [
              301.517578125,
              610.0
            ],
            [
              85.763671875,
              610.0
            ]
          ],
          "children": null,
          "section_hierarchy": {
            "1": "/page/72/SectionHeader/1",
            "3": "/page/73/SectionHeader/8"
          },
          "images": {}
        },
        {
          "id": "/page/73/Code/16",
          "block_type": "Code",
          "html": "<pre>def distance(x1, y1, x2, y2):\n    return 0.0</pre>",
          "polygon": [
            [
              85.0166015625,
              616.0
            ],
            [
              238.0,
              616.0
            ],
            [
              238.0,
              639.0
            ],
            [
              85.0166015625,
              639.0
            ]
          ],
          "children": null,
          "section_hierarchy": {
            "1": "/page/72/SectionHeader/1",
            "3": "/page/73/SectionHeader/8"
          },
          "images": {}
        },
        {
          "id": "/page/73/Text/17",
          "block_type": "Text",
          "html": "<p>Obviously, this version doesn't compute distances; it always returns zero. But it is syntactically correct, and it runs, which means that you can test it before you make it more complicated.</p>",
          "polygon": [
            [
              85.166015625,
              644.2734375
            ],
            [
              482.90625,
              644.2734375
            ],
            [
              482.90625,
              680.0
            ],
            [
              85.166015625,
              680.0
            ]
          ],
          "children": null,
          "section_hierarchy": {
            "1": "/page/72/SectionHeader/1",
            "3": "/page/73/SectionHeader/8"
          },
          "images": {}
        },
        {
          "id": "/page/73/Text/18",
          "block_type": "Text",
          "html": "<p>To test the new function, call it with sample arguments:</p>",
          "polygon": [
            [
              86.0,
              690.6796875
            ],
            [
              330.802734375,
              690.6796875
            ],
            [
              330.802734375,
              701.0
            ],
            [
              86.0,
              701.0
            ]
          ],
          "children": null,
          "section_hierarchy": {
            "1": "/page/72/SectionHeader/1",
            "3": "/page/73/SectionHeader/8"
          },
          "images": {}
        }
      ],
      "section_hierarchy": {
        "1": "/page/72/SectionHeader/1",
        "3": "/page/73/SectionHeader/8"
      },
      "images": null
    },
    {
      "id": "/page/74/Page/230",
      "block_type": "Page",
      "html": "<content-ref src='/page/74/PageHeader/0'></content-ref><content-ref src='/page/74/PageHeader/15'></content-ref><content-ref src='/page/74/Text/1'></content-ref><content-ref src='/page/74/Text/2'></content-ref><content-ref src='/page/74/TextInlineMath/3'></content-ref><content-ref src='/page/74/Code/4'></content-ref><content-ref src='/page/74/Text/5'></content-ref><content-ref src='/page/74/Text/16'></content-ref><content-ref src='/page/74/Text/17'></content-ref><content-ref src='/page/74/Text/6'></content-ref><content-ref src='/page/74/Code/7'></content-ref><content-ref src='/page/74/Text/8'></content-ref><content-ref src='/page/74/Code/9'></content-ref><content-ref src='/page/74/Text/10'></content-ref><content-ref src='/page/74/Text/11'></content-ref><content-ref src='/page/74/Text/12'></content-ref><content-ref src='/page/74/Text/13'></content-ref><content-ref src='/page/74/ListItem/14'></content-ref>",
      "polygon": [
