      ],
      "children": [
        {
          "id": "/page/74/PageHeader/0",
          "block_type": "PageHeader",
          "html": "<p><b>6.2. Incremental development 53</b></p>",
          "polygon": [
            [
              127.97314453125,
              61.0
            ],
            [
              526.0,
              61.0
            ],
            [
              526.0,
              71.0
            ],
            [
              127.97314453125,
              71.0
            ]
          ],
          "children": null,
          "section_hierarchy": {
            "1": "/page/72/SectionHeader/1",
            "3": "/page/73/SectionHeader/8"
          },
          "images": {}
        },
        {
          "id": "/page/74/PageHeader/15",
          "block_type": "PageHeader",
          "html": "<p></p>",
          "polygon": [
            [
              515.77734375,
              60.76318359375
            ],
            [
              525.9375,
              60.76318359375
            ],
            [
              525.9375,
              70.23779296875
            ],
            [
              515.77734375,
              70.23779296875
            ]
          ],
          "children": null,
          "section_hierarchy": {
            "1": "/page/72/SectionHeader/1",
            "3": "/page/73/SectionHeader/8"
          },
          "images": {}
        },
        {
          "id": "/page/74/Text/1",
          "block_type": "Text",
          "html": "<p>&gt;&gt;&gt; distance(1, 2, 4, 6) 0.0</p>",
          "polygon": [
            [
              130.0,
              89.0
            ],
            [
              255.9462890625,
              87.93017578125
            ],
            [
              255.9462890625,
              111.0
            ],
            [
              130.0,
              111.0
            ]
          ],
          "children": null,
          "section_hierarchy": {
            "1": "/page/72/SectionHeader/1",
            "3": "/page/73/SectionHeader/8"
          },
          "images": {}
        },
        {
          "id": "/page/74/Text/2",
          "block_type": "Text",
          "html": "<p>I chose these values so that the horizontal distance is 3 and the vertical distance is 4; that way, the result is 5 (the hypotenuse of a 3-4-5 triangle). When testing a function, it is useful to know the right answer.</p>",
          "polygon": [
            [
              129.392578125,
              117.0
            ],
            [
              526.0,
              117.0
            ],
            [
              526.0,
              151.20703125
            ],
            [
              129.392578125,
              151.20703125
            ]
          ],
          "children": null,
          "section_hierarchy": {
            "1": "/page/72/SectionHeader/1",
            "3": "/page/73/SectionHeader/8"
          },
          "images": {}
        },
        {
          "id": "/page/74/TextInlineMath/3",
          "block_type": "TextInlineMath",
          "html": "<p>At this point we have confirmed that the function is syntactically correct, and we can start adding code to the body. A reasonable next step is to find the differences x2 − x1 and y2 − y1. The next version stores those values in temporary variables and prints them.</p>",
          "polygon": [
            [
              129.09375,
              160.681640625
            ],
            [
              526.53515625,
              160.681640625
            ],
            [
              526.53515625,
              197.0
            ],
            [
              129.09375,
              197.0
            ]
          ],
          "children": null,
          "section_hierarchy": {
            "1": "/page/72/SectionHeader/1",
            "3": "/page/73/SectionHeader/8"
          },
          "images": {}
        },
        {
          "id": "/page/74/Code/4",
          "block_type": "Code",
          "html": "<pre>def distance(x1, y1, x2, y2):\n    dx = x2 - x1\n    dy = y2 - y1\n    print 'dx is', dx\n    print 'dy is', dy\n    return 0.0</pre>",
          "polygon": [
            [
              129.69140625,
              202.0
            ],
            [
              281.0,
              202.0
            ],
            [
              281.0,
              278.630859375
            ],
            [
              129.69140625,
              278.630859375
            ]
          ],
          "children": null,
          "section_hierarchy": {
            "1": "/page/72/SectionHeader/1",
            "3": "/page/73/SectionHeader/8"
          },
          "images": {}
        },
        {
          "id": "/page/74/Text/5",
          "block_type": "Text",
          "html": "<p>If the function is working, it should display dx is 3 and 'dy is 4'. If so, we know that the function is getting the right arguments and performing the first computation correctly. If not, there are only a few lines to check.</p>",
          "polygon": [
            [
              128.9443359375,
              279.0
            ],
            [
              526.0,
              279.0
            ],
            [
              526.0,
              313.62890625
            ],
            [
              128.9443359375,
              313.62890625
            ]
          ],
          "children": null,
          "section_hierarchy": {
            "1": "/page/72/SectionHeader/1",
            "3": "/page/73/SectionHeader/8"
          },
          "images": {}
        },
        {
          "id": "/page/74/Text/16",
          "block_type": "Text",
          "html": "<p>'</p>",
          "polygon": [
            [
              321.0,
              265.0
            ],
            [
              327.0,
              265.0
            ],
            [
              327.0,
              275.0
            ],
            [
              321.0,
              275.0
            ]
          ],
          "children": null,
          "section_hierarchy": {
            "1": "/page/72/SectionHeader/1",
            "3": "/page/73/SectionHeader/8"
          },
          "images": {}
        },
        {
          "id": "/page/74/Text/17",
          "block_type": "Text",
          "html": "<p>'</p>",
          "polygon": [
            [
              363.0,
              265.0
            ],
            [
              368.0,
              265.0
            ],
            [
              368.0,
              275.0
            ],
            [
              363.0,
              275.0
            ]
          ],
          "children": null,
          "section_hierarchy": {
            "1": "/page/72/SectionHeader/1",
            "3": "/page/73/SectionHeader/8"
          },
          "images": {}
        },
        {
          "id": "/page/74/Text/6",
          "block_type": "Text",
          "html": "<p>Next we compute the sum of squares of dx and dy:</p>",
          "polygon": [
            [
              128.9443359375,
              323.0
            ],
            [
              352.0,
              323.0
            ],
            [
              352.0,
              333.3515625
            ],
            [
              128.9443359375,
              333.3515625
            ]
          ],
          "children": null,
          "section_hierarchy": {
            "1": "/page/72/SectionHeader/1",
            "3": "/page/73/SectionHeader/8"
          },
          "images": {}
        },
        {
          "id": "/page/74/Code/7",
          "block_type": "Code",
          "html": "<pre>def distance(x1, y1, x2, y2):\n    dx = x2 - x1\n    dy = y2 - y1\n    dsquared = dx**2 + dy**2\n    print 'dsquared is: ', dsquared\n    return 0.0</pre>",
          "polygon": [
            [
              130.0,
              339.0
            ],
            [
              314.3671875,
              339.0
            ],
            [
              314.3671875,
              411.46875
            ],
            [
              130.0,
              411.46875
            ]
          ],
          "children": null,
          "section_hierarchy": {
            "1": "/page/72/SectionHeader/1",
            "3": "/page/73/SectionHeader/8"
          },
          "images": {}
        },
        {
          "id": "/page/74/Text/8",
          "block_type": "Text",
          "html": "<p>Again, you would run the program at this stage and check the output (which should be 25). Finally, you can use math.sqrt to compute and return the result:</p>",
          "polygon": [
            [
              128.6455078125,
              416.0
            ],
            [
              526.53515625,
              416.0
            ],
            [
              526.53515625,
              439.0
            ],
            [
              128.6455078125,
              439.0
            ]
          ],
          "children": null,
          "section_hierarchy": {
            "1": "/page/72/SectionHeader/1",
            "3": "/page/73/SectionHeader/8"
          },
          "images": {}
        },
        {
          "id": "/page/74/Code/9",
          "block_type": "Code",
          "html": "<pre>def distance(x1, y1, x2, y2):\n    dx = x2 - x1\n    dy = y2 - y1\n    dsquared = dx**2 + dy**2\n    result = math.sqrt(dsquared)\n    return result</pre>",
          "polygon": [
            [
              127.4501953125,
              442.01953125
            ],
            [
              297.0,
              442.01953125
            ],
            [
              297.0,
              517.81640625
            ],
            [
              127.4501953125,
              517.81640625
            ]
          ],
          "children": null,
          "section_hierarchy": {
            "1": "/page/72/SectionHeader/1",
            "3": "/page/73/SectionHeader/8"
          },
          "images": {}
        },
        {
          "id": "/page/74/Text/10",
          "block_type": "Text",
          "html": "<p>If that works correctly, you are done. Otherwise, you might want to print the value of result before the return statement.</p>",
          "polygon": [
            [
              129.2431640625,
              520.5234375
            ],
            [
              527.1328125,
              520.5234375
            ],
            [
              527.1328125,
              544.0
            ],
            [
              129.2431640625,
              544.0
            ]
          ],
          "children": null,
          "section_hierarchy": {
            "1": "/page/72/SectionHeader/1",
            "3": "/page/73/SectionHeader/8"
          },
          "images": {}
        },
        {
          "id": "/page/74/Text/11",
          "block_type": "Text",
          "html": "<p>The final version of the function doesn't display anything when it runs; it only returns a value. The print statements we wrote are useful for debugging, but once you get the function working, you should remove them. Code like that is called <b>scaffolding</b> because it is helpful for building the program but is not part of the final product.</p>",
          "polygon": [
            [
              128.49609375,
              552.62109375
            ],
            [
              526.0,
              552.62109375
            ],
            [
              526.0,
              600.57421875
            ],
            [
              128.49609375,
              600.57421875
            ]
          ],
          "children": null,
          "section_hierarchy": {
            "1": "/page/72/SectionHeader/1",
            "3": "/page/73/SectionHeader/8"
          },
          "images": {}
        },
        {
          "id": "/page/74/Text/12",
          "block_type": "Text",
          "html": "<p>When you start out, you should add only a line or two of code at a time. As you gain more experience, you might find yourself writing and debugging bigger chunks. Either way, incremental development can save you a lot of debugging time.</p>",
          "polygon": [
            [
              128.3466796875,
              610.0
            ],
            [
              526.53515625,
              608.6953125
            ],
            [
              526.53515625,
              645.0
            ],
            [
              128.3466796875,
              645.046875
            ]
          ],
          "children": null,
          "section_hierarchy": {
            "1": "/page/72/SectionHeader/1",
            "3": "/page/73/SectionHeader/8"
          },
          "images": {}
        },
        {
          "id": "/page/74/Text/13",
          "block_type": "Text",
          "html": "<p>The key aspects of the process are:</p>",
          "polygon": [
            [
              130.0,
