          },
          "images": null
        },
        {
          "id": "/page/75/Text/3",
          "block_type": "Text",
          "html": "<p><b>Exercise 6.2.</b> <i>Use incremental development to write a function called</i> hypotenuse <i>that returns the</i> <i>length of the hypotenuse of a right triangle given the lengths of the two legs as arguments. Record</i> <i>each stage of the development process as you go.</i></p>",
          "polygon": [
            [
              86.0,
              163.0986328125
            ],
            [
              482.90625,
              163.0986328125
            ],
            [
              482.90625,
              198.0
            ],
            [
              86.0,
              198.0
            ]
          ],
          "children": null,
          "section_hierarchy": {
            "1": "/page/72/SectionHeader/1",
            "3": "/page/75/SectionHeader/4"
          },
          "images": {}
        },
        {
          "id": "/page/75/SectionHeader/4",
          "block_type": "SectionHeader",
          "html": "<h3><b>6.3 Composition</b></h3>",
          "polygon": [
            [
              85.9130859375,
              230.291015625
            ],
            [
              204.0,
              230.291015625
            ],
            [
              204.0,
              245.0
            ],
            [
              85.9130859375,
              245.0
            ]
          ],
          "children": null,
          "section_hierarchy": {
            "1": "/page/72/SectionHeader/1",
            "3": "/page/75/SectionHeader/4"
          },
          "images": {}
        },
        {
          "id": "/page/75/Text/5",
          "block_type": "Text",
          "html": "<p>As you should expect by now, you can call one function from within another. This ability is called <b>composition</b>.</p>",
          "polygon": [
            [
              86.0,
              258.521484375
            ],
            [
              482.30859375,
              258.521484375
            ],
            [
              482.30859375,
              281.337890625
            ],
            [
              86.0,
              281.337890625
            ]
          ],
          "children": null,
          "section_hierarchy": {
            "1": "/page/72/SectionHeader/1",
            "3": "/page/75/SectionHeader/4"
          },
          "images": {}
        },
        {
          "id": "/page/75/Text/6",
          "block_type": "Text",
          "html": "<p>As an example, we'll write a function that takes two points, the center of the circle and a point on the perimeter, and computes the area of the circle.</p>",
          "polygon": [
            [
              85.46484375,
              291.392578125
            ],
            [
              482.30859375,
              291.392578125
            ],
            [
              482.30859375,
              314.208984375
            ],
            [
              85.46484375,
              314.208984375
            ]
          ],
          "children": null,
          "section_hierarchy": {
            "1": "/page/72/SectionHeader/1",
            "3": "/page/75/SectionHeader/4"
          },
          "images": {}
        },
        {
          "id": "/page/75/Text/7",
          "block_type": "Text",
          "html": "<p>Assume that the center point is stored in the variables xc and yc, and the perimeter point is in xp and yp. The first step is to find the radius of the circle, which is the distance between the two points. We just wrote a function, distance, that does that:</p>",
          "polygon": [
            [
              85.6142578125,
              323.876953125
            ],
            [
              483.50390625,
              323.876953125
            ],
            [
              483.50390625,
              360.0
            ],
            [
              85.6142578125,
              360.0
            ]
          ],
          "children": null,
          "section_hierarchy": {
            "1": "/page/72/SectionHeader/1",
            "3": "/page/75/SectionHeader/4"
          },
          "images": {}
        },
        {
          "id": "/page/75/TextInlineMath/8",
          "block_type": "TextInlineMath",
          "html": "<p>radius = distance(xc, yc, xp, yp)</p>",
          "polygon": [
            [
              85.46484375,
              367.0
            ],
            [
              259.0,
              367.0
            ],
            [
              259.0,
              377.244140625
            ],
            [
              85.46484375,
              377.244140625
            ]
          ],
          "children": null,
          "section_hierarchy": {
            "1": "/page/72/SectionHeader/1",
            "3": "/page/75/SectionHeader/4"
          },
          "images": {}
        },
        {
          "id": "/page/75/Text/9",
          "block_type": "Text",
          "html": "<p>The next step is to find the area of a circle with that radius; we just wrote that, too:</p>",
          "polygon": [
            [
              85.6142578125,
              382.271484375
            ],
            [
              447.046875,
              382.271484375
            ],
            [
              447.046875,
              394.0
            ],
            [
              85.6142578125,
              394.0
            ]
          ],
          "children": null,
          "section_hierarchy": {
            "1": "/page/72/SectionHeader/1",
            "3": "/page/75/SectionHeader/4"
          },
          "images": {}
        },
        {
          "id": "/page/75/Text/10",
          "block_type": "Text",
          "html": "<p>result = area(radius)</p>",
          "polygon": [
            [
              86.0,
              398.70703125
            ],
            [
              196.0,
              398.70703125
            ],
            [
              196.0,
              411.0
            ],
            [
              86.0,
              411.0
            ]
          ],
          "children": null,
          "section_hierarchy": {
            "1": "/page/72/SectionHeader/1",
            "3": "/page/75/SectionHeader/4"
          },
          "images": {}
        },
        {
          "id": "/page/75/Text/11",
          "block_type": "Text",
          "html": "<p>Encapsulating these steps in a function, we get:</p>",
          "polygon": [
            [
              85.53955078125,
              417.26953125
            ],
            [
              294.0,
              417.26953125
            ],
            [
              294.0,
              428.0
            ],
            [
              85.53955078125,
              428.0
            ]
          ],
          "children": null,
          "section_hierarchy": {
            "1": "/page/72/SectionHeader/1",
            "3": "/page/75/SectionHeader/4"
          },
          "images": {}
        },
        {
          "id": "/page/75/Code/12",
          "block_type": "Code",
          "html": "<pre>def circle_area(xc, yc, xp, yp):\n    radius = distance(xc, yc, xp, yp)\n    result = area(radius)\n    return result</pre>",
          "polygon": [
            [
              85.68896484375,
              434.28515625
            ],
            [
              280.0,
              434.28515625
            ],
            [
              280.0,
              483.01171875
            ],
            [
              85.68896484375,
              483.01171875
            ]
          ],
          "children": null,
          "section_hierarchy": {
            "1": "/page/72/SectionHeader/1",
            "3": "/page/75/SectionHeader/4"
          },
          "images": {}
        },
        {
          "id": "/page/75/Text/13",
          "block_type": "Text",
          "html": "<p>The temporary variables radius and result are useful for development and debugging, but once the program is working, we can make it more concise by composing the function calls:</p>",
          "polygon": [
            [
              85.46484375,
              488.0390625
            ],
            [
              482.607421875,
              488.0390625
            ],
            [
              482.607421875,
              523.0
            ],
            [
              85.46484375,
              523.0
            ]
          ],
          "children": null,
          "section_hierarchy": {
            "1": "/page/72/SectionHeader/1",
            "3": "/page/75/SectionHeader/4"
          },
          "images": {}
        },
        {
          "id": "/page/75/Text/14",
          "block_type": "Text",
          "html": "<p>def circle_area(xc, yc, xp, yp): return area(distance(xc, yc, xp, yp))</p>",
          "polygon": [
            [
              85.0166015625,
              530.0
            ],
            [
              301.0,
              530.0
            ],
            [
              301.0,
              552.0
            ],
            [
              85.0166015625,
              552.0
            ]
          ],
          "children": null,
          "section_hierarchy": {
            "1": "/page/72/SectionHeader/1",
            "3": "/page/75/SectionHeader/15"
          },
          "images": {}
        },
        {
          "id": "/page/75/SectionHeader/15",
          "block_type": "SectionHeader",
          "html": "<h3><b>6.4 Boolean functions</b></h3>",
          "polygon": [
            [
              85.46484375,
              584.33203125
            ],
            [
              238.0,
              584.33203125
            ],
            [
              238.0,
              599.02734375
            ],
            [
              85.46484375,
              599.02734375
            ]
          ],
          "children": null,
          "section_hierarchy": {
            "1": "/page/72/SectionHeader/1",
            "3": "/page/75/SectionHeader/15"
          },
          "images": {}
        },
        {
          "id": "/page/75/Text/16",
          "block_type": "Text",
          "html": "<p>Functions can return booleans, which is often convenient for hiding complicated tests inside functions. For example:</p>",
          "polygon": [
            [
              85.166015625,
              612.5625
            ],
            [
              482.0,
              612.5625
            ],
            [
              482.0,
              635.0
            ],
            [
              85.166015625,
              635.0
            ]
          ],
          "children": null,
          "section_hierarchy": {
            "1": "/page/72/SectionHeader/1",
            "3": "/page/75/SectionHeader/15"
          },
          "images": {}
        },
        {
          "id": "/page/75/Code/17",
          "block_type": "Code",
          "html": "<pre>def is_divisible(x, y):\n    if x % y == 0:\n        return True\n    else:\n        return False</pre>",
          "polygon": [
            [
              84.4189453125,
              641.56640625
            ],
            [
              207.0,
              641.56640625
            ],
            [
              207.0,
              702.66796875
            ],
            [
              84.4189453125,
              702.66796875
            ]
          ],
          "children": null,
          "section_hierarchy": {
            "1": "/page/72/SectionHeader/1",
            "3": "/page/75/SectionHeader/15"
          },
          "images": {}
        }
      ],
      "section_hierarchy": {
        "1": "/page/72/SectionHeader/1",
