      ],
      "children": [
        {
          "id": "/page/77/PageHeader/0",
          "block_type": "PageHeader",
          "html": "<p><b>56 Chapter 6. Fruitful functions</b></p>",
          "polygon": [
            [
              86.0,
              61.0
            ],
            [
              482.30859375,
              61.0
            ],
            [
              482.30859375,
              71.0
            ],
            [
              86.0,
              71.0
            ]
          ],
          "children": null,
          "section_hierarchy": {
            "1": "/page/72/SectionHeader/1",
            "3": "/page/76/SectionHeader/9"
          },
          "images": {}
        },
        {
          "id": "/page/77/PageHeader/20",
          "block_type": "PageHeader",
          "html": "<p></p>",
          "polygon": [
            [
              85.6142578125,
              61.14990234375
            ],
            [
              96.3720703125,
              61.14990234375
            ],
            [
              96.3720703125,
              70.04443359375
            ],
            [
              85.6142578125,
              70.04443359375
            ]
          ],
          "children": null,
          "section_hierarchy": {
            "1": "/page/72/SectionHeader/1",
            "3": "/page/76/SectionHeader/9"
          },
          "images": {}
        },
        {
          "id": "/page/77/Text/1",
          "block_type": "Text",
          "html": "<p>This definition says that the factorial of 0 is 1, and the factorial of any other value, n, is n multiplied by the factorial of n − 1.</p>",
          "polygon": [
            [
              85.763671875,
              87.78515625
            ],
            [
              482.607421875,
              87.78515625
            ],
            [
              482.607421875,
              111.0
            ],
            [
              85.763671875,
              111.0
            ]
          ],
          "children": null,
          "section_hierarchy": {
            "1": "/page/72/SectionHeader/1",
            "3": "/page/76/SectionHeader/9"
          },
          "images": {}
        },
        {
          "id": "/page/77/Text/2",
          "block_type": "Text",
          "html": "<p>So 3! is 3 times 2!, which is 2 times 1!, which is 1 times 0!. Putting it all together, 3! equals 3 times 2 times 1 times 1, which is 6.</p>",
          "polygon": [
            [
              85.166015625,
              121.81640625
            ],
            [
              482.009765625,
              121.81640625
            ],
            [
              482.009765625,
              145.0
            ],
            [
              85.166015625,
              145.0
            ]
          ],
          "children": null,
          "section_hierarchy": {
            "1": "/page/72/SectionHeader/1",
            "3": "/page/76/SectionHeader/9"
          },
          "images": {}
        },
        {
          "id": "/page/77/Text/3",
          "block_type": "Text",
          "html": "<p>If you can write a recursive definition of something, you can usually write a Python program to evaluate it. The first step is to decide what the parameters should be. In this case it should be clear that factorial takes an integer:</p>",
          "polygon": [
            [
              85.3154296875,
              156.0
            ],
            [
              482.30859375,
              156.0
            ],
            [
              482.30859375,
              190.0
            ],
            [
              85.3154296875,
              190.0
            ]
          ],
          "children": null,
          "section_hierarchy": {
            "1": "/page/72/SectionHeader/1",
            "3": "/page/76/SectionHeader/9"
          },
          "images": {}
        },
        {
          "id": "/page/77/Text/4",
          "block_type": "Text",
          "html": "<p>def factorial(n):</p>",
          "polygon": [
            [
              85.0166015625,
              198.0
            ],
            [
              175.0,
              198.0
            ],
            [
              175.0,
              208.44140625
            ],
            [
              85.0166015625,
              208.44140625
            ]
          ],
          "children": null,
          "section_hierarchy": {
            "1": "/page/72/SectionHeader/1",
            "3": "/page/76/SectionHeader/9"
          },
          "images": {}
        },
        {
          "id": "/page/77/Text/5",
          "block_type": "Text",
          "html": "<p>If the argument happens to be 0, all we have to do is return 1:</p>",
          "polygon": [
            [
              85.6142578125,
              215.0
            ],
            [
              356.0,
              215.0
            ],
            [
              356.0,
              225.0703125
            ],
            [
              85.6142578125,
              225.0703125
            ]
          ],
          "children": null,
          "section_hierarchy": {
            "1": "/page/72/SectionHeader/1",
            "3": "/page/76/SectionHeader/9"
          },
          "images": {}
        },
        {
          "id": "/page/77/TextInlineMath/6",
          "block_type": "TextInlineMath",
          "html": "<p>def factorial(n): if n == 0: return 1</p>",
          "polygon": [
            [
              85.39013671875,
              231.2578125
            ],
            [
              175.0,
              231.2578125
            ],
            [
              175.0,
              267.0
            ],
            [
              85.39013671875,
              267.0
            ]
          ],
          "children": null,
          "section_hierarchy": {
            "1": "/page/72/SectionHeader/1",
            "3": "/page/76/SectionHeader/9"
          },
          "images": {}
        },
        {
          "id": "/page/77/Text/7",
          "block_type": "Text",
          "html": "<p>Otherwise, and this is the interesting part, we have to make a recursive call to find the factorial of n − 1 and then multiply it by n:</p>",
          "polygon": [
            [
              85.6142578125,
              273.990234375
            ],
            [
              482.90625,
              273.990234375
            ],
            [
              482.90625,
              296.0
            ],
            [
              85.6142578125,
              296.0
            ]
          ],
          "children": null,
          "section_hierarchy": {
            "1": "/page/72/SectionHeader/1",
            "3": "/page/76/SectionHeader/9"
          },
          "images": {}
        },
        {
          "id": "/page/77/Code/8",
          "block_type": "Code",
          "html": "<pre>def factorial(n):\n    if n == 0:\n        return 1\n    else:\n        recurse = factorial(n-1)\n        result = n * recurse\n        return result</pre>",
          "polygon": [
            [
              85.166015625,
              304.0
            ],
            [
              254.0,
              304.0
            ],
            [
              254.0,
              387.0
            ],
            [
              85.166015625,
              387.0
            ]
          ],
          "children": null,
          "section_hierarchy": {
            "1": "/page/72/SectionHeader/1",
            "3": "/page/76/SectionHeader/9"
          },
          "images": {}
        },
        {
          "id": "/page/77/Text/9",
          "block_type": "Text",
          "html": "<p>The flow of execution for this program is similar to the flow of countdown in Section 5.8. If we call factorial with the value 3:</p>",
          "polygon": [
            [
              85.3154296875,
              393.099609375
            ],
            [
              482.0,
              393.099609375
            ],
            [
              482.0,
              417.0
            ],
            [
              85.3154296875,
              417.0
            ]
          ],
          "children": null,
          "section_hierarchy": {
            "1": "/page/72/SectionHeader/1",
            "3": "/page/76/SectionHeader/9"
          },
          "images": {}
        },
        {
          "id": "/page/77/Text/10",
          "block_type": "Text",
          "html": "<p>Since 3 is not 0, we take the second branch and calculate the factorial of n-1...</p>",
          "polygon": [
            [
              84.8671875,
              426.55078125
            ],
            [
              425.0,
              426.55078125
            ],
            [
              425.0,
              438.0
            ],
            [
              84.8671875,
              438.0
            ]
          ],
          "children": null,
          "section_hierarchy": {
            "1": "/page/72/SectionHeader/1",
            "3": "/page/76/SectionHeader/9"
          },
          "images": {}
        },
        {
          "id": "/page/77/Text/11",
          "block_type": "Text",
          "html": "<p>Since 2 is not 0, we take the second branch and calculate the factorial of n-1...</p>",
          "polygon": [
            [
              110.4169921875,
              453.62109375
            ],
            [
              450.0,
              453.62109375
            ],
            [
              450.0,
              464.0
            ],
            [
              110.4169921875,
              464.0
            ]
          ],
          "children": null,
          "section_hierarchy": {
            "1": "/page/72/SectionHeader/1",
            "3": "/page/76/SectionHeader/9"
          },
          "images": {}
        },
        {
          "id": "/page/77/Text/12",
          "block_type": "Text",
          "html": "<p>Since 1 is not 0, we take the second branch and calculate the factorial of n-1...</p>",
          "polygon": [
            [
              132.30615234375,
              472.95703125
            ],
            [
              436.0,
              472.95703125
            ],
            [
              436.0,
              495.0
            ],
            [
              132.30615234375,
              495.0
            ]
          ],
          "children": null,
          "section_hierarchy": {
            "1": "/page/72/SectionHeader/1",
            "3": "/page/76/SectionHeader/9"
          },
          "images": {}
        },
        {
          "id": "/page/77/Text/13",
          "block_type": "Text",
          "html": "<p>Since 0 is 0, we take the first branch and return 1 without making any more recursive calls.</p>",
          "polygon": [
            [
              151.0576171875,
              503.0
            ],
            [
              417.76171875,
              503.0
            ],
            [
              417.76171875,
              525.0
            ],
            [
              151.0576171875,
              525.0
            ]
          ],
          "children": null,
          "section_hierarchy": {
            "1": "/page/72/SectionHeader/1",
            "3": "/page/76/SectionHeader/9"
          },
          "images": {}
        },
        {
          "id": "/page/77/Text/14",
          "block_type": "Text",
          "html": "<p>The return value (1) is multiplied by n, which is 1, and the result is returned.</p>",
          "polygon": [
            [
              131.70849609375,
              533.0
            ],
            [
              436.2890625,
              533.0
            ],
            [
              436.2890625,
              556.1015625
            ],
            [
              131.70849609375,
              556.1015625
            ]
          ],
          "children": null,
          "section_hierarchy": {
            "1": "/page/72/SectionHeader/1",
            "3": "/page/76/SectionHeader/9"
          },
          "images": {}
        },
        {
          "id": "/page/77/Text/15",
          "block_type": "Text",
          "html": "<p>The return value (1) is multiplied by n, which is 2, and the result is returned.</p>",
          "polygon": [
            [
              110.1181640625,
              563.8359375
            ],
            [
              447.046875,
              563.8359375
            ],
            [
              447.046875,
              574.0
            ],
            [
              110.1181640625,
              574.0
            ]
          ],
          "children": null,
          "section_hierarchy": {
            "1": "/page/72/SectionHeader/1",
            "3": "/page/76/SectionHeader/9"
          },
          "images": {}
        },
        {
          "id": "/page/77/Text/16",
          "block_type": "Text",
          "html": "<p>The return value (2) is multiplied by n, which is 3, and the result, 6, becomes the return value of the function call that started the whole process.</p>",
          "polygon": [
            [
              85.9130859375,
              588.97265625
            ],
            [
              482.30859375,
              588.97265625
            ],
            [
              482.30859375,
              612.0
            ],
            [
              85.9130859375,
              612.0
            ]
          ],
          "children": null,
          "section_hierarchy": {
            "1": "/page/72/SectionHeader/1",
            "3": "/page/76/SectionHeader/9"
          },
          "images": {}
        },
        {
          "id": "/page/77/Text/17",
          "block_type": "Text",
          "html": "<p>Figure 6.1 shows what the stack diagram looks like for this sequence of function calls.</p>",
          "polygon": [
            [
              86.0,
              623.390625
            ],
            [
              466.171875,
              623.390625
            ],
            [
              466.171875,
              634.0
            ],
            [
              86.0,
              634.0
            ]
          ],
          "children": null,
          "section_hierarchy": {
            "1": "/page/72/SectionHeader/1",
            "3": "/page/76/SectionHeader/9"
          },
          "images": {}
        },
        {
          "id": "/page/77/Text/18",
          "block_type": "Text",
          "html": "<p>The return values are shown being passed back up the stack. In each frame, the return value is the value of result, which is the product of n and recurse.</p>",
          "polygon": [
            [
              85.9130859375,
              645.0
            ],
            [
              483.50390625,
              645.0
            ],
            [
              483.50390625,
              667.0
            ],
            [
              85.9130859375,
              667.0
            ]
          ],
          "children": null,
          "section_hierarchy": {
            "1": "/page/72/SectionHeader/1",
            "3": "/page/76/SectionHeader/9"
          },
          "images": {}
        },
        {
          "id": "/page/77/Text/19",
          "block_type": "Text",
          "html": "<p>In the last frame, the local variables recurse and result do not exist, because the branch that creates them does not execute.</p>",
