          ],
          "children": null,
          "section_hierarchy": {
            "1": "/page/72/SectionHeader/1",
            "3": "/page/79/SectionHeader/3"
          },
          "images": {}
        },
        {
          "id": "/page/80/Text/1",
          "block_type": "Text",
          "html": "<p>If we get past both checks, then we know that n is positive or zero, so we can prove that the recursion terminates.</p>",
          "polygon": [
            [
              128.9443359375,
              89.0
            ],
            [
              526.0,
              89.0
            ],
            [
              526.0,
              111.0
            ],
            [
              128.9443359375,
              111.0
            ]
          ],
          "children": null,
          "section_hierarchy": {
            "1": "/page/72/SectionHeader/1",
            "3": "/page/79/SectionHeader/3"
          },
          "images": {}
        },
        {
          "id": "/page/80/Text/2",
          "block_type": "Text",
          "html": "<p>This program demonstrates a pattern sometimes called a <b>guardian</b>. The first two conditionals act as guardians, protecting the code that follows from values that might cause an error. The guardians make it possible to prove the correctness of the code.</p>",
          "polygon": [
            [
              128.794921875,
              121.9130859375
            ],
            [
              526.0,
              121.9130859375
            ],
            [
              526.0,
              157.0
            ],
            [
              128.794921875,
              157.0
            ]
          ],
          "children": null,
          "section_hierarchy": {
            "1": "/page/72/SectionHeader/1",
            "3": "/page/79/SectionHeader/3"
          },
          "images": {}
        },
        {
          "id": "/page/80/Text/3",
          "block_type": "Text",
          "html": "<p>In Section 11.3 we will see a more flexible alternative to printing an error message: raising an exception.</p>",
          "polygon": [
            [
              128.9443359375,
              169.0
            ],
            [
              526.0,
              169.0
            ],
            [
              526.0,
              192.0
            ],
            [
              128.9443359375,
              192.0
            ]
          ],
          "children": null,
          "section_hierarchy": {
            "1": "/page/72/SectionHeader/1",
            "3": "/page/80/SectionHeader/4"
          },
          "images": {}
        },
        {
          "id": "/page/80/SectionHeader/4",
          "block_type": "SectionHeader",
          "html": "<h3><b>6.9 Debugging</b></h3>",
          "polygon": [
            [
              128.49609375,
              226.0
            ],
            [
              236.0,
              226.0
            ],
            [
              236.0,
              241.505859375
            ],
            [
              128.49609375,
              241.505859375
            ]
          ],
          "children": null,
          "section_hierarchy": {
            "1": "/page/72/SectionHeader/1",
            "3": "/page/80/SectionHeader/4"
          },
          "images": {}
        },
        {
          "id": "/page/80/Text/5",
          "block_type": "Text",
          "html": "<p>Breaking a large program into smaller functions creates natural checkpoints for debugging. If a function is not working, there are three possibilities to consider:</p>",
          "polygon": [
            [
              129.09375,
              254.654296875
            ],
            [
              526.0,
              254.654296875
            ],
            [
              526.0,
              278.0
            ],
            [
              129.09375,
              278.0
            ]
          ],
          "children": null,
          "section_hierarchy": {
            "1": "/page/72/SectionHeader/1",
            "3": "/page/80/SectionHeader/4"
          },
          "images": {}
        },
        {
          "id": "/page/80/ListGroup/190",
          "block_type": "ListGroup",
          "html": "<p><ul><content-ref src='/page/80/ListItem/6'></content-ref><content-ref src='/page/80/ListItem/7'></content-ref><content-ref src='/page/80/ListItem/8'></content-ref></ul></p>",
          "polygon": [
            [
              142.83984375,
              294.29296875
            ],
            [
              527.431640625,
              294.29296875
            ],
            [
              527.431640625,
              364.0
            ],
            [
              142.83984375,
              364.0
            ]
          ],
          "children": [
            {
              "id": "/page/80/ListItem/6",
              "block_type": "ListItem",
              "html": "<li> There is something wrong with the arguments the function is getting; a precondition is violated.</li>",
              "polygon": [
                [
                  143.0,
                  294.29296875
                ],
                [
                  527.431640625,
                  294.29296875
                ],
                [
                  527.431640625,
                  318.0
                ],
                [
                  143.0,
                  318.0
                ]
              ],
              "children": null,
              "section_hierarchy": {
                "1": "/page/72/SectionHeader/1",
                "3": "/page/80/SectionHeader/4"
              },
              "images": {}
            },
            {
              "id": "/page/80/ListItem/7",
              "block_type": "ListItem",
              "html": "<li> There is something wrong with the function; a postcondition is violated.</li>",
              "polygon": [
                [
                  142.83984375,
                  329.87109375
                ],
                [
                  472.1484375,
                  329.87109375
                ],
                [
                  472.1484375,
                  341.0
                ],
                [
                  142.83984375,
                  341.0
                ]
              ],
              "children": null,
              "section_hierarchy": {
                "1": "/page/72/SectionHeader/1",
                "3": "/page/80/SectionHeader/4"
              },
              "images": {}
            },
            {
              "id": "/page/80/ListItem/8",
              "block_type": "ListItem",
              "html": "<li> There is something wrong with the return value or the way it is being used.</li>",
              "polygon": [
                [
                  143.0,
                  353.267578125
                ],
                [
                  486.0,
                  353.267578125
                ],
                [
                  486.0,
                  364.0
                ],
                [
                  143.0,
                  364.0
                ]
              ],
              "children": null,
              "section_hierarchy": {
                "1": "/page/72/SectionHeader/1",
                "3": "/page/80/SectionHeader/4"
              },
              "images": {}
            }
          ],
          "section_hierarchy": {
            "1": "/page/72/SectionHeader/1",
            "3": "/page/80/SectionHeader/4"
          },
          "images": null
        },
        {
          "id": "/page/80/Text/9",
          "block_type": "Text",
          "html": "<p>To rule out the first possibility, you can add a print statement at the beginning of the function and display the values of the parameters (and maybe their types). Or you can write code that checks the preconditions explicitly.</p>",
          "polygon": [
            [
              128.6455078125,
              379.951171875
            ],
            [
              526.53515625,
              379.951171875
            ],
            [
              526.53515625,
              416.0
            ],
            [
              128.6455078125,
              416.0
            ]
          ],
          "children": null,
          "section_hierarchy": {
            "1": "/page/72/SectionHeader/1",
            "3": "/page/80/SectionHeader/4"
          },
          "images": {}
        },
        {
          "id": "/page/80/Text/10",
          "block_type": "Text",
          "html": "<p>If the parameters look good, add a print statement before each return statement that displays the return value. If possible, check the result by hand. Consider calling the function with values that make it easy to check the result (as in Section 6.2).</p>",
          "polygon": [
            [
              128.794921875,
              426.55078125
            ],
            [
              526.833984375,
              426.55078125
            ],
            [
              526.833984375,
              462.90234375
            ],
            [
              128.794921875,
              462.90234375
            ]
          ],
          "children": null,
          "section_hierarchy": {
            "1": "/page/72/SectionHeader/1",
            "3": "/page/80/SectionHeader/4"
          },
          "images": {}
        },
        {
          "id": "/page/80/Text/11",
          "block_type": "Text",
          "html": "<p>If the function seems to be working, look at the function call to make sure the return value is being used correctly (or used at all!).</p>",
          "polygon": [
            [
              129.2431640625,
              473.34375
            ],
            [
              527.1328125,
              473.34375
            ],
            [
              527.1328125,
              497.0
            ],
            [
              129.2431640625,
              497.0
            ]
          ],
          "children": null,
          "section_hierarchy": {
            "1": "/page/72/SectionHeader/1",
            "3": "/page/80/SectionHeader/4"
          },
          "images": {}
        },
        {
          "id": "/page/80/Text/12",
          "block_type": "Text",
          "html": "<p>Adding print statements at the beginning and end of a function can help make the flow of execution more visible. For example, here is a version of factorial with print statements:</p>",
          "polygon": [
            [
              128.9443359375,
              508.921875
            ],
            [
              527.1328125,
              508.921875
            ],
            [
              527.1328125,
              531.0
            ],
            [
              128.9443359375,
              531.0
            ]
          ],
          "children": null,
          "section_hierarchy": {
            "1": "/page/72/SectionHeader/1",
            "3": "/page/80/SectionHeader/4"
          },
          "images": {}
        },
        {
          "id": "/page/80/Code/13",
          "block_type": "Code",
          "html": "<pre>def factorial(n):\n    space = ' ' * (4 * n)\n    print space, 'factorial', n\n    if n == 0:\n        print space, 'returning 1'\n                                    \n        return 1\n    else:\n        recurse = factorial(n-1)\n        result = n * recurse\n        print space, 'returning', result\n        return result</pre>",
          "polygon": [
            [
              130.0,
              537.0
            ],
            [
              339.0,
              537.0
            ],
            [
              339.0,
              670.95703125
            ],
            [
              130.0,
              670.95703125
            ]
          ],
          "children": null,
          "section_hierarchy": {
            "1": "/page/72/SectionHeader/1",
            "3": "/page/80/SectionHeader/4"
          },
          "images": {}
        },
        {
          "id": "/page/80/Text/14",
          "block_type": "Text",
          "html": "<p>space is a string of space characters that controls the indentation of the output. Here is the result of factorial(5) :</p>",
          "polygon": [
            [
              128.197265625,
              677.91796875
            ],
            [
              526.236328125,
              677.91796875
            ],
            [
              526.236328125,
              701.0
            ],
            [
              128.197265625,
              701.0
            ]
          ],
          "children": null,
          "section_hierarchy": {
            "1": "/page/72/SectionHeader/1",
            "3": "/page/80/SectionHeader/4"
          },
          "images": {}
        }
      ],
      "section_hierarchy": {
