        },
        {
          "id": "/page/87/Text/3",
          "block_type": "Text",
          "html": "<p>The loop condition is True, which is always true, so the loop runs until it hits the break statement.</p>",
          "polygon": [
            [
              85.3154296875,
              177.9873046875
            ],
            [
              482.90625,
              177.9873046875
            ],
            [
              482.90625,
              202.0
            ],
            [
              85.3154296875,
              202.0
            ]
          ],
          "children": null,
          "section_hierarchy": {
            "1": "/page/84/SectionHeader/1",
            "3": "/page/86/SectionHeader/12"
          },
          "images": {}
        },
        {
          "id": "/page/87/Text/4",
          "block_type": "Text",
          "html": "<p>Each time through, it prompts the user with an angle bracket. If the user types done, the break statement exits the loop. Otherwise the program echoes whatever the user types and goes back to the top of the loop. Here's a sample run:</p>",
          "polygon": [
            [
              85.0166015625,
              211.921875
            ],
            [
              482.30859375,
              211.921875
            ],
            [
              482.30859375,
              248.0
            ],
            [
              85.0166015625,
              248.0
            ]
          ],
          "children": null,
          "section_hierarchy": {
            "1": "/page/84/SectionHeader/1",
            "3": "/page/86/SectionHeader/12"
          },
          "images": {}
        },
        {
          "id": "/page/87/TextInlineMath/5",
          "block_type": "TextInlineMath",
          "html": "<p>&gt; not done not done &gt; done Done!</p>",
          "polygon": [
            [
              85.166015625,
              254.07421875
            ],
            [
              139.0,
              254.07421875
            ],
            [
              139.0,
              302.80078125
            ],
            [
              85.166015625,
              302.80078125
            ]
          ],
          "children": null,
          "section_hierarchy": {
            "1": "/page/84/SectionHeader/1",
            "3": "/page/86/SectionHeader/12"
          },
          "images": {}
        },
        {
          "id": "/page/87/Text/6",
          "block_type": "Text",
          "html": "<p>This way of writing while loops is common because you can check the condition anywhere in the loop (not just at the top) and you can express the stop condition affirmatively (\"stop when this happens\") rather than negatively (\"keep going until that happens.\").</p>",
          "polygon": [
            [
              85.166015625,
              308.98828125
            ],
            [
              483.50390625,
              308.98828125
            ],
            [
              483.50390625,
              344.0
            ],
            [
              85.166015625,
              344.0
            ]
          ],
          "children": null,
          "section_hierarchy": {
            "1": "/page/84/SectionHeader/1",
            "3": "/page/87/SectionHeader/7"
          },
          "images": {}
        },
        {
          "id": "/page/87/SectionHeader/7",
          "block_type": "SectionHeader",
          "html": "<h3><b>7.5 Square roots</b></h3>",
          "polygon": [
            [
              85.166015625,
              375.50390625
            ],
            [
              201.0,
              375.50390625
            ],
            [
              201.0,
              392.0
            ],
            [
              85.166015625,
              392.0
            ]
          ],
          "children": null,
          "section_hierarchy": {
            "1": "/page/84/SectionHeader/1",
            "3": "/page/87/SectionHeader/7"
          },
          "images": {}
        },
        {
          "id": "/page/87/Text/8",
          "block_type": "Text",
          "html": "<p>Loops are often used in programs that compute numerical results by starting with an approximate answer and iteratively improving it.</p>",
          "polygon": [
            [
              85.3154296875,
              405.28125
            ],
            [
              482.0,
              405.28125
            ],
            [
              482.0,
              429.2578125
            ],
            [
              85.3154296875,
              429.2578125
            ]
          ],
          "children": null,
          "section_hierarchy": {
            "1": "/page/84/SectionHeader/1",
            "3": "/page/87/SectionHeader/7"
          },
          "images": {}
        },
        {
          "id": "/page/87/Text/9",
          "block_type": "Text",
          "html": "<p>For example, one way of computing square roots is Newton's method. Suppose that you want to know the square root of a. If you start with almost any estimate, x, you can compute a better estimate with the following formula:</p>",
          "polygon": [
            [
              85.3154296875,
              438.92578125
            ],
            [
              483.50390625,
              438.92578125
            ],
            [
              483.50390625,
              475.0
            ],
            [
              85.3154296875,
              475.0
            ]
          ],
          "children": null,
          "section_hierarchy": {
            "1": "/page/84/SectionHeader/1",
            "3": "/page/87/SectionHeader/7"
          },
          "images": {}
        },
        {
          "id": "/page/87/Equation/10",
          "block_type": "Equation",
          "html": "\n<p><math>$$y={\\frac{x+a/x}{2}}$$</math></p>\n",
          "polygon": [
            [
              255.19921875,
              494.0
            ],
            [
              312.275390625,
              494.0
            ],
            [
              312.275390625,
              518.0
            ],
            [
              255.19921875,
              518.0
            ]
          ],
          "children": null,
          "section_hierarchy": {
            "1": "/page/84/SectionHeader/1",
            "3": "/page/87/SectionHeader/7"
          },
          "images": {}
        },
        {
          "id": "/page/87/Text/11",
          "block_type": "Text",
          "html": "<p>For example, if a is 4 and x is 3:</p>",
          "polygon": [
            [
              84.8671875,
              521.296875
            ],
            [
              224.0,
              521.296875
            ],
            [
              224.0,
              533.0
            ],
            [
              84.8671875,
              533.0
            ]
          ],
          "children": null,
          "section_hierarchy": {
            "1": "/page/84/SectionHeader/1",
            "3": "/page/87/SectionHeader/7"
          },
          "images": {}
        },
        {
          "id": "/page/87/Code/12",
          "block_type": "Code",
          "html": "<pre>&gt;&gt;&gt; a = 4.0\n&gt;&gt;&gt; x = 3.0\n&gt;&gt;&gt; y = (x + a/x) / 2\n&gt;&gt;&gt; print y\n2.16666666667</pre>",
          "polygon": [
            [
              85.3154296875,
              540.0
            ],
            [
              197.0771484375,
              540.0
            ],
            [
              197.0771484375,
              599.0
            ],
            [
              85.3154296875,
              599.0
            ]
          ],
          "children": null,
          "section_hierarchy": {
            "1": "/page/84/SectionHeader/1",
            "3": "/page/87/SectionHeader/7"
          },
          "images": {}
        },
        {
          "id": "/page/87/TextInlineMath/13",
          "block_type": "TextInlineMath",
          "html": "<p>Which is closer to the correct answer (√ 4 = 2). If we repeat the process with the new estimate, it gets even closer:</p>",
          "polygon": [
            [
              85.6142578125,
              597.0
            ],
            [
              482.30859375,
              597.0
            ],
            [
              482.30859375,
              629.0
            ],
            [
              85.6142578125,
              629.0
            ]
          ],
          "children": null,
          "section_hierarchy": {
            "1": "/page/84/SectionHeader/1",
            "3": "/page/87/SectionHeader/7"
          },
          "images": {}
        },
        {
          "id": "/page/87/Code/14",
          "block_type": "Code",
          "html": "<pre>&gt;&gt;&gt; x = y\n&gt;&gt;&gt; y = (x + a/x) / 2\n&gt;&gt;&gt; print y\n2.00641025641</pre>",
          "polygon": [
            [
              84.4189453125,
              634.60546875
            ],
            [
              198.8701171875,
              634.60546875
            ],
            [
              198.8701171875,
              683.33203125
            ],
            [
              84.4189453125,
              683.33203125
            ]
          ],
          "children": null,
          "section_hierarchy": {
            "1": "/page/84/SectionHeader/1",
            "3": "/page/87/SectionHeader/7"
          },
          "images": {}
        },
        {
          "id": "/page/87/Text/15",
          "block_type": "Text",
          "html": "<p>After a few more updates, the estimate is almost exact:</p>",
          "polygon": [
            [
              86.0,
              690.6796875
            ],
            [
              326.0,
              690.6796875
            ],
            [
              326.0,
              701.5078125
            ],
            [
              86.0,
              701.5078125
            ]
          ],
          "children": null,
          "section_hierarchy": {
            "1": "/page/84/SectionHeader/1",
            "3": "/page/87/SectionHeader/7"
          },
          "images": {}
        }
      ],
      "section_hierarchy": {
        "1": "/page/84/SectionHeader/1",
        "3": "/page/87/SectionHeader/7"
      },
      "images": null
    },
    {
      "id": "/page/88/Page/203",
      "block_type": "Page",
      "html": "<content-ref src='/page/88/PageHeader/0'></content-ref><content-ref src='/page/88/PageHeader/13'></content-ref><content-ref src='/page/88/TextInlineMath/1'></content-ref><content-ref src='/page/88/Text/2'></content-ref><content-ref src='/page/88/Code/3'></content-ref><content-ref src='/page/88/Text/4'></content-ref><content-ref src='/page/88/Code/5'></content-ref><content-ref src='/page/88/Text/6'></content-ref><content-ref src='/page/88/Text/7'></content-ref><content-ref src='/page/88/Code/8'></content-ref><content-ref src='/page/88/Text/9'></content-ref><content-ref src='/page/88/SectionHeader/10'></content-ref><content-ref src='/page/88/Text/11'></content-ref><content-ref src='/page/88/Text/12'></content-ref>",
      "polygon": [
        [
          0.0,
          0.0
        ],
        [
          612.0,
          0.0
        ],
        [
          612.0,
          792.0
        ],
        [
          0.0,
          792.0
        ]
      ],
      "children": [
        {
          "id": "/page/88/PageHeader/0",
          "block_type": "PageHeader",
          "html": "<p><b>7.6. Algorithms 67</b></p>",
          "polygon": [
            [
              127.52490234375,
              60.8115234375
            ],
            [
              526.0,
              60.8115234375
            ],
            [
              526.0,
              71.0
            ],
            [
              127.52490234375,
              71.0
            ]
          ],
          "children": null,
          "section_hierarchy": {
            "1": "/page/84/SectionHeader/1",
            "3": "/page/87/SectionHeader/7"
          },
          "images": {}
        },
        {
          "id": "/page/88/PageHeader/13",
          "block_type": "PageHeader",
          "html": "<p></p>",
          "polygon": [
            [
              515.1796875,
              60.47314453125
            ],
            [
              525.9375,
              60.47314453125
            ],
            [
              525.9375,
              70.23779296875
            ],
            [
              515.1796875,
              70.23779296875
            ]
          ],
          "children": null,
          "section_hierarchy": {
            "1": "/page/84/SectionHeader/1",
            "3": "/page/87/SectionHeader/7"
          },
          "images": {}
        },
        {
          "id": "/page/88/TextInlineMath/1",
          "block_type": "TextInlineMath",
          "html": "<p>&gt;&gt;&gt; x = y &gt;&gt;&gt; y = (x + a/x) / 2 &gt;&gt;&gt; print y 2.00001024003 &gt;&gt;&gt; x = y &gt;&gt;&gt; y = (x + a/x) / 2 &gt;&gt;&gt; print y 2.00000000003</p>",
          "polygon": [
            [
              129.09375,
              89.0
            ],
            [
              240.85546875,
              89.0
            ],
            [
              240.85546875,
              184.0
            ],
            [
              129.09375,
              184.0
            ]
          ],
          "children": null,
          "section_hierarchy": {
            "1": "/page/84/SectionHeader/1",
            "3": "/page/87/SectionHeader/7"
          },
          "images": {}
        },
        {
          "id": "/page/88/Text/2",
          "block_type": "Text",
          "html": "<p>In general we don't know ahead of time how many steps it takes to get to the right answer, but we know when we get there because the estimate stops changing:</p>",
          "polygon": [
            [
              128.6455078125,
              189.87890625
            ],
            [
              526.0,
              189.87890625
            ],
            [
              526.0,
              213.0
            ],
            [
              128.6455078125,
              213.0
            ]
          ],
          "children": null,
          "section_hierarchy": {
            "1": "/page/84/SectionHeader/1",
            "3": "/page/87/SectionHeader/7"
          },
          "images": {}
        },
        {
          "id": "/page/88/Code/3",
          "block_type": "Code",
          "html": "<pre>&gt;&gt;&gt; x = y\n&gt;&gt;&gt; y = (x + a/x) / 2\n&gt;&gt;&gt; print y\n2.0\n&gt;&gt;&gt; x = y\n&gt;&gt;&gt; y = (x + a/x) / 2\n&gt;&gt;&gt; print y\n2.0</pre>",
          "polygon": [
            [
              129.69140625,
              219.0
            ],
            [
              241.453125,
              219.0
            ],
            [
              241.453125,
              316.916015625
            ],
            [
              129.69140625,
              316.916015625
            ]
          ],
          "children": null,
          "section_hierarchy": {
            "1": "/page/84/SectionHeader/1",
            "3": "/page/87/SectionHeader/7"
          },
          "images": {}
        },
        {
          "id": "/page/88/Text/4",
          "block_type": "Text",
          "html": "<p>When y == x, we can stop. Here is a loop that starts with an initial estimate, x, and improves it until it stops changing:</p>",
          "polygon": [
            [
              128.3466796875,
              321.0
            ],
            [
              526.0,
              321.0
            ],
            [
              526.0,
              343.40625
            ],
            [
              128.3466796875,
              343.40625
            ]
          ],
          "children": null,
          "section_hierarchy": {
            "1": "/page/84/SectionHeader/1",
            "3": "/page/87/SectionHeader/7"
          },
          "images": {}
        },
        {
          "id": "/page/88/Code/5",
          "block_type": "Code",
          "html": "<pre>while True:\n    print x\n    y = (x + a/x) / 2\n    if y == x:\n        break\n    x = y</pre>",
          "polygon": [
            [
              130.0,
              347.66015625
            ],
            [
              240.1083984375,
              347.66015625
            ],
            [
              240.1083984375,
              420.36328125
            ],
            [
              130.0,
              420.36328125
            ]
          ],
          "children": null,
          "section_hierarchy": {
            "1": "/page/84/SectionHeader/1",
            "3": "/page/87/SectionHeader/7"
          },
          "images": {}
        },
        {
          "id": "/page/88/Text/6",
          "block_type": "Text",
          "html": "<p>For most values of a this works fine, but in general it is dangerous to test float equality. Floating-point values are only approximately right: most rational numbers, like 1/3, and irrational numbers, like √ 2, can't be represented exactly with a float.</p>",
          "polygon": [
            [
              128.9443359375,
              426.9375
            ],
            [
              526.53515625,
              426.9375
            ],
            [
              526.53515625,
              462.515625
            ],
            [
              128.9443359375,
              462.515625
            ]
          ],
          "children": null,
          "section_hierarchy": {
            "1": "/page/84/SectionHeader/1",
            "3": "/page/87/SectionHeader/7"
          },
          "images": {}
        },
        {
          "id": "/page/88/Text/7",
          "block_type": "Text",
          "html": "<p>Rather than checking whether x and y are exactly equal, it is safer to use the built-in function abs to compute the absolute value, or magnitude, of the difference between them:</p>",
          "polygon": [
            [
              128.6455078125,
              471.796875
            ],
            [
              526.0,
              471.796875
            ],
            [
              526.0,
              495.0
            ],
            [
              128.6455078125,
              495.0
            ]
          ],
          "children": null,
          "section_hierarchy": {
            "1": "/page/84/SectionHeader/1",
            "3": "/page/87/SectionHeader/7"
          },
          "images": {}
        },
        {
          "id": "/page/88/Code/8",
          "block_type": "Code",
          "html": "<pre>if abs(y-x) &lt; epsilon:\n    break</pre>",
          "polygon": [
            [
              151.0,
              501.0
            ],
            [
              266.0,
              501.0
            ],
            [
              266.0,
              524.390625
            ],
            [
              151.0,
              524.390625
            ]
          ],
          "children": null,
          "section_hierarchy": {
            "1": "/page/84/SectionHeader/1",
            "3": "/page/87/SectionHeader/7"
          },
          "images": {}
        },
        {
          "id": "/page/88/Text/9",
          "block_type": "Text",
          "html": "<p>Where epsilon has a value like 0.0000001 that determines how close is close enough. <b>Exercise 7.2.</b> <i>Encapsulate this loop in a function called</i> square_root <i>that takes</i> a <i>as a parameter,</i> <i>chooses a reasonable value of</i> x<i>, and returns an estimate of the square root of</i> a.</p>",
          "polygon": [
            [
              128.3466796875,
              529.41796875
            ],
            [
              526.0,
              529.41796875
            ],
            [
              526.0,
              564.22265625
            ],
            [
              128.3466796875,
              564.22265625
            ]
          ],
          "children": null,
          "section_hierarchy": {
            "1": "/page/84/SectionHeader/1",
            "3": "/page/88/SectionHeader/10"
          },
          "images": {}
        },
        {
          "id": "/page/88/SectionHeader/10",
          "block_type": "SectionHeader",
          "html": "<h3><b>7.6 Algorithms</b></h3>",
          "polygon": [
            [
              128.6455078125,
              593.2265625
            ],
            [
              237.0,
              593.2265625
            ],
            [
              237.0,
              609.0
            ],
            [
              128.6455078125,
              609.0
            ]
          ],
          "children": null,
          "section_hierarchy": {
            "1": "/page/84/SectionHeader/1",
            "3": "/page/88/SectionHeader/10"
          },
          "images": {}
        },
        {
          "id": "/page/88/Text/11",
          "block_type": "Text",
          "html": "<p>Newton's method is an example of an <b>algorithm</b>: it is a mechanical process for solving a category of problems (in this case, computing square roots).</p>",
          "polygon": [
            [
              129.2431640625,
              620.296875
            ],
            [
              526.0,
              620.296875
            ],
            [
              526.0,
              644.0
            ],
            [
              129.2431640625,
              644.0
            ]
          ],
          "children": null,
          "section_hierarchy": {
            "1": "/page/84/SectionHeader/1",
            "3": "/page/88/SectionHeader/10"
          },
          "images": {}
        },
        {
          "id": "/page/88/Text/12",
          "block_type": "Text",
          "html": "<p>It is not easy to define an algorithm. It might help to start with something that is not an algorithm. When you learned to multiply single-digit numbers, you probably memorized the multiplication table. In effect, you memorized 100 specific solutions. That kind of knowledge is not algorithmic.</p>",
          "polygon": [
            [
              129.2431640625,
              652.78125
            ],
            [
              526.53515625,
              652.78125
            ],
            [
              526.53515625,
              701.5078125
            ],
            [
              129.2431640625,
              701.5078125
            ]
          ],
          "children": null,
          "section_hierarchy": {
            "1": "/page/84/SectionHeader/1",
            "3": "/page/88/SectionHeader/10"
          },
          "images": {}
        }
      ],
      "section_hierarchy": {
        "1": "/page/84/SectionHeader/1",
        "3": "/page/88/SectionHeader/10"
      },
      "images": null
    },
    {
