        {
          "id": "/page/101/Text/2",
          "block_type": "Text",
          "html": "<p><b>Exercise 8.12.</b> <i>ROT13 is a weak form of encryption that involves \"rotating\" each letter in a word</i> <i>by 13 places. To rotate a letter means to shift it through the alphabet, wrapping around to the</i> <i>beginning if necessary, so 'A' shifted by 3 is 'D' and 'Z' shifted by 1 is 'A'.</i></p>",
          "polygon": [
            [
              85.166015625,
              320.0
            ],
            [
              482.30859375,
              320.0
            ],
            [
              482.30859375,
              355.587890625
