            ]
          ],
          "children": null,
          "section_hierarchy": {
            "1": "/page/102/SectionHeader/1",
            "3": "/page/106/SectionHeader/4"
          },
          "images": {}
        },
        {
          "id": "/page/106/Text/6",
          "block_type": "Text",
          "html": "<p>Taking has_no_e as an example, there are two obvious cases to check: words that have an 'e' should return False; words that don't should return True. You should have no trouble coming up with one of each.</p>",
          "polygon": [
            [
              128.49609375,
              269.9296875
            ],
            [
              527.1328125,
              269.9296875
            ],
            [
              527.1328125,
              305.12109375
            ],
            [
              128.49609375,
              305.12109375
            ]
          ],
          "children": null,
          "section_hierarchy": {
            "1": "/page/102/SectionHeader/1",
            "3": "/page/106/SectionHeader/4"
          },
          "images": {}
        },
        {
          "id": "/page/106/Text/7",
          "block_type": "Text",
          "html": "<p>Within each case, there are some less obvious subcases. Among the words that have an \"e,\" you should test words with an \"e\" at the beginning, the end, and somewhere in the middle. You should test long words, short words, and very short words, like the empty string. The empty string is an example of a <b>special case</b>, which is one of the non-obvious cases where errors often lurk.</p>",
          "polygon": [
            [
              128.3466796875,
              317.109375
            ],
            [
              527.1328125,
              317.109375
            ],
            [
              527.1328125,
              376.27734375
            ],
            [
              128.3466796875,
              376.27734375
            ]
          ],
          "children": null,
          "section_hierarchy": {
            "1": "/page/102/SectionHeader/1",
            "3": "/page/106/SectionHeader/4"
          },
          "images": {}
        },
        {
          "id": "/page/106/Text/8",
          "block_type": "Text",
          "html": "<p>In addition to the test cases you generate, you can also test your program with a word list like words.txt. By scanning the output, you might be able to catch errors, but be careful: you might catch one kind of error (words that should not be included, but are) and not another (words that should be included, but aren't).</p>",
          "polygon": [
            [
              128.794921875,
              387.4921875
            ],
            [
              527.431640625,
              387.4921875
            ],
            [
              527.431640625,
              435.4453125
            ],
            [
              128.794921875,
              435.4453125
            ]
          ],
          "children": null,
          "section_hierarchy": {
            "1": "/page/102/SectionHeader/1",
            "3": "/page/106/SectionHeader/4"
          },
          "images": {}
        },
        {
          "id": "/page/106/Text/9",
          "block_type": "Text",
          "html": "<p>In general, testing can help you find bugs, but it is not easy to generate a good set of test cases, and even if you do, you can't be sure your program is correct.</p>",
          "polygon": [
            [
              129.69140625,
              446.2734375
            ],
            [
              527.1328125,
              446.2734375
            ],
            [
              527.1328125,
