          "children": null,
          "section_hierarchy": {
            "1": "/page/108/SectionHeader/1",
            "3": "/page/113/SectionHeader/6"
          },
          "images": {}
        },
        {
          "id": "/page/113/Text/7",
          "block_type": "Text",
          "html": "<p>There are several ways to delete elements from a list. If you know the index of the element you want, you can use pop: ''''''</p>",
          "polygon": [
            [
              85.9130859375,
              295.453125
            ],
            [
              482.30859375,
              295.453125
            ],
            [
              482.30859375,
              320.0
            ],
            [
              85.9130859375,
              320.0
            ]
          ],
          "children": null,
          "section_hierarchy": {
            "1": "/page/108/SectionHeader/1",
            "3": "/page/113/SectionHeader/6"
          },
          "images": {}
        },
        {
          "id": "/page/113/Code/8",
          "block_type": "Code",
          "html": "<pre>&gt;&gt;&gt; t = [a, b, c]\n&gt;&gt;&gt; x = t.pop(1)\n&gt;&gt;&gt; print t\n['a', 'c']\n&gt;&gt;&gt; print x\nb</pre>",
          "polygon": [
            [
              85.0166015625,
              318.076171875
            ],
            [
              207.0,
              318.076171875
            ],
            [
              207.0,
              394.0
            ],
            [
              85.0166015625,
              394.0
            ]
          ],
          "children": null,
          "section_hierarchy": {
            "1": "/page/108/SectionHeader/1",
            "3": "/page/113/SectionHeader/6"
          },
          "images": {}
        },
        {
          "id": "/page/113/Text/9",
          "block_type": "Text",
          "html": "<p>pop modifies the list and returns the element that was removed. If you don't provide an index, it deletes and returns the last element.</p>",
          "polygon": [
            [
              85.166015625,
              396.38671875
            ],
            [
              482.30859375,
              396.38671875
            ],
            [
              482.30859375,
              421.0
            ],
            [
              85.166015625,
              421.0
            ]
          ],
          "children": null,
          "section_hierarchy": {
            "1": "/page/108/SectionHeader/1",
            "3": "/page/113/SectionHeader/6"
          },
          "images": {}
        },
        {
          "id": "/page/113/Text/10",
          "block_type": "Text",
          "html": "<p>If you don't need the removed value, you can use the del operator: ''''''</p>",
          "polygon": [
            [
              85.3154296875,
              427.32421875
            ],
            [
              381.90234375,
              427.32421875
            ],
            [
              381.90234375,
