        {
          "id": "/page/115/TextInlineMath/5",
          "block_type": "TextInlineMath",
          "html": "<p>&gt;&gt;&gt; a = banana  &gt;&gt;&gt; b = 'banana'  &gt;&gt;&gt; a is b True</p>",
          "polygon": [
            [
              85.763671875,
              235.0
            ],
            [
              171.0791015625,
              235.0
            ],
            [
              171.0791015625,
              288.4921875
            ],
            [
              85.763671875,
              288.4921875
            ]
          ],
          "children": null,
          "section_hierarchy": {
            "1": "/page/108/SectionHeader/1",
            "3": "/page/114/SectionHeader/12"
          },
          "images": {}
        },
        {
          "id": "/page/115/Text/20",
          "block_type": "Text",
          "html": "<p>'</p>",
          "polygon": [
            [
              128.0,
              222.0
            ],
            [
              133.0,
              222.0
            ],
            [
              133.0,
              232.0
            ],
            [
              128.0,
              232.0
            ]
          ],
          "children": null,
          "section_hierarchy": {
            "1": "/page/108/SectionHeader/1",
            "3": "/page/114/SectionHeader/12"
          },
          "images": {}
        },
        {
          "id": "/page/115/Text/21",
          "block_type": "Text",
          "html": "<p>'</p>",
          "polygon": [
            [
              165.0,
              222.0
            ],
            [
              170.0,
              222.0
            ],
            [
              170.0,
              232.0
            ],
            [
              165.0,
              232.0
            ]
          ],
          "children": null,
          "section_hierarchy": {
            "1": "/page/108/SectionHeader/1",
            "3": "/page/114/SectionHeader/12"
          },
          "images": {}
        },
        {
          "id": "/page/115/Text/6",
          "block_type": "Text",
          "html": "<p>In this example, Python only created one string object, and both a and b refer to it.</p>",
          "polygon": [
            [
              85.3154296875,
              287.71875
            ],
            [
              447.0,
              287.71875
            ],
            [
              447.0,
              298.93359375
            ],
            [
              85.3154296875,
              298.93359375
            ]
          ],
          "children": null,
          "section_hierarchy": {
            "1": "/page/108/SectionHeader/1",
            "3": "/page/114/SectionHeader/12"
          },
          "images": {}
        },
        {
          "id": "/page/115/Caption/7",
          "block_type": "Caption",
          "html": "<p>But when you create two lists, you get two objects:</p>",
          "polygon": [
            [
              83.970703125,
              306.861328125
            ],
            [
              309.0,
              306.861328125
            ],
            [
              309.0,
              318.0
            ],
            [
              83.970703125,
              318.0
            ]
          ],
          "children": null,
          "section_hierarchy": {
            "1": "/page/108/SectionHeader/1",
            "3": "/page/114/SectionHeader/12"
          },
          "images": {}
        },
        {
          "id": "/page/115/TextInlineMath/8",
          "block_type": "TextInlineMath",
          "html": "<p>&gt;&gt;&gt; a = [1, 2, 3] &gt;&gt;&gt; b = [1, 2, 3] &gt;&gt;&gt; a is b False</p>",
          "polygon": [
            [
              85.24072265625,
              321.169921875
            ],
            [
              175.0,
              321.169921875
            ],
            [
              175.0,
              370.0
            ],
            [
              85.24072265625,
              370.0
            ]
          ],
          "children": null,
          "section_hierarchy": {
            "1": "/page/108/SectionHeader/1",
            "3": "/page/114/SectionHeader/12"
          },
          "images": {}
        },
        {
          "id": "/page/115/Text/9",
          "block_type": "Text",
          "html": "<p>So the state diagram looks like Figure 10.3.</p>",
          "polygon": [
            [
              84.8671875,
              372.796875
            ],
            [
              274.623046875,
              372.796875
            ],
            [
              274.623046875,
              385.0
            ],
            [
              84.8671875,
              385.0
            ]
          ],
          "children": null,
          "section_hierarchy": {
            "1": "/page/108/SectionHeader/1",
            "3": "/page/114/SectionHeader/12"
          },
          "images": {}
        },
        {
          "id": "/page/115/Text/10",
          "block_type": "Text",
          "html": "<p>In this case we would say that the two lists are <b>equivalent</b>, because they have the same elements, but not <b>identical</b>, because they are not the same object. If two objects are identical, they are also equivalent, but if they are equivalent, they are not necessarily identical.</p>",
          "polygon": [
            [
              85.6142578125,
              392.51953125
            ],
            [
              482.30859375,
              392.51953125
            ],
            [
              482.30859375,
              429.0
            ],
            [
              85.6142578125,
              429.0
            ]
          ],
          "children": null,
          "section_hierarchy": {
            "1": "/page/108/SectionHeader/1",
            "3": "/page/114/SectionHeader/12"
          },
          "images": {}
        },
        {
          "id": "/page/115/Text/11",
          "block_type": "Text",
          "html": "<p>Until now, we have been using \"object\" and \"value\" interchangeably, but it is more precise to say that an object has a value. If you execute [1,2,3], you get a list object whose value is a sequence of integers. If another list has the same elements, we say it has the same value, but it is not the same object.</p>",
          "polygon": [
            [
              85.46484375,
              437.37890625
            ],
            [
              482.90625,
              437.37890625
            ],
            [
              482.90625,
              485.33203125
            ],
            [
              85.46484375,
              485.33203125
            ]
          ],
          "children": null,
          "section_hierarchy": {
            "1": "/page/108/SectionHeader/1",
            "3": "/page/115/SectionHeader/12"
          },
          "images": {}
        },
        {
          "id": "/page/115/SectionHeader/12",
          "block_type": "SectionHeader",
          "html": "<h3><b>10.11 Aliasing</b></h3>",
          "polygon": [
            [
              86.0,
              512.7890625
            ],
            [
              189.6064453125,
              512.7890625
            ],
            [
              189.6064453125,
              528.2578125
            ],
            [
              86.0,
              528.2578125
            ]
          ],
          "children": null,
          "section_hierarchy": {
            "1": "/page/108/SectionHeader/1",
            "3": "/page/115/SectionHeader/12"
          },
          "images": {}
        },
        {
          "id": "/page/115/Text/13",
          "block_type": "Text",
          "html": "<p>If a refers to an object and you assign b = a, then both variables refer to the same object:</p>",
          "polygon": [
            [
              85.46484375,
              538.69921875
            ],
            [
              474.5390625,
              538.69921875
            ],
            [
              474.5390625,
              550.0
            ],
            [
              85.46484375,
              550.0
            ]
          ],
          "children": null,
          "section_hierarchy": {
            "1": "/page/108/SectionHeader/1",
            "3": "/page/115/SectionHeader/12"
          },
          "images": {}
        },
        {
          "id": "/page/115/Code/14",
          "block_type": "Code",
          "html": "<pre>&gt;&gt;&gt; a = [1, 2, 3]\n&gt;&gt;&gt; b = a\n&gt;&gt;&gt; b is a\nTrue</pre>",
          "polygon": [
            [
              85.166015625,
              554.16796875
            ],
            [
              175.0,
              554.16796875
            ],
            [
              175.0,
              605.98828125
            ],
            [
              85.166015625,
              605.98828125
            ]
          ],
          "children": null,
          "section_hierarchy": {
            "1": "/page/108/SectionHeader/1",
            "3": "/page/115/SectionHeader/12"
          },
          "images": {}
        },
        {
          "id": "/page/115/Text/15",
          "block_type": "Text",
          "html": "<p>The state diagram looks like Figure 10.4.</p>",
          "polygon": [
            [
              86.0,
              606.76171875
            ],
            [
              265.060546875,
              606.76171875
            ],
            [
              265.060546875,
              618.36328125
            ],
            [
              86.0,
              618.36328125
            ]
          ],
          "children": null,
          "section_hierarchy": {
            "1": "/page/108/SectionHeader/1",
            "3": "/page/115/SectionHeader/12"
          },
          "images": {}
        },
        {
          "id": "/page/115/Text/16",
          "block_type": "Text",
          "html": "<p>The association of a variable with an object is called a <b>reference</b>. In this example, there are two references to the same object.</p>",
          "polygon": [
            [
              85.3154296875,
              625.7109375
            ],
            [
              484.1015625,
              625.7109375
            ],
            [
              484.1015625,
              650.0
            ],
            [
              85.3154296875,
              650.0
            ]
          ],
          "children": null,
          "section_hierarchy": {
            "1": "/page/108/SectionHeader/1",
            "3": "/page/115/SectionHeader/12"
          },
          "images": {}
        },
        {
          "id": "/page/115/Text/17",
          "block_type": "Text",
          "html": "<p>An object with more than one reference has more than one name, so we say that the object is <b>aliased</b>.</p>",
          "polygon": [
            [
              85.6142578125,
              657.03515625
            ],
            [
              483.50390625,
              657.03515625
            ],
            [
              483.50390625,
              681.0
            ],
            [
              85.6142578125,
              681.0
            ]
          ],
          "children": null,
          "section_hierarchy": {
            "1": "/page/108/SectionHeader/1",
            "3": "/page/115/SectionHeader/12"
          },
          "images": {}
        },
        {
          "id": "/page/115/Text/18",
          "block_type": "Text",
          "html": "<p>If the aliased object is mutable, changes made with one alias affect the other:</p>",
          "polygon": [
            [
              85.763671875,
              689.90625
            ],
            [
              421.0,
              689.90625
            ],
            [
              421.0,
              701.0
            ],
            [
              85.763671875,
              701.0
            ]
          ],
          "children": null,
          "section_hierarchy": {
            "1": "/page/108/SectionHeader/1",
            "3": "/page/115/SectionHeader/12"
          },
          "images": {}
        }
      ],
      "section_hierarchy": {
        "1": "/page/108/SectionHeader/1",
        "3": "/page/115/SectionHeader/12"
      },
      "images": null
    },
    {
