          },
          "images": {}
        },
        {
          "id": "/page/122/SectionHeader/1",
          "block_type": "SectionHeader",
          "html": "<h1><b>Dictionaries</b></h1>",
          "polygon": [
            [
              128.57080078125,
              214.048828125
            ],
            [
              269.0,
              214.048828125
            ],
            [
              269.0,
              241.0
            ],
            [
              128.57080078125,
              241.0
            ]
          ],
          "children": null,
          "section_hierarchy": {
            "1": "/page/122/SectionHeader/1"
          },
          "images": {}
        },
        {
          "id": "/page/122/Text/2",
          "block_type": "Text",
          "html": "<p>A <b>dictionary</b> is like a list, but more general. In a list, the indices have to be integers; in a dictionary they can be (almost) any type.</p>",
          "polygon": [
            [
              128.6455078125,
              286.0
            ],
            [
              526.53515625,
              286.0
            ],
            [
              526.53515625,
              308.021484375
            ],
            [
              128.6455078125,
              308.021484375
            ]
          ],
          "children": null,
          "section_hierarchy": {
            "1": "/page/122/SectionHeader/1"
          },
          "images": {}
        },
        {
          "id": "/page/122/Text/3",
          "block_type": "Text",
          "html": "<p>You can think of a dictionary as a mapping between a set of indices (which are called <b>keys</b>) and a set of values. Each key maps to a value. The association of a key and a value is called a <b>key-value pair</b> or sometimes an <b>item</b>.</p>",
          "polygon": [
            [
              129.392578125,
              316.142578125
            ],
            [
              527.431640625,
              316.142578125
            ],
            [
              527.431640625,
              351.0
            ],
            [
              129.392578125,
              351.0
            ]
          ],
          "children": null,
          "section_hierarchy": {
            "1": "/page/122/SectionHeader/1"
          },
          "images": {}
        },
        {
          "id": "/page/122/Text/4",
          "block_type": "Text",
          "html": "<p>As an example, we'll build a dictionary that maps from English to Spanish words, so the keys and the values are all strings.</p>",
          "polygon": [
            [
              128.49609375,
              359.068359375
            ],
            [
              527.1328125,
              359.068359375
            ],
            [
              527.1328125,
              382.0
            ],
            [
              128.49609375,
              382.0
            ]
          ],
          "children": null,
          "section_hierarchy": {
            "1": "/page/122/SectionHeader/1"
          },
          "images": {}
        },
        {
          "id": "/page/122/Text/5",
          "block_type": "Text",
          "html": "<p>The function dict creates a new dictionary with no items. Because dict is the name of a built-in function, you should avoid using it as a variable name.</p>",
          "polygon": [
            [
              129.09375,
              390.779296875
            ],
            [
              527.1328125,
              390.779296875
            ],
            [
              527.1328125,
              413.0
            ],
            [
              129.09375,
              413.0
            ]
          ],
          "children": null,
          "section_hierarchy": {
            "1": "/page/122/SectionHeader/1"
          },
          "images": {}
        },
        {
          "id": "/page/122/Code/6",
          "block_type": "Code",
          "html": "<pre>&gt;&gt;&gt; eng2sp = dict()\n&gt;&gt;&gt; print eng2sp\n{}</pre>",
          "polygon": [
            [
              129.16845703125,
              418.0
            ],
            [
              229.0,
              418.0
            ],
            [
              229.0,
              453.234375
            ],
            [
              129.16845703125,
              453.234375
            ]
          ],
          "children": null,
          "section_hierarchy": {
            "1": "/page/122/SectionHeader/1"
          },
          "images": {}
        },
        {
          "id": "/page/122/Text/7",
          "block_type": "Text",
          "html": "<p>The squiggly-brackets, {}, represent an empty dictionary. To add items to the dictionary, you can use square brackets: ''''</p>",
          "polygon": [
            [
              128.6455078125,
              455.94140625
            ],
            [
              526.53515625,
              455.94140625
            ],
            [
              526.53515625,
              480.0
            ],
            [
              128.6455078125,
              480.0
            ]
          ],
          "children": null,
