          },
          "images": {}
        },
        {
          "id": "/page/130/SectionHeader/4",
          "block_type": "SectionHeader",
          "html": "<h3><b>11.7 Long integers</b></h3>",
          "polygon": [
            [
              128.197265625,
              233.384765625
            ],
            [
              259.0,
              233.384765625
            ],
            [
              259.0,
              249.240234375
            ],
            [
              128.197265625,
              249.240234375
            ]
          ],
          "children": null,
          "section_hierarchy": {
            "1": "/page/122/SectionHeader/1",
            "3": "/page/130/SectionHeader/4"
          },
          "images": {}
        },
        {
          "id": "/page/130/Text/5",
          "block_type": "Text",
          "html": "<p>If you compute fibonacci(50), you get:</p>",
          "polygon": [
            [
              129.31787109375,
              260.068359375
            ],
            [
              308.0,
              260.068359375
            ],
            [
              308.0,
              272.0
            ],
            [
              129.31787109375,
              272.0
            ]
          ],
          "children": null,
          "section_hierarchy": {
            "1": "/page/122/SectionHeader/1",
            "3": "/page/130/SectionHeader/4"
          },
          "images": {}
        },
        {
          "id": "/page/130/Code/6",
          "block_type": "Code",
          "html": "<pre>&gt;&gt;&gt; fibonacci(50)\n12586269025L</pre>",
          "polygon": [
            [
              128.197265625,
              275.73046875
            ],
            [
              219.0,
              275.73046875
            ],
            [
              219.0,
              300.0
            ],
            [
              128.197265625,
              300.0
            ]
          ],
          "children": null,
          "section_hierarchy": {
            "1": "/page/122/SectionHeader/1",
            "3": "/page/130/SectionHeader/4"
          },
          "images": {}
        },
        {
          "id": "/page/130/Text/7",
          "block_type": "Text",
          "html": "<p>The L at the end indicates that the result is a long integer, or type long. In Python 3, long is gone; all integers, even really big ones, are type int.</p>",
          "polygon": [
            [
              128.794921875,
              306.0
            ],
            [
              527.431640625,
              306.0
            ],
            [
              527.431640625,
              329.0
            ],
            [
              128.794921875,
              329.0
            ]
          ],
          "children": null,
          "section_hierarchy": {
            "1": "/page/122/SectionHeader/1",
            "3": "/page/130/SectionHeader/4"
          },
          "images": {}
        },
        {
          "id": "/page/130/Text/8",
          "block_type": "Text",
          "html": "<p>Values with type int have a limited range; long integers can be arbitrarily big, but as they get bigger they consume more space and time.</p>",
          "polygon": [
            [
              128.794921875,
              337.798828125
            ],
            [
              527.431640625,
              337.798828125
            ],
            [
              527.431640625,
              361.001953125
            ],
            [
              128.794921875,
              361.001953125
            ]
          ],
          "children": null,
          "section_hierarchy": {
            "1": "/page/122/SectionHeader/1",
            "3": "/page/130/SectionHeader/4"
          },
          "images": {}
        },
        {
          "id": "/page/130/Text/9",
          "block_type": "Text",
          "html": "<p>The mathematical operators work on long integers, and the functions in the math module, too, so in general any code that works with int will also work with long.</p>",
          "polygon": [
            [
              128.3466796875,
              370.283203125
            ],
            [
              527.1328125,
              370.283203125
            ],
            [
              527.1328125,
              394.0
            ],
            [
              128.3466796875,
              394.0
            ]
          ],
          "children": null,
          "section_hierarchy": {
            "1": "/page/122/SectionHeader/1",
            "3": "/page/130/SectionHeader/4"
          },
          "images": {}
        },
        {
          "id": "/page/130/Text/10",
          "block_type": "Text",
          "html": "<p>Any time the result of a computation is too big to be represented with an integer, Python converts the result as a long integer:</p>",
          "polygon": [
            [
              128.6455078125,
              402.9609375
            ],
            [
              527.1328125,
              402.9609375
            ],
            [
              527.1328125,
              426.1640625
            ],
            [
              128.6455078125,
              426.1640625
            ]
          ],
          "children": null,
          "section_hierarchy": {
            "1": "/page/122/SectionHeader/1",
            "3": "/page/130/SectionHeader/4"
          },
          "images": {}
        },
        {
          "id": "/page/130/Code/11",
          "block_type": "Code",
          "html": "<pre>&gt;&gt;&gt; 1000 * 1000\n1000000\n&gt;&gt;&gt; 100000 * 100000\n10000000000L</pre>",
          "polygon": [
            [
              128.6455078125,
              430.8046875
            ],
            [
              229.0,
              430.8046875
            ],
            [
              229.0,
              479.0
            ],
            [
              128.6455078125,
              479.0
            ]
          ],
          "children": null,
          "section_hierarchy": {
            "1": "/page/122/SectionHeader/1",
            "3": "/page/130/SectionHeader/4"
          },
          "images": {}
        },
        {
          "id": "/page/130/Text/12",
          "block_type": "Text",
          "html": "<p>In the first case the result has type int; in the second case it is long. <b>Exercise 11.8.</b> <i>Exponentiation of large integers is the basis of common algorithms for public-key en</i><i>cryption. Read the Wikipedia page on the RSA algorithm (</i>http: // en. wikipedia. org/ wiki/ RSA_ ( algorithm) <i>) and write functions to encode and decode messages.</i></p>",
          "polygon": [
            [
              128.0478515625,
              485.0
            ],
            [
              526.0,
              485.0
            ],
            [
              526.0,
              532.0
            ],
            [
              128.0478515625,
              532.0
            ]
          ],
          "children": null,
          "section_hierarchy": {
            "1": "/page/122/SectionHeader/1",
            "3": "/page/130/SectionHeader/13"
          },
          "images": {}
        },
        {
          "id": "/page/130/SectionHeader/13",
          "block_type": "SectionHeader",
          "html": "<h3><b>11.8 Debugging</b></h3>",
          "polygon": [
            [
              128.9443359375,
              559.58203125
            ],
            [
              244.2919921875,
              559.58203125
            ],
            [
              244.2919921875,
              576.0
            ],
            [
              128.9443359375,
              576.0
            ]
          ],
          "children": null,
          "section_hierarchy": {
            "1": "/page/122/SectionHeader/1",
            "3": "/page/130/SectionHeader/13"
          },
          "images": {}
        },
        {
          "id": "/page/130/Text/14",
          "block_type": "Text",
          "html": "<p>As you work with bigger datasets it can become unwieldy to debug by printing and checking data by hand. Here are some suggestions for debugging large datasets:</p>",
          "polygon": [
            [
              128.197265625,
              587.8125
            ],
            [
              526.0,
              587.8125
            ],
            [
              526.0,
              611.015625
            ],
            [
              128.197265625,
              611.015625
            ]
          ],
          "children": null,
          "section_hierarchy": {
            "1": "/page/122/SectionHeader/1",
            "3": "/page/130/SectionHeader/13"
          },
          "images": {}
        },
        {
          "id": "/page/130/ListItem/15",
          "block_type": "ListItem",
          "html": "<li><b>Scale down the input:</b> If possible, reduce the size of the dataset. For example if the program reads a text file, start with just the first 10 lines, or with the smallest example you can find. You can either edit the files themselves, or (better) modify the program so it reads only the first n lines.</li>",
          "polygon": [
            [
              129.5419921875,
              624.1640625
            ],
            [
              526.0,
              624.1640625
            ],
            [
              526.0,
              672.1171875
            ],
            [
              129.5419921875,
              672.1171875
            ]
          ],
          "children": null,
          "section_hierarchy": {
            "1": "/page/122/SectionHeader/1",
            "3": "/page/130/SectionHeader/13"
          },
          "images": {}
        },
        {
          "id": "/page/130/Text/16",
          "block_type": "Text",
          "html": "<p>If there is an error, you can reduce n to the smallest value that manifests the error, and then increase it gradually as you find and correct errors.</p>",
          "polygon": [
            [
              153.896484375,
              677.91796875
            ],
            [
              526.236328125,
              677.91796875
            ],
            [
              526.236328125,
              701.12109375
            ],
            [
              153.896484375,
              701.12109375
            ]
          ],
          "children": null,
          "section_hierarchy": {
            "1": "/page/122/SectionHeader/1",
            "3": "/page/130/SectionHeader/13"
          },
          "images": {}
        }
      ],
      "section_hierarchy": {
        "1": "/page/122/SectionHeader/1",
        "3": "/page/130/SectionHeader/13"
      },
      "images": null
    },
    {
      "id": "/page/131/Page/175",
      "block_type": "Page",
      "html": "<content-ref src='/page/131/PageHeader/0'></content-ref><content-ref src='/page/131/PageHeader/23'></content-ref><content-ref src='/page/131/ListItem/1'></content-ref><content-ref src='/page/131/Text/2'></content-ref><content-ref src='/page/131/ListItem/3'></content-ref><content-ref src='/page/131/Text/4'></content-ref><content-ref src='/page/131/ListItem/5'></content-ref><content-ref src='/page/131/Text/6'></content-ref><content-ref src='/page/131/SectionHeader/7'></content-ref><content-ref src='/page/131/Text/8'></content-ref><content-ref src='/page/131/ListGroup/175'></content-ref><content-ref src='/page/131/Text/22'></content-ref>",
      "polygon": [
        [
          0.0,
          0.0
        ],
        [
