        },
        {
          "id": "/page/134/Text/3",
          "block_type": "Text",
          "html": "<p>A tuple is a sequence of values. The values can be any type, and they are indexed by integers, so in that respect tuples are a lot like lists. The important difference is that tuples are immutable.</p>",
