          "id": "/page/135/Text/11",
          "block_type": "Text",
          "html": "<p>This solution is cumbersome; <b>tuple assignment</b> is more elegant:</p>",
          "polygon": [
            [
              85.83837890625,
              416.49609375
            ],
            [
              368.15625,
              416.49609375
            ],
            [
              368.15625,
              428.09765625
            ],
            [
              85.83837890625,
              428.09765625
            ]
          ],
          "children": null,
          "section_hierarchy": {
            "1": "/page/134/SectionHeader/1",
            "3": "/page/135/SectionHeader/8"
          },
          "images": {}
        },
        {
          "id": "/page/135/Code/12",
          "block_type": "Code",
          "html": "<pre>&gt;&gt;&gt; a, b = b, a</pre>",
          "polygon": [
            [
              85.3154296875,
              434.671875
            ],
            [
              165.7001953125,
              434.671875
            ],
            [
              165.7001953125,
              446.2734375
            ],
            [
              85.3154296875,
              446.2734375
            ]
          ],
          "children": null,
          "section_hierarchy": {
            "1": "/page/134/SectionHeader/1",
            "3": "/page/135/SectionHeader/8"
          },
          "images": {}
        },
        {
          "id": "/page/135/Text/13",
          "block_type": "Text",
          "html": "<p>The left side is a tuple of variables; the right side is a tuple of expressions. Each value is assigned to its respective variable. All the expressions on the right side are evaluated before any of the assignments.</p>",
          "polygon": [
            [
              85.3154296875,
              451.6875
            ],
            [
              483.50390625,
              451.6875
            ],
            [
              483.50390625,
              488.0390625
            ],
            [
              85.3154296875,
              488.0390625
            ]
          ],
          "children": null,
          "section_hierarchy": {
            "1": "/page/134/SectionHeader/1",
            "3": "/page/135/SectionHeader/8"
          },
          "images": {}
        },
        {
          "id": "/page/135/Text/14",
          "block_type": "Text",
          "html": "<p>The number of variables on the left and the number of values on the right have to be the same:</p>",
          "polygon": [
            [
              85.6142578125,
              498.48046875
            ],
            [
              483.50390625,
              498.48046875
            ],
            [
              483.50390625,
              523.0
            ],
            [
              85.6142578125,
              523.0
            ]
          ],
          "children": null,
          "section_hierarchy": {
            "1": "/page/134/SectionHeader/1",
            "3": "/page/135/SectionHeader/8"
          },
          "images": {}
        },
        {
          "id": "/page/135/Code/15",
          "block_type": "Code",
          "html": "<pre>&gt;&gt;&gt; a, b = 1, 2, 3\nValueError: too many values to unpack</pre>",
          "polygon": [
            [
              85.39013671875,
              529.8046875
            ],
            [
              280.599609375,
              529.8046875
            ],
            [
              280.0,
              553.0
            ],
            [
              84.19482421875,
              553.0
            ]
          ],
          "children": null,
          "section_hierarchy": {
            "1": "/page/134/SectionHeader/1",
            "3": "/page/135/SectionHeader/8"
          },
          "images": {}
        },
        {
          "id": "/page/135/Text/16",
          "block_type": "Text",
          "html": "<p>More generally, the right side can be any kind of sequence (string, list or tuple). For example, to split an email address into a user name and a domain, you could write: ''</p>",
          "polygon": [
            [
              85.3154296875,
              559.1953125
            ],
            [
              482.30859375,
              559.1953125
            ],
            [
              482.30859375,
              588.0
            ],
            [
              85.3154296875,
              588.0
            ]
          ],
          "children": null,
          "section_hierarchy": {
            "1": "/page/134/SectionHeader/1",
            "3": "/page/135/SectionHeader/8"
          },
          "images": {}
        },
        {
          "id": "/page/135/Code/17",
          "block_type": "Code",
          "html": "<pre>&gt;&gt;&gt; addr = monty@python.org\n                              \n&gt;&gt;&gt; uname, domain = addr.split('@')</pre>",
          "polygon": [
            [
              84.4189453125,
              590.0
            ],
            [
              269.9912109375,
              590.0
            ],
            [
              269.9912109375,
              613.0
            ],
            [
              84.4189453125,
              613.0
            ]
          ],
          "children": null,
          "section_hierarchy": {
            "1": "/page/134/SectionHeader/1",
            "3": "/page/135/SectionHeader/8"
          },
          "images": {}
        },
        {
          "id": "/page/135/Text/18",
          "block_type": "Text",
          "html": "<p>The return value from split is a list with two elements; the first element is assigned to uname, the second to domain.</p>",
          "polygon": [
