            "3": "/page/146/SectionHeader/1"
          },
          "images": {}
        },
        {
          "id": "/page/146/Text/7",
          "block_type": "Text",
          "html": "<p>process_file loops through the lines of the file, passing them one at a time to process_line. The histogram hist is being used as an accumulator.</p>",
          "polygon": [
            [
              128.197265625,
              427.7109375
            ],
            [
              526.236328125,
              427.7109375
            ],
            [
              526.236328125,
              451.0
            ],
            [
              128.197265625,
              451.0
            ]
          ],
          "children": null,
          "section_hierarchy": {
            "1": "/page/144/SectionHeader/1",
            "3": "/page/146/SectionHeader/1"
          },
          "images": {}
        },
        {
          "id": "/page/146/Text/8",
          "block_type": "Text",
          "html": "<p>process_line uses the string method replace to replace hyphens with spaces before using split to break the line into a list of strings. It traverses the list of words and uses strip and lower to remove punctuation and convert to lower case. (It is a shorthand to say that strings are \"converted;\" remember that string are immutable, so methods like strip and lower return new strings.)</p>",
          "polygon": [
            [
              128.794921875,
              460.96875
            ],
