          ],
          "children": null,
          "section_hierarchy": {
            "1": "/page/154/SectionHeader/1",
            "3": "/page/160/SectionHeader/10"
          },
          "images": {}
        },
        {
          "id": "/page/161/Text/1",
          "block_type": "Text",
          "html": "<p>If you run this program, it reads itself and prints the number of lines in the file, which is 7. You can also import it like this:</p>",
          "polygon": [
            [
              85.166015625,
              88.41357421875
            ],
            [
              482.30859375,
              86.86669921875
            ],
            [
              482.30859375,
              111.0
            ],
            [
              85.166015625,
              111.0
            ]
          ],
          "children": null,
          "section_hierarchy": {
            "1": "/page/154/SectionHeader/1",
            "3": "/page/160/SectionHeader/10"
          },
          "images": {}
        },
        {
          "id": "/page/161/Code/2",
          "block_type": "Code",
          "html": "<pre>&gt;&gt;&gt; import wc\n7\nNow you have a module object wc:\n&gt;&gt;&gt; print wc\n&lt;module 'wc' from 'wc.py'&gt;\nThat provides a function called linecount:\n&gt;&gt;&gt; wc.linecount('wc.py')\n7</pre>",
          "polygon": [
            [
              86.0,
              118.0
            ],
            [
              276.416015625,
              118.0
            ],
            [
              276.416015625,
              234.0
            ],
            [
              86.0,
              234.0
            ]
          ],
          "children": null,
          "section_hierarchy": {
            "1": "/page/154/SectionHeader/1",
            "3": "/page/160/SectionHeader/10"
          },
          "images": {}
        },
        {
          "id": "/page/161/Text/3",
          "block_type": "Text",
          "html": "<p>So that's how you write modules in Python.</p>",
          "polygon": [
            [
              86.0,
              239.765625
            ],
            [
              280.001953125,
              239.765625
            ],
            [
              280.001953125,
              251.0
            ],
            [
              86.0,
              251.0
            ]
          ],
          "children": null,
          "section_hierarchy": {
            "1": "/page/154/SectionHeader/1",
            "3": "/page/160/SectionHeader/10"
          },
          "images": {}
        },
        {
          "id": "/page/161/Text/4",
          "block_type": "Text",
          "html": "<p>The only problem with this example is that when you import the module it executes the test code at the bottom. Normally when you import a module, it defines new functions but it doesn't execute them.</p>",
          "polygon": [
            [
              85.9130859375,
              261.421875
            ],
            [
              482.30859375,
              261.421875
            ],
            [
              482.30859375,
              297.0
            ],
            [
              85.9130859375,
              297.0
            ]
          ],
          "children": null,
          "section_hierarchy": {
            "1": "/page/154/SectionHeader/1",
            "3": "/page/160/SectionHeader/10"
          },
          "images": {}
        },
        {
          "id": "/page/161/Text/5",
          "block_type": "Text",
          "html": "<p>Programs that will be imported as modules often use the following idiom: ''</p>",
          "polygon": [
            [
              85.763671875,
              307.634765625
            ],
            [
              414.474609375,
              307.634765625
            ],
            [
              414.474609375,
              322.0
            ],
            [
              85.763671875,
              322.0
            ]
          ],
          "children": null,
          "section_hierarchy": {
            "1": "/page/154/SectionHeader/1",
            "3": "/page/160/SectionHeader/10"
          },
          "images": {}
        },
        {
          "id": "/page/161/TextInlineMath/6",
          "block_type": "TextInlineMath",
          "html": "<p>if __name__ == __main__: print linecount('wc.py')</p>",
          "polygon": [
            [
              86.0,
              324.0
            ],
            [
              233.0,
              323.103515625
            ],
            [
              233.0,
              347.0
            ],
            [
              86.0,
              347.0
            ]
          ],
          "children": null,
          "section_hierarchy": {
            "1": "/page/154/SectionHeader/1",
            "3": "/page/160/SectionHeader/10"
          },
          "images": {}
        },
        {
          "id": "/page/161/Text/7",
          "block_type": "Text",
          "html": "<p>__name__ is a built-in variable that is set when the program starts. If the program is running as a script, __name__ has the value __main__; in that case, the test code is executed. Otherwise, if the module is being imported, the test code is skipped.</p>",
          "polygon": [
            [
              85.763671875,
              353.07421875
            ],
            [
              482.90625,
              353.07421875
            ],
            [
              482.90625,
              390.5859375
            ],
            [
              85.763671875,
              390.5859375
            ]
          ],
          "children": null,
          "section_hierarchy": {
            "1": "/page/154/SectionHeader/1",
            "3": "/page/160/SectionHeader/10"
          },
          "images": {}
        },
        {
          "id": "/page/161/Text/8",
          "block_type": "Text",
          "html": "<p><b>Exercise 14.5.</b> <i>Type this example into a file named</i> wc.py <i>and run it as a script. Then run the</i> <i>Python interpreter and</i> import wc<i>. What is the value of</i> __name__ <i>when the module is being</i> <i>imported?</i></p>",
          "polygon": [
            [
              85.763671875,
              391.0
            ],
            [
              483.50390625,
              391.0
            ],
            [
              483.50390625,
              426.0
            ],
            [
              85.763671875,
              426.0
            ]
          ],
          "children": null,
          "section_hierarchy": {
            "1": "/page/154/SectionHeader/1",
            "3": "/page/160/SectionHeader/10"
          },
          "images": {}
        },
        {
          "id": "/page/161/Text/9",
          "block_type": "Text",
          "html": "<p><i>Warning: If you import a module that has already been imported, Python does nothing. It does not</i> <i>re-read the file, even if it has changed.</i></p>",
          "polygon": [
            [
              85.3154296875,
              435.83203125
            ],
            [
              482.30859375,
              435.83203125
            ],
            [
              482.30859375,
              459.03515625
            ],
            [
              85.3154296875,
              459.03515625
            ]
          ],
          "children": null,
          "section_hierarchy": {
            "1": "/page/154/SectionHeader/1",
            "3": "/page/160/SectionHeader/10"
          },
          "images": {}
        },
        {
          "id": "/page/161/Text/10",
          "block_type": "Text",
          "html": "<p><i>If you want to reload a module, you can use the built-in function</i> reload<i>, but it can be tricky, so</i> <i>the safest thing to do is restart the interpreter and then import the module again.</i></p>",
          "polygon": [
            [
              85.3154296875,
              470.0
            ],
            [
              483.50390625,
              470.0
            ],
            [
              483.50390625,
              493.0
            ],
            [
              85.3154296875,
              493.0
            ]
          ],
          "children": null,
          "section_hierarchy": {
            "1": "/page/154/SectionHeader/1",
            "3": "/page/161/SectionHeader/11"
          },
          "images": {}
        },
        {
          "id": "/page/161/SectionHeader/11",
          "block_type": "SectionHeader",
          "html": "<h3><b>14.10 Debugging</b></h3>",
          "polygon": [
            [
              85.83837890625,
              523.6171875
            ],
            [
              207.38671875,
              523.6171875
            ],
            [
              207.38671875,
              540.0
            ],
            [
              85.83837890625,
              540.0
            ]
          ],
          "children": null,
          "section_hierarchy": {
            "1": "/page/154/SectionHeader/1",
            "3": "/page/161/SectionHeader/11"
          },
          "images": {}
        },
        {
          "id": "/page/161/Text/12",
          "block_type": "Text",
          "html": "<p>When you are reading and writing files, you might run into problems with whitespace. These errors can be hard to debug because spaces, tabs and newlines are normally invisible: ''</p>",
          "polygon": [
            [
              85.9130859375,
              553.39453125
            ],
            [
              482.90625,
              553.39453125
            ],
            [
              482.90625,
              580.0
            ],
            [
              85.9130859375,
              580.0
            ]
          ],
          "children": null,
          "section_hierarchy": {
            "1": "/page/154/SectionHeader/1",
            "3": "/page/161/SectionHeader/11"
          },
          "images": {}
        },
        {
          "id": "/page/161/Code/13",
          "block_type": "Code",
          "html": "<pre>&gt;&gt;&gt; s = 1 2\\t 3\\n 4\n                       \n&gt;&gt;&gt; print s\n1 2 3\n 4</pre>",
          "polygon": [
            [
              86.0,
              581.625
            ],
            [
              197.82421875,
              581.625
            ],
            [
              197.82421875,
              631.125
            ],
            [
              86.0,
              631.125
            ]
          ],
          "children": null,
          "section_hierarchy": {
            "1": "/page/154/SectionHeader/1",
            "3": "/page/161/SectionHeader/11"
          },
          "images": {}
        },
        {
          "id": "/page/161/Text/14",
          "block_type": "Text",
          "html": "<p>The built-in function repr can help. It takes any object as an argument and returns a string representation of the object. For strings, it represents whitespace characters with backslash sequences:</p>",
          "polygon": [
            [
              86.0,
              636.15234375
            ],
            [
              483.50390625,
              636.15234375
            ],
            [
              483.50390625,
              671.0
            ],
            [
              86.0,
              671.0
            ]
          ],
          "children": null,
          "section_hierarchy": {
            "1": "/page/154/SectionHeader/1",
            "3": "/page/161/SectionHeader/11"
          },
          "images": {}
        },
        {
          "id": "/page/161/Code/15",
          "block_type": "Code",
          "html": "<pre>&gt;&gt;&gt; print repr(s)\n'1 2\\t 3\\n 4'</pre>",
          "polygon": [
            [
              86.0,
              674.82421875
            ],
            [
              177.0556640625,
              674.82421875
            ],
            [
              175.8603515625,
