          "id": "/page/164/Text/5",
          "block_type": "Text",
          "html": "<p>In mathematical notation, points are often written in parentheses with a comma separating the coordinates. For example, (0, 0) represents the origin, and (x, y) represents the point x units to the right and y units up from the origin.</p>",
          "polygon": [
            [
              128.6455078125,
              422.68359375
            ],
            [
              528.328125,
              422.68359375
            ],
            [
              528.328125,
              459.03515625
            ],
            [
              128.6455078125,
              459.03515625
            ]
          ],
          "children": null,
          "section_hierarchy": {
            "1": "/page/164/SectionHeader/1",
            "3": "/page/164/SectionHeader/3"
          },
          "images": {}
        },
        {
          "id": "/page/164/Text/6",
          "block_type": "Text",
          "html": "<p>There are several ways we might represent points in Python:</p>",
          "polygon": [
            [
              128.794921875,
              466.76953125
            ],
            [
              396.544921875,
              466.76953125
            ],
            [
              396.544921875,
              478.0
            ],
            [
              128.794921875,
              478.0
            ]
          ],
          "children": null,
          "section_hierarchy": {
            "1": "/page/164/SectionHeader/1",
            "3": "/page/164/SectionHeader/3"
          },
          "images": {}
        },
        {
          "id": "/page/164/ListGroup/143",
          "block_type": "ListGroup",
          "html": "<p><ul><content-ref src='/page/164/ListItem/7'></content-ref><content-ref src='/page/164/ListItem/8'></content-ref><content-ref src='/page/164/ListItem/9'></content-ref></ul></p>",
          "polygon": [
            [
              143.0,
              488.8125
            ],
            [
              450.6328125,
              488.8125
            ],
            [
              450.6328125,
              540.0
            ],
            [
              143.0,
              540.0
            ]
          ],
          "children": [
            {
              "id": "/page/164/ListItem/7",
              "block_type": "ListItem",
              "html": "<li> We could store the coordinates separately in two variables, x and y.</li>",
              "polygon": [
                [
                  143.0,
                  488.8125
                ],
                [
                  450.6328125,
                  488.8125
                ],
                [
                  450.6328125,
                  500.0
                ],
                [
                  143.0,
                  500.0
                ]
              ],
              "children": null,
              "section_hierarchy": {
                "1": "/page/164/SectionHeader/1",
                "3": "/page/164/SectionHeader/3"
              },
              "images": {}
            },
            {
              "id": "/page/164/ListItem/8",
              "block_type": "ListItem",
              "html": "<li> We could store the coordinates as elements in a list or tuple.</li>",
              "polygon": [
                [
                  143.0,
                  508.921875
                ],
                [
                  418.359375,
                  508.921875
                ],
                [
                  418.359375,
                  520.0
                ],
                [
                  143.0,
                  520.0
                ]
              ],
              "children": null,
              "section_hierarchy": {
                "1": "/page/164/SectionHeader/1",
                "3": "/page/164/SectionHeader/3"
              },
              "images": {}
            },
            {
              "id": "/page/164/ListItem/9",
              "block_type": "ListItem",
              "html": "<li> We could create a new type to represent points as objects.</li>",
              "polygon": [
                [
                  143.0,
                  527.87109375
                ],
                [
                  408.19921875,
                  527.87109375
                ],
                [
                  408.19921875,
                  540.0
                ],
                [
                  143.0,
                  540.0
                ]
              ],
              "children": null,
              "section_hierarchy": {
                "1": "/page/164/SectionHeader/1",
                "3": "/page/164/SectionHeader/3"
              },
              "images": {}
            }
          ],
          "section_hierarchy": {
            "1": "/page/164/SectionHeader/1",
            "3": "/page/164/SectionHeader/3"
          },
          "images": null
        },
        {
          "id": "/page/164/Text/10",
          "block_type": "Text",
          "html": "<p>Creating a new type is (a little) more complicated than the other options, but it has advantages that will be apparent soon.</p>",
          "polygon": [
            [
              128.794921875,
              550.30078125
            ],
            [
              526.833984375,
              550.30078125
            ],
            [
              526.833984375,
              574.27734375
            ],
            [
              128.794921875,
              574.27734375
            ]
          ],
          "children": null,
          "section_hierarchy": {
            "1": "/page/164/SectionHeader/1",
            "3": "/page/164/SectionHeader/3"
          },
          "images": {}
        },
        {
          "id": "/page/164/Text/11",
          "block_type": "Text",
          "html": "<p>A user-defined type is also called a <b>class</b>. A class definition looks like this:</p>",
          "polygon": [
            [
              127.7490234375,
              582.01171875
            ],
            [
              456.609375,
              582.01171875
            ],
            [
              456.609375,
              594.0
            ],
            [
              127.7490234375,
              594.0
            ]
          ],
          "children": null,
          "section_hierarchy": {
            "1": "/page/164/SectionHeader/1",
            "3": "/page/164/SectionHeader/3"
          },
          "images": {}
        },
        {
          "id": "/page/164/Code/12",
          "block_type": "Code",
          "html": "<pre>class Point(object):\n    \"\"\"Represents a point in 2-D space.\"\"\"</pre>",
          "polygon": [
            [
              129.8408203125,
              597.8671875
            ],
            [
              350.82421875,
              597.8671875
            ],
            [
              350.82421875,
              622.0
            ],
            [
              129.8408203125,
              622.0
            ]
          ],
          "children": null,
          "section_hierarchy": {
            "1": "/page/164/SectionHeader/1",
            "3": "/page/164/SectionHeader/3"
          },
          "images": {}
        },
        {
          "id": "/page/164/Text/13",
          "block_type": "Text",
          "html": "<p>This header indicates that the new class is a Point, which is a kind of object, which is a built-in type.</p>",
          "polygon": [
            [
              128.3466796875,
              625.7109375
            ],
            [
              527.1328125,
              625.7109375
            ],
            [
              527.1328125,
              650.0
            ],
            [
              128.3466796875,
              650.0
            ]
          ],
          "children": null,
          "section_hierarchy": {
            "1": "/page/164/SectionHeader/1",
            "3": "/page/164/SectionHeader/3"
          },
          "images": {}
        },
        {
          "id": "/page/164/Text/14",
          "block_type": "Text",
          "html": "<p>The body is a docstring that explains what the class is for. You can define variables and functions inside a class definition, but we will get back to that later.</p>",
          "polygon": [
            [
              128.49609375,
              657.421875
            ],
            [
              527.1328125,
              657.421875
            ],
            [
              527.1328125,
              681.0
            ],
            [
              128.49609375,
              681.0
            ]
          ],
          "children": null,
          "section_hierarchy": {
            "1": "/page/164/SectionHeader/1",
            "3": "/page/164/SectionHeader/3"
          },
          "images": {}
        },
        {
          "id": "/page/164/Text/15",
          "block_type": "Text",
          "html": "<p>Defining a class named Point creates a class object.</p>",
          "polygon": [
            [
              128.57080078125,
              690.6796875
            ],
            [
              355.0078125,
              690.6796875
            ],
            [
              355.0078125,
              701.0
            ],
            [
              128.57080078125,
              701.0
            ]
          ],
          "children": null,
          "section_hierarchy": {
            "1": "/page/164/SectionHeader/1",
            "3": "/page/164/SectionHeader/3"
          },
          "images": {}
        }
      ],
      "section_hierarchy": {
        "1": "/page/164/SectionHeader/1",
        "3": "/page/164/SectionHeader/3"
      },
      "images": null
    },
    {
      "id": "/page/165/Page/219",
      "block_type": "Page",
      "html": "<content-ref src='/page/165/PageHeader/0'></content-ref><content-ref src='/page/165/FigureGroup/219'></content-ref><content-ref src='/page/165/TextInlineMath/3'></content-ref><content-ref src='/page/165/Text/4'></content-ref><content-ref src='/page/165/Text/5'></content-ref><content-ref src='/page/165/Code/6'></content-ref><content-ref src='/page/165/Text/7'></content-ref><content-ref src='/page/165/Text/8'></content-ref><content-ref src='/page/165/SectionHeader/9'></content-ref><content-ref src='/page/165/Text/10'></content-ref><content-ref src='/page/165/Code/11'></content-ref><content-ref src='/page/165/Text/12'></content-ref><content-ref src='/page/165/Text/13'></content-ref><content-ref src='/page/165/Text/14'></content-ref><content-ref src='/page/165/Text/15'></content-ref><content-ref src='/page/165/Text/16'></content-ref><content-ref src='/page/165/Code/17'></content-ref><content-ref src='/page/165/Text/18'></content-ref><content-ref src='/page/165/Text/19'></content-ref><content-ref src='/page/165/Text/20'></content-ref>",
      "polygon": [
