              }
            },
            {
              "id": "/page/165/Caption/2",
              "block_type": "Caption",
              "html": "<p>Figure 15.1: Object diagram.</p>",
              "polygon": [
                [
                  219.4892578125,
                  143.9560546875
                ],
                [
                  347.0,
                  143.9560546875
                ],
                [
                  347.0,
                  155.0
                ],
                [
                  219.4892578125,
                  155.0
                ]
              ],
              "children": null,
              "section_hierarchy": {
                "1": "/page/164/SectionHeader/1",
                "3": "/page/164/SectionHeader/3"
              },
              "images": {}
            }
          ],
          "section_hierarchy": {
            "1": "/page/164/SectionHeader/1",
            "3": "/page/164/SectionHeader/3"
          },
          "images": null
        },
        {
          "id": "/page/165/TextInlineMath/3",
          "block_type": "TextInlineMath",
          "html": "<p>&gt;&gt;&gt; print Point &lt;class '__main__.Point'&gt;</p>",
          "polygon": [
            [
              86.0,
              174.0
            ],
            [
              216.052734375,
              174.0
            ],
            [
              216.052734375,
              200.3203125
            ],
            [
              86.0,
              200.3203125
            ]
          ],
          "children": null,
          "section_hierarchy": {
            "1": "/page/164/SectionHeader/1",
            "3": "/page/164/SectionHeader/3"
          },
          "images": {}
        },
        {
          "id": "/page/165/Text/4",
          "block_type": "Text",
          "html": "<p>Because Point is defined at the top level, its \"full name\" is __main__.Point.</p>",
          "polygon": [
            [
              85.46484375,
              201.8671875
            ],
            [
              421.0,
              201.8671875
            ],
            [
              421.0,
              212.30859375
            ],
            [
              85.46484375,
              212.30859375
            ]
          ],
          "children": null,
          "section_hierarchy": {
            "1": "/page/164/SectionHeader/1",
            "3": "/page/164/SectionHeader/3"
          },
          "images": {}
        },
        {
          "id": "/page/165/Text/5",
          "block_type": "Text",
          "html": "<p>The class object is like a factory for creating objects. To create a Point, you call Point as if it were a function.</p>",
          "polygon": [
            [
              85.6142578125,
              220.0
            ],
            [
              482.30859375,
              220.0
            ],
            [
              482.30859375,
              243.0
            ],
            [
              85.6142578125,
              243.0
            ]
          ],
          "children": null,
          "section_hierarchy": {
            "1": "/page/164/SectionHeader/1",
            "3": "/page/164/SectionHeader/3"
          },
          "images": {}
        },
        {
          "id": "/page/165/Code/6",
          "block_type": "Code",
          "html": "<pre>&gt;&gt;&gt; blank = Point()\n&gt;&gt;&gt; print blank\n&lt;__main__.Point instance at 0xb7e9d3ac&gt;</pre>",
          "polygon": [
            [
              85.3154296875,
              246.919921875
            ],
            [
              290.0,
              246.919921875
            ],
            [
              290.0,
              282.0
            ],
            [
              85.3154296875,
              282.0
            ]
          ],
          "children": null,
          "section_hierarchy": {
            "1": "/page/164/SectionHeader/1",
            "3": "/page/164/SectionHeader/3"
          },
          "images": {}
        },
        {
          "id": "/page/165/Text/7",
          "block_type": "Text",
          "html": "<p>The return value is a reference to a Point object, which we assign to blank. Creating a new object is called <b>instantiation</b>, and the object is an <b>instance</b> of the class.</p>",
          "polygon": [
            [
              86.0,
              282.69140625
            ],
            [
              482.30859375,
              282.69140625
            ],
            [
              482.30859375,
              309.0
            ],
            [
              86.0,
              309.0
            ]
          ],
          "children": null,
          "section_hierarchy": {
            "1": "/page/164/SectionHeader/1",
            "3": "/page/164/SectionHeader/3"
          },
          "images": {}
        },
        {
          "id": "/page/165/Text/8",
          "block_type": "Text",
          "html": "<p>When you print an instance, Python tells you what class it belongs to and where it is stored in memory (the prefix 0x means that the following number is in hexadecimal).</p>",
          "polygon": [
            [
              85.763671875,
              316.529296875
            ],
            [
              483.205078125,
              316.529296875
            ],
            [
              483.205078125,
              340.0
            ],
            [
              85.763671875,
              340.0
            ]
          ],
          "children": null,
          "section_hierarchy": {
            "1": "/page/164/SectionHeader/1",
            "3": "/page/165/SectionHeader/9"
          },
          "images": {}
        },
        {
          "id": "/page/165/SectionHeader/9",
          "block_type": "SectionHeader",
          "html": "<h3><b>15.2 Attributes</b></h3>",
          "polygon": [
            [
              85.9130859375,
              365.0625
            ],
            [
              193.0,
              365.0625
            ],
            [
              193.0,
              381.0
            ],
            [
              85.9130859375,
              381.0
            ]
          ],
          "children": null,
          "section_hierarchy": {
            "1": "/page/164/SectionHeader/1",
            "3": "/page/165/SectionHeader/9"
          },
          "images": {}
        },
        {
          "id": "/page/165/Text/10",
          "block_type": "Text",
          "html": "<p>You can assign values to an instance using dot notation:</p>",
          "polygon": [
            [
              86.0,
              390.392578125
            ],
            [
              332.296875,
              390.392578125
            ],
            [
              332.296875,
              402.0
            ],
            [
              86.0,
              402.0
            ]
          ],
          "children": null,
          "section_hierarchy": {
            "1": "/page/164/SectionHeader/1",
            "3": "/page/165/SectionHeader/9"
          },
          "images": {}
        },
        {
          "id": "/page/165/Code/11",
          "block_type": "Code",
          "html": "<pre>&gt;&gt;&gt; blank.x = 3.0\n&gt;&gt;&gt; blank.y = 4.0</pre>",
          "polygon": [
            [
              85.68896484375,
              405.28125
            ],
            [
              175.0,
              405.28125
            ],
            [
              175.0,
              430.8046875
            ],
            [
              85.68896484375,
              430.8046875
            ]
          ],
          "children": null,
          "section_hierarchy": {
            "1": "/page/164/SectionHeader/1",
            "3": "/page/165/SectionHeader/9"
          },
          "images": {}
        },
        {
          "id": "/page/165/Text/12",
          "block_type": "Text",
          "html": "<p>This syntax is similar to the syntax for selecting a variable from a module, such as math.pi or string.whitespace. In this case, though, we are assigning values to named elements of an object. These elements are called <b>attributes</b>.</p>",
          "polygon": [
            [
              85.3154296875,
              433.125
            ],
            [
              483.50390625,
              433.125
            ],
            [
              483.50390625,
              468.703125
            ],
            [
              85.3154296875,
              468.703125
            ]
          ],
          "children": null,
          "section_hierarchy": {
            "1": "/page/164/SectionHeader/1",
            "3": "/page/165/SectionHeader/9"
          },
          "images": {}
        },
        {
          "id": "/page/165/Text/13",
          "block_type": "Text",
          "html": "<p>As a noun, \"AT-trib-ute\" is pronounced with emphasis on the first syllable, as opposed to \"a-TRIB-ute,\" which is a verb.</p>",
          "polygon": [
            [
              85.763671875,
              474.890625
            ],
            [
              482.90625,
              474.890625
            ],
            [
              482.90625,
              499.0
            ],
            [
              85.763671875,
              499.0
            ]
          ],
          "children": null,
          "section_hierarchy": {
            "1": "/page/164/SectionHeader/1",
            "3": "/page/165/SectionHeader/9"
          },
          "images": {}
        },
        {
          "id": "/page/165/Text/14",
          "block_type": "Text",
          "html": "<p>The following diagram shows the result of these assignments. A state diagram that shows an object and its attributes is called an <b>object diagram</b>; see Figure 15.1.</p>",
          "polygon": [
            [
              85.763671875,
              506.98828125
            ],
            [
              483.802734375,
              506.98828125
            ],
            [
              483.802734375,
              530.19140625
            ],
            [
              85.763671875,
              530.19140625
            ]
          ],
          "children": null,
          "section_hierarchy": {
            "1": "/page/164/SectionHeader/1",
            "3": "/page/165/SectionHeader/9"
          },
          "images": {}
        },
        {
          "id": "/page/165/Text/15",
          "block_type": "Text",
          "html": "<p>The variable blank refers to a Point object, which contains two attributes. Each attribute refers to a floating-point number.</p>",
          "polygon": [
            [
              86.0,
              537.5390625
            ],
            [
              483.50390625,
              537.5390625
            ],
            [
              483.50390625,
              561.0
            ],
            [
              86.0,
              561.0
            ]
          ],
          "children": null,
          "section_hierarchy": {
            "1": "/page/164/SectionHeader/1",
            "3": "/page/165/SectionHeader/9"
          },
          "images": {}
        },
        {
          "id": "/page/165/Text/16",
          "block_type": "Text",
          "html": "<p>You can read the value of an attribute using the same syntax:</p>",
          "polygon": [
            [
              85.46484375,
              568.08984375
            ],
            [
              354.111328125,
              568.08984375
            ],
            [
              354.111328125,
              580.0
            ],
            [
              85.46484375,
              580.0
            ]
          ],
          "children": null,
          "section_hierarchy": {
            "1": "/page/164/SectionHeader/1",
            "3": "/page/165/SectionHeader/9"
          },
          "images": {}
        },
        {
          "id": "/page/165/Code/17",
          "block_type": "Code",
          "html": "<pre>&gt;&gt;&gt; print blank.y\n4.0\n&gt;&gt;&gt; x = blank.x\n&gt;&gt;&gt; print x\n3.0</pre>",
          "polygon": [
            [
              84.34423828125,
              584.0
            ],
            [
              175.0,
              584.0
            ],
            [
              175.0,
              645.046875
            ],
            [
              84.34423828125,
              645.046875
            ]
          ],
          "children": null,
          "section_hierarchy": {
            "1": "/page/164/SectionHeader/1",
            "3": "/page/165/SectionHeader/9"
          },
          "images": {}
        },
        {
          "id": "/page/165/Text/18",
          "block_type": "Text",
          "html": "<p>The expression blank.x means, \"Go to the object blank refers to and get the value of x.\" In this case, we assign that value to a variable named x. There is no conflict between the variable x and the attribute x.</p>",
