          "images": {}
        },
        {
          "id": "/page/166/SectionHeader/7",
          "block_type": "SectionHeader",
          "html": "<h3><b>15.3 Rectangles</b></h3>",
          "polygon": [
            [
              127.97314453125,
              315.94921875
            ],
            [
              240.0,
              315.94921875
            ],
            [
              240.0,
              332.0
            ],
            [
              127.97314453125,
              332.0
            ]
          ],
          "children": null,
          "section_hierarchy": {
            "1": "/page/164/SectionHeader/1",
            "3": "/page/166/SectionHeader/7"
          },
          "images": {}
        },
        {
          "id": "/page/166/Text/8",
          "block_type": "Text",
          "html": "<p>Sometimes it is obvious what the attributes of an object should be, but other times you have to make decisions. For example, imagine you are designing a class to represent rectangles. What attributes would you use to specify the location and size of a rectangle? You can ignore angle; to keep things simple, assume that the rectangle is either vertical or horizontal.</p>",
          "polygon": [
            [
              128.49609375,
              343.40625
            ],
            [
              526.0,
              343.40625
            ],
            [
              526.0,
              391.74609375
            ],
            [
              128.49609375,
              391.74609375
            ]
          ],
          "children": null,
          "section_hierarchy": {
            "1": "/page/164/SectionHeader/1",
            "3": "/page/166/SectionHeader/7"
          },
          "images": {}
        },
        {
          "id": "/page/166/Text/9",
          "block_type": "Text",
          "html": "<p>There are at least two possibilities:</p>",
          "polygon": [
            [
              128.42138671875,
              411.85546875
            ],
            [
              281.197265625,
              411.85546875
            ],
            [
              281.197265625,
              423.0
            ],
            [
              128.42138671875,
              423.0
            ]
          ],
          "children": null,
          "section_hierarchy": {
            "1": "/page/164/SectionHeader/1",
            "3": "/page/166/SectionHeader/7"
          },
          "images": {}
        },
        {
          "id": "/page/166/ListGroup/193",
          "block_type": "ListGroup",
          "html": "<p><ul><content-ref src='/page/166/ListItem/10'></content-ref><content-ref src='/page/166/ListItem/11'></content-ref></ul></p>",
          "polygon": [
            [
              143.0,
              435.83203125
            ],
            [
              526.0,
              435.83203125
            ],
            [
              526.0,
              479.0
            ],
            [
              143.0,
              479.0
            ]
          ],
          "children": [
            {
              "id": "/page/166/ListItem/10",
              "block_type": "ListItem",
              "html": "<li> You could specify one corner of the rectangle (or the center), the width, and the height.</li>",
              "polygon": [
                [
                  143.0,
                  435.83203125
                ],
                [
                  526.0,
                  435.83203125
                ],
                [
                  526.0,
                  459.03515625
                ],
                [
                  143.0,
