        ]
      ],
      "children": [
        {
          "id": "/page/168/PageHeader/0",
          "block_type": "PageHeader",
          "html": "<p><b>15.6. Copying 147</b></p>",
          "polygon": [
            [
              127.82373046875,
              61.0
            ],
            [
              526.0,
              61.0
            ],
            [
              526.0,
              71.0
            ],
            [
              127.82373046875,
              71.0
            ]
          ],
          "children": null,
          "section_hierarchy": {
            "1": "/page/164/SectionHeader/1",
            "3": "/page/167/SectionHeader/11"
          },
          "images": {}
        },
        {
          "id": "/page/168/PageHeader/12",
          "block_type": "PageHeader",
          "html": "<p></p>",
          "polygon": [
            [
              509.501953125,
              60.134765625
            ],
            [
              525.638671875,
              60.134765625
            ],
            [
              525.638671875,
              69.8994140625
            ],
            [
              509.501953125,
              69.8994140625
            ]
          ],
          "children": null,
          "section_hierarchy": {
            "1": "/page/164/SectionHeader/1",
            "3": "/page/167/SectionHeader/11"
          },
          "images": {}
        },
        {
          "id": "/page/168/Text/1",
          "block_type": "Text",
          "html": "<p>Here is an example that demonstrates the effect:</p>",
          "polygon": [
            [
              128.42138671875,
              89.0
            ],
            [
              341.0,
              88.02685546875
            ],
            [
              341.0,
              99.0
            ],
            [
              128.42138671875,
              99.580078125
            ]
          ],
          "children": null,
          "section_hierarchy": {
            "1": "/page/164/SectionHeader/1",
            "3": "/page/167/SectionHeader/11"
          },
          "images": {}
        },
        {
          "id": "/page/168/Code/2",
          "block_type": "Code",
          "html": "<pre>&gt;&gt;&gt; print box.width\n100.0\n&gt;&gt;&gt; print box.height\n200.0\n&gt;&gt;&gt; grow_rectangle(box, 50, 100)\n&gt;&gt;&gt; print box.width\n150.0\n&gt;&gt;&gt; print box.height\n300.0</pre>",
          "polygon": [
            [
              128.57080078125,
              107.0
            ],
            [
              297.0,
              107.0
            ],
            [
              297.0,
              215.015625
            ],
            [
              128.57080078125,
              215.015625
            ]
          ],
          "children": null,
          "section_hierarchy": {
            "1": "/page/164/SectionHeader/1",
            "3": "/page/167/SectionHeader/11"
          },
          "images": {}
        },
        {
          "id": "/page/168/Text/3",
          "block_type": "Text",
          "html": "<p>Inside the function, rect is an alias for box, so if the function modifies rect, box changes. <b>Exercise 15.2.</b> <i>Write a function named</i> move_rectangle <i>that takes a Rectangle and two numbers</i> <i>named</i> dx and dy<i>. It should change the location of the rectangle by adding</i> dx <i>to the</i> x <i>coordinate of</i> corner <i>and adding</i> dy <i>to the</i> y <i>coordinate of</i> corner.</p>",
          "polygon": [
            [
              128.6455078125,
              222.0
            ],
            [
              526.53515625,
              222.0
            ],
            [
              526.53515625,
              268.0
            ],
            [
              128.6455078125,
              268.0
            ]
          ],
          "children": null,
          "section_hierarchy": {
            "1": "/page/164/SectionHeader/1",
            "3": "/page/168/SectionHeader/4"
          },
          "images": {}
        },
        {
          "id": "/page/168/SectionHeader/4",
          "block_type": "SectionHeader",
          "html": "<h3><b>15.6 Copying</b></h3>",
          "polygon": [
            [
              128.197265625,
              302.02734375
            ],
            [
              226.0,
              302.02734375
            ],
            [
              226.0,
              317.49609375
            ],
            [
              128.197265625,
              317.49609375
            ]
          ],
          "children": null,
          "section_hierarchy": {
            "1": "/page/164/SectionHeader/1",
            "3": "/page/168/SectionHeader/4"
          },
          "images": {}
        },
        {
          "id": "/page/168/Text/5",
          "block_type": "Text",
          "html": "<p>Aliasing can make a program difficult to read because changes in one place might have unexpected effects in another place. It is hard to keep track of all the variables that might refer to a given object.</p>",
          "polygon": [
            [
              129.2431640625,
              330.64453125
            ],
            [
              526.0,
              330.64453125
            ],
            [
              526.0,
              366.0
            ],
            [
              129.2431640625,
              366.0
            ]
          ],
          "children": null,
          "section_hierarchy": {
            "1": "/page/164/SectionHeader/1",
            "3": "/page/168/SectionHeader/4"
          },
          "images": {}
        },
        {
          "id": "/page/168/Text/6",
          "block_type": "Text",
          "html": "<p>Copying an object is often an alternative to aliasing. The copy module contains a function called copy that can duplicate any object:</p>",
          "polygon": [
            [
              129.2431640625,
              377.630859375
            ],
            [
              526.53515625,
              377.630859375
            ],
            [
              526.53515625,
              400.25390625
            ],
            [
              129.2431640625,
              400.25390625
            ]
          ],
          "children": null,
          "section_hierarchy": {
            "1": "/page/164/SectionHeader/1",
            "3": "/page/168/SectionHeader/4"
          },
          "images": {}
        },
        {
          "id": "/page/168/Code/7",
          "block_type": "Code",
          "html": "<pre>&gt;&gt;&gt; p1 = Point()\n&gt;&gt;&gt; p1.x = 3.0\n&gt;&gt;&gt; p1.y = 4.0\n&gt;&gt;&gt; import copy\n&gt;&gt;&gt; p2 = copy.copy(p1)</pre>",
          "polygon": [
            [
              129.16845703125,
              408.0
            ],
            [
              245.0,
              408.0
            ],
            [
              245.0,
              479.0
            ],
            [
              127.97314453125,
              479.0
            ]
          ],
          "children": null,
          "section_hierarchy": {
            "1": "/page/164/SectionHeader/1",
            "3": "/page/168/SectionHeader/4"
          },
          "images": {}
        },
        {
          "id": "/page/168/Text/8",
          "block_type": "Text",
          "html": "<p>p1 and p2 contain the same data, but they are not the same Point.</p>",
          "polygon": [
            [
              129.69140625,
              485.33203125
            ],
            [
              415.0,
              485.33203125
            ],
            [
              415.0,
              497.0
            ],
            [
              129.69140625,
              497.0
            ]
          ],
          "children": null,
          "section_hierarchy": {
            "1": "/page/164/SectionHeader/1",
            "3": "/page/168/SectionHeader/4"
          },
          "images": {}
        },
        {
          "id": "/page/168/Code/9",
          "block_type": "Code",
          "html": "<pre>&gt;&gt;&gt; print_point(p1)\n(3.0, 4.0)\n&gt;&gt;&gt; print_point(p2)\n(3.0, 4.0)\n&gt;&gt;&gt; p1 is p2\nFalse\n&gt;&gt;&gt; p1 == p2\nFalse</pre>",
          "polygon": [
            [
              128.27197265625,
              504.28125
            ],
            [
              229.0,
              504.28125
            ],
            [
              229.0,
              600.0
            ],
            [
              128.27197265625,
              600.0
            ]
          ],
          "children": null,
          "section_hierarchy": {
            "1": "/page/164/SectionHeader/1",
            "3": "/page/168/SectionHeader/4"
          },
          "images": {}
        },
        {
          "id": "/page/168/Text/10",
          "block_type": "Text",
          "html": "<p>The is operator indicates that p1 and p2 are not the same object, which is what we expected. But you might have expected == to yield True because these points contain the same data. In that case, you will be disappointed to learn that for instances, the default behavior of the == operator is the same as the is operator; it checks object identity, not object equivalence. This behavior can be changed—we'll see how later.</p>",
          "polygon": [
            [
              128.794921875,
              608.0
            ],
            [
              526.0,
              608.0
            ],
            [
              526.0,
              667.0
            ],
            [
              128.794921875,
              667.0
            ]
          ],
          "children": null,
          "section_hierarchy": {
            "1": "/page/164/SectionHeader/1",
            "3": "/page/168/SectionHeader/4"
          },
          "images": {}
        },
        {
          "id": "/page/168/Text/11",
          "block_type": "Text",
          "html": "<p>If you use copy.copy to duplicate a Rectangle, you will find that it copies the Rectangle object but not the embedded Point.</p>",
          "polygon": [
            [
              128.197265625,
              677.14453125
            ],
            [
              526.0,
              677.14453125
            ],
            [
              526.0,
              701.0
            ],
            [
              128.197265625,
              701.0
            ]
          ],
          "children": null,
          "section_hierarchy": {
            "1": "/page/164/SectionHeader/1",
            "3": "/page/168/SectionHeader/4"
          },
          "images": {}
        }
      ],
      "section_hierarchy": {
        "1": "/page/164/SectionHeader/1",
        "3": "/page/168/SectionHeader/4"
      },
      "images": null
    },
