          "children": null,
          "section_hierarchy": {
            "1": "/page/178/SectionHeader/1",
            "3": "/page/181/SectionHeader/1"
          },
          "images": {}
        },
        {
          "id": "/page/181/Text/2",
          "block_type": "Text",
          "html": "<p>is_after (from Exercise 16.2) is slightly more complicated because it takes two Time objects as parameters. In this case it is conventional to name the first parameter self and the second parameter other:</p>",
          "polygon": [
            [
              85.9130859375,
              110.1181640625
            ],
            [
              483.50390625,
              108.5712890625
            ],
            [
              483.50390625,
              150.7236328125
            ],
            [
              85.9130859375,
              152.2705078125
            ]
          ],
          "children": null,
          "section_hierarchy": {
            "1": "/page/178/SectionHeader/1",
            "3": "/page/181/SectionHeader/1"
          },
          "images": {}
        },
        {
          "id": "/page/181/Text/3",
          "block_type": "Text",
          "html": "<p># inside class Time:</p>",
          "polygon": [
            [
              86.0,
              150.0
            ],
            [
              191.0,
              149.466796875
            ],
            [
              191.0,
              160.1015625
            ],
            [
              86.0,
              161.6484375
            ]
          ],
          "children": null,
          "section_hierarchy": {
            "1": "/page/178/SectionHeader/1",
            "3": "/page/181/SectionHeader/1"
          },
          "images": {}
        },
        {
          "id": "/page/181/Code/4",
          "block_type": "Code",
          "html": "<pre>def is_after(self, other):\n    return self.time_to_int() &gt; other.time_to_int()</pre>",
          "polygon": [
            [
              104.21630859375,
              174.0
            ],
            [
              376.5234375,
              174.0
            ],
            [
              376.5234375,
              197.806640625
            ],
            [
              104.21630859375,
              197.806640625
            ]
          ],
          "children": null,
          "section_hierarchy": {
            "1": "/page/178/SectionHeader/1",
            "3": "/page/181/SectionHeader/1"
          },
          "images": {}
        },
        {
          "id": "/page/181/Text/5",
          "block_type": "Text",
          "html": "<p>To use this method, you have to invoke it on one object and pass the other as an argument: &gt;&gt;&gt; end.is_after(start)</p>",
          "polygon": [
            [
              85.46484375,
              199.546875
            ],
            [
              482.90625,
              199.546875
            ],
            [
              482.90625,
              225.0
            ],
            [
              85.46484375,
              225.0
            ]
          ],
          "children": null,
          "section_hierarchy": {
            "1": "/page/178/SectionHeader/1",
            "3": "/page/181/SectionHeader/1"
          },
          "images": {}
        },
        {
          "id": "/page/181/Text/6",
          "block_type": "Text",
          "html": "<p>True</p>",
          "polygon": [
            [
              84.94189453125,
              226.6171875
            ],
            [
              107.0,
              226.6171875
            ],
            [
              107.0,
              238.21875
            ],
            [
              84.94189453125,
              238.21875
            ]
          ],
          "children": null,
          "section_hierarchy": {
            "1": "/page/178/SectionHeader/1",
            "3": "/page/181/SectionHeader/1"
          },
          "images": {}
        },
        {
          "id": "/page/181/Text/7",
          "block_type": "Text",
          "html": "<p>One nice thing about this syntax is that it almost reads like English: \"end is after start?\"</p>",
          "polygon": [
            [
              85.6142578125,
              239.37890625
            ],
            [
              471.0,
              239.37890625
            ],
            [
              471.0,
