          },
          "images": {}
        },
        {
          "id": "/page/192/Text/16",
          "block_type": "Text",
          "html": "<p>A method like this that uses another function without doing much real work is sometimes called a <b>veneer</b>. The metaphor comes from woodworking, where it is common to glue a thin layer of good quality wood to the surface of a cheaper piece of wood.</p>",
          "polygon": [
            [
              128.794921875,
              665.15625
            ],
            [
              526.236328125,
              665.15625
            ],
