          "images": {}
        },
        {
          "id": "/page/206/Code/7",
          "block_type": "Code",
          "html": "<pre>self.te_code = self.te(width=25, height=10)\nself.te_code.insert(END, 'world.clear()\\n')\nself.te_code.insert(END, 'bob = Turtle(world)\\n')</pre>",
          "polygon": [
            [
              171.0,
              318.0
            ],
            [
              428.0,
              318.0
            ],
            [
              428.0,
              354.0
            ],
            [
              171.0,
              354.0
            ]
          ],
          "children": null,
          "section_hierarchy": {
            "1": "/page/200/SectionHeader/1",
            "3": "/page/204/SectionHeader/12"
          },
          "images": {}
        },
        {
          "id": "/page/206/Code/8",
          "block_type": "Code",
          "html": "<pre>self.bu(text=Run code', command=self.run_text)</pre>",
          "polygon": [
            [
              171.0,
              355.0
            ],
            [
              417.0,
              355.0
            ],
            [
              417.0,
              378.0
            ],
            [
              171.0,
              378.0
            ]
          ],
          "children": null,
          "section_hierarchy": {
            "1": "/page/200/SectionHeader/1",
            "3": "/page/204/SectionHeader/12"
          },
          "images": {}
        },
        {
          "id": "/page/206/Text/9",
          "block_type": "Text",
          "html": "<p>run_text is similar to run_file except that it takes the code from the Text widget instead of from a file:</p>",
          "polygon": [
            [
              127.599609375,
              384.978515625
            ],
            [
              526.236328125,
              384.978515625
            ],
            [
              526.236328125,
              407.0
            ],
            [
              127.599609375,
              407.0
            ]
          ],
          "children": null,
          "section_hierarchy": {
            "1": "/page/200/SectionHeader/1",
            "3": "/page/204/SectionHeader/12"
          },
          "images": {}
        },
        {
          "id": "/page/206/Code/10",
          "block_type": "Code",
          "html": "<pre>def run_text(self):\n   source = self.te_code.get(1.0, END)\n   self.inter.run_code(source, '&lt;user-provided code&gt;')</pre>",
          "polygon": [
            [
              150.609375,
              414.0
            ],
            [
              438.0,
              414.0
            ],
            [
              438.0,
              449.3671875
            ],
            [
              150.609375,
              449.3671875
            ]
          ],
          "children": null,
          "section_hierarchy": {
            "1": "/page/200/SectionHeader/1",
            "3": "/page/204/SectionHeader/12"
          },
          "images": {}
        },
        {
          "id": "/page/206/Text/11",
          "block_type": "Text",
          "html": "<p>Unfortunately, the details of widget layout are different in other languages, and in different Python modules. Tkinter alone provides three different mechanisms for arranging widgets. These mechanisms are called <b>geometry managers</b>. The one I demonstrated in this section is the \"grid\" geometry manager; the others are called \"pack\" and \"place\".</p>",
          "polygon": [
            [
              127.4501953125,
              454.78125
            ],
            [
              526.0,
              454.78125
            ],
            [
              526.0,
              502.0
            ],
            [
              127.4501953125,
              502.0
            ]
          ],
          "children": null,
          "section_hierarchy": {
            "1": "/page/200/SectionHeader/1",
            "3": "/page/204/SectionHeader/12"
          },
          "images": {}
        },
        {
          "id": "/page/206/Text/12",
          "block_type": "Text",
          "html": "<p>Fortunately, most of the concepts in this section apply to other GUI modules and other languages.</p>",
          "polygon": [
            [
              128.9443359375,
              512.0
            ],
            [
              526.0,
              512.0
            ],
            [
              526.0,
              534.4453125
            ],
            [
              128.9443359375,
              534.4453125
            ]
          ],
          "children": null,
          "section_hierarchy": {
            "1": "/page/200/SectionHeader/1",
            "3": "/page/206/SectionHeader/13"
          },
          "images": {}
        },
        {
          "id": "/page/206/SectionHeader/13",
          "block_type": "SectionHeader",
          "html": "<h3><b>19.7 Menus and Callables</b></h3>",
          "polygon": [
            [
              127.67431640625,
              564.99609375
            ],
            [
              308.0,
              564.99609375
            ],
            [
              308.0,
              580.0
            ],
            [
              127.67431640625,
              580.0
            ]
          ],
          "children": null,
          "section_hierarchy": {
            "1": "/page/200/SectionHeader/1",
            "3": "/page/206/SectionHeader/13"
          },
          "images": {}
        },
        {
          "id": "/page/206/Text/14",
          "block_type": "Text",
          "html": "<p>A Menubutton is a widget that looks like a button, but when pressed it pops up a menu. After the user selects an item, the menu disappears.</p>",
          "polygon": [
            [
              128.6455078125,
              591.6796875
            ],
            [
              526.0,
              591.6796875
            ],
            [
              526.0,
              615.0
            ],
            [
              128.6455078125,
              615.0
            ]
          ],
          "children": null,
          "section_hierarchy": {
            "1": "/page/200/SectionHeader/1",
            "3": "/page/206/SectionHeader/13"
          },
          "images": {}
        },
        {
          "id": "/page/206/Text/15",
          "block_type": "Text",
          "html": "<p>Here is code that creates a color selection Menubutton (you can download it from http: //thinkpython.com/code/menubutton_demo.py):</p>",
          "polygon": [
            [
              128.6455078125,
              624.55078125
            ],
            [
              526.0,
              624.55078125
            ],
            [
              526.0,
              648.0
            ],
            [
              128.6455078125,
              648.0
            ]
          ],
          "children": null,
          "section_hierarchy": {
            "1": "/page/200/SectionHeader/1",
            "3": "/page/206/SectionHeader/13"
          },
          "images": {}
        },
        {
          "id": "/page/206/Code/16",
          "block_type": "Code",
          "html": "<pre>g = Gui()\ng.la('Select a color:')\ncolors = ['red', 'green', 'blue']\nmb = g.mb(text=colors[0])</pre>",
          "polygon": [
            [
              128.57080078125,
              653.0
            ],
            [
              302.0,
              653.0
            ],
            [
              302.0,
              701.0
            ],
            [
              128.57080078125,
              701.0
            ]
          ],
          "children": null,
          "section_hierarchy": {
            "1": "/page/200/SectionHeader/1",
            "3": "/page/206/SectionHeader/13"
          },
          "images": {}
        }
      ],
      "section_hierarchy": {
        "1": "/page/200/SectionHeader/1",
        "3": "/page/206/SectionHeader/13"
      },
      "images": null
    },
    {
      "id": "/page/207/Page/210",
      "block_type": "Page",
      "html": "<content-ref src='/page/207/PageHeader/0'></content-ref><content-ref src='/page/207/PageHeader/17'></content-ref><content-ref src='/page/207/Text/1'></content-ref><content-ref src='/page/207/Code/2'></content-ref><content-ref src='/page/207/Text/3'></content-ref><content-ref src='/page/207/Text/4'></content-ref><content-ref src='/page/207/Text/5'></content-ref><content-ref src='/page/207/Text/6'></content-ref><content-ref src='/page/207/Code/7'></content-ref><content-ref src='/page/207/Text/8'></content-ref><content-ref src='/page/207/SectionHeader/9'></content-ref><content-ref src='/page/207/Text/10'></content-ref><content-ref src='/page/207/Text/11'></content-ref><content-ref src='/page/207/Text/12'></content-ref><content-ref src='/page/207/TextInlineMath/13'></content-ref><content-ref src='/page/207/Text/14'></content-ref><content-ref src='/page/207/Text/15'></content-ref><content-ref src='/page/207/Code/16'></content-ref>",
      "polygon": [
        [
          0.0,
          0.0
        ],
        [
          612.0,
          0.0
        ],
        [
          612.0,
          792.0
        ],
        [
          0.0,
          792.0
        ]
      ],
      "children": [
        {
          "id": "/page/207/PageHeader/0",
          "block_type": "PageHeader",
          "html": "<p><b>186 Chapter 19. Case study: Tkinter</b></p>",
          "polygon": [
            [
              86.0,
              60.8115234375
            ],
            [
              483.802734375,
              60.8115234375
            ],
            [
              483.802734375,
              71.0
            ],
            [
              86.0,
              71.0
            ]
          ],
          "children": null,
          "section_hierarchy": {
            "1": "/page/200/SectionHeader/1",
            "3": "/page/206/SectionHeader/13"
          },
          "images": {}
        },
        {
          "id": "/page/207/PageHeader/17",
          "block_type": "PageHeader",
          "html": "<p></p>",
          "polygon": [
            [
              85.3154296875,
              60.47314453125
            ],
            [
              100.5556640625,
              60.47314453125
            ],
            [
              100.5556640625,
              69.85107421875
            ],
            [
              85.3154296875,
              69.85107421875
            ]
          ],
          "children": null,
          "section_hierarchy": {
            "1": "/page/200/SectionHeader/1",
            "3": "/page/206/SectionHeader/13"
          },
          "images": {}
        },
        {
          "id": "/page/207/Text/1",
          "block_type": "Text",
          "html": "<p>mb creates the Menubutton. Initially, the text on the button is the name of the default color. The following loop creates one menu item for each color:</p>",
          "polygon": [
            [
              85.3154296875,
              88.171875
            ],
            [
              482.90625,
              88.171875
            ],
            [
              482.90625,
              111.0
            ],
            [
              85.3154296875,
              111.0
            ]
          ],
          "children": null,
          "section_hierarchy": {
            "1": "/page/200/SectionHeader/1",
            "3": "/page/206/SectionHeader/13"
          },
          "images": {}
        },
        {
          "id": "/page/207/Code/2",
          "block_type": "Code",
          "html": "<pre>for color in colors:\n    g.mi(mb, text=color, command=Callable(set_color, color))</pre>",
          "polygon": [
            [
              85.3154296875,
              117.2724609375
            ],
            [
              414.7734375,
              117.2724609375
            ],
            [
              414.7734375,
              140.0888671875
            ],
            [
              85.3154296875,
              140.0888671875
            ]
          ],
          "children": null,
          "section_hierarchy": {
            "1": "/page/200/SectionHeader/1",
            "3": "/page/206/SectionHeader/13"
          },
          "images": {}
        },
        {
          "id": "/page/207/Text/3",
          "block_type": "Text",
          "html": "<p>The first argument of mi is the Menubutton these items are associated with.</p>",
          "polygon": [
            [
              85.763671875,
              144.6328125
            ],
            [
              417.0,
              144.6328125
            ],
            [
              417.0,
              157.0
            ],
            [
              85.763671875,
              157.0
            ]
          ],
          "children": null,
          "section_hierarchy": {
            "1": "/page/200/SectionHeader/1",
            "3": "/page/206/SectionHeader/13"
          },
          "images": {}
        },
        {
          "id": "/page/207/Text/4",
          "block_type": "Text",
          "html": "<p>The command option is a Callable object, which is something new. So far we have seen functions and bound methods used as callbacks, which works fine if you don't have to pass any arguments to the function. Otherwise you have to construct a Callable object that contains a function, like set_color, and its arguments, like color.</p>",
          "polygon": [
            [
              86.0,
              166.869140625
            ],
            [
              482.607421875,
              166.869140625
            ],
            [
              482.607421875,
              214.0
            ],
            [
              86.0,
              214.0
            ]
          ],
          "children": null,
          "section_hierarchy": {
            "1": "/page/200/SectionHeader/1",
            "3": "/page/206/SectionHeader/13"
          },
          "images": {}
        },
        {
          "id": "/page/207/Text/5",
          "block_type": "Text",
          "html": "<p>The Callable object stores a reference to the function and the arguments as attributes. Later, when the user clicks on a menu item, the callback calls the function and passes the stored arguments.</p>",
          "polygon": [
            [
              85.9130859375,
              223.330078125
            ],
            [
              482.90625,
              223.330078125
            ],
            [
              482.90625,
              259.0
            ],
            [
              85.9130859375,
              259.0
            ]
          ],
          "children": null,
          "section_hierarchy": {
            "1": "/page/200/SectionHeader/1",
            "3": "/page/206/SectionHeader/13"
          },
          "images": {}
        },
        {
          "id": "/page/207/Text/6",
          "block_type": "Text",
          "html": "<p>Here is what set_color might look like:</p>",
          "polygon": [
            [
              85.6142578125,
              268.962890625
            ],
            [
              264.0146484375,
              268.962890625
            ],
            [
              264.0146484375,
              280.0
            ],
            [
              85.6142578125,
              280.0
            ]
          ],
          "children": null,
          "section_hierarchy": {
            "1": "/page/200/SectionHeader/1",
            "3": "/page/206/SectionHeader/13"
          },
          "images": {}
        },
        {
          "id": "/page/207/Code/7",
          "block_type": "Code",
          "html": "<pre>def set_color(color):\n    mb.config(text=color)\n    print color</pre>",
          "polygon": [
            [
              85.09130859375,
              285.3984375
            ],
            [
              217.546875,
              285.3984375
            ],
            [
              217.546875,
              321.0
            ],
            [
              85.09130859375,
              321.0
            ]
          ],
          "children": null,
          "section_hierarchy": {
            "1": "/page/200/SectionHeader/1",
            "3": "/page/206/SectionHeader/13"
          },
          "images": {}
        },
        {
          "id": "/page/207/Text/8",
          "block_type": "Text",
          "html": "<p>When the user selects a menu item and set_color is called, it configures the Menubutton to display the newly-selected color. It also print the color; if you try this example, you can confirm that set_color is called when you select an item (and not called when you create the Callable object).</p>",
          "polygon": [
            [
              85.46484375,
              326.197265625
            ],
            [
              482.607421875,
              326.197265625
            ],
            [
              482.607421875,
              374.0
            ],
            [
              85.46484375,
              374.0
            ]
          ],
          "children": null,
          "section_hierarchy": {
            "1": "/page/200/SectionHeader/1",
            "3": "/page/207/SectionHeader/9"
          },
          "images": {}
        },
        {
          "id": "/page/207/SectionHeader/9",
          "block_type": "SectionHeader",
          "html": "<h3><b>19.8 Binding</b></h3>",
          "polygon": [
            [
              86.0,
              404.12109375
            ],
            [
              180.4921875,
              404.12109375
            ],
            [
              180.4921875,
              419.0
            ],
            [
              86.0,
              419.0
            ]
          ],
          "children": null,
          "section_hierarchy": {
            "1": "/page/200/SectionHeader/1",
            "3": "/page/207/SectionHeader/9"
          },
          "images": {}
        },
        {
          "id": "/page/207/Text/10",
          "block_type": "Text",
          "html": "<p>A <b>binding</b> is an association between a widget, an event and a callback: when an event (like a button press) happens on a widget, the callback is invoked.</p>",
          "polygon": [
            [
              85.9130859375,
              431.578125
            ],
            [
              482.30859375,
              431.578125
            ],
            [
              482.30859375,
              455.0
            ],
            [
              85.9130859375,
              455.0
            ]
          ],
          "children": null,
          "section_hierarchy": {
            "1": "/page/200/SectionHeader/1",
            "3": "/page/207/SectionHeader/9"
          },
          "images": {}
        },
        {
          "id": "/page/207/Text/11",
          "block_type": "Text",
          "html": "<p>Many widgets have default bindings. For example, when you press a button, the default binding changes the relief of the button to make it look depressed. When you release the button, the binding restores the appearance of the button and invokes the callback specified with the command option.</p>",
          "polygon": [
            [
              85.3154296875,
              464.8359375
            ],
            [
              483.50390625,
              464.8359375
            ],
            [
              483.50390625,
              512.015625
            ],
            [
              85.3154296875,
              512.015625
            ]
          ],
          "children": null,
          "section_hierarchy": {
            "1": "/page/200/SectionHeader/1",
            "3": "/page/207/SectionHeader/9"
          },
          "images": {}
        },
        {
          "id": "/page/207/Text/12",
          "block_type": "Text",
          "html": "<p>You can use the bind method to override these default bindings or to add new ones. For example, this code creates a binding for a canvas (you can download the code in this section from http://thinkpython.com/code/draggable_demo.py): ''</p>",
          "polygon": [
            [
              85.6142578125,
              520.91015625
            ],
            [
              483.50390625,
              520.91015625
            ],
            [
              483.50390625,
              560.0
            ],
            [
              85.6142578125,
              560.0
            ]
          ],
          "children": null,
          "section_hierarchy": {
            "1": "/page/200/SectionHeader/1",
            "3": "/page/207/SectionHeader/9"
          },
          "images": {}
        },
        {
          "id": "/page/207/TextInlineMath/13",
          "block_type": "TextInlineMath",
          "html": "<p>ca.bind(&lt;ButtonPress-1&gt;, make_circle)</p>",
          "polygon": [
            [
              85.9130859375,
              563.0
            ],
            [
              290.0,
              563.0
            ],
            [
              290.0,
              573.50390625
            ],
            [
              85.9130859375,
              573.50390625
            ]
          ],
          "children": null,
          "section_hierarchy": {
            "1": "/page/200/SectionHeader/1",
            "3": "/page/207/SectionHeader/9"
          },
          "images": {}
        },
        {
          "id": "/page/207/Text/14",
          "block_type": "Text",
          "html": "<p>The first argument is an event string; this event is triggered when the user presses the left mouse button. Other mouse events include ButtonMotion, ButtonRelease and Double-Button.</p>",
          "polygon": [
            [
              85.763671875,
              580.0
            ],
            [
              483.205078125,
              580.0
            ],
            [
              483.205078125,
              615.0
            ],
            [
              85.763671875,
              615.0
            ]
          ],
          "children": null,
          "section_hierarchy": {
            "1": "/page/200/SectionHeader/1",
            "3": "/page/207/SectionHeader/9"
          },
          "images": {}
        },
        {
          "id": "/page/207/Text/15",
          "block_type": "Text",
          "html": "<p>The second argument is an event handler. An event handler is a function or bound method, like a callback, but an important difference is that an event handler takes an Event object as a parameter. Here is an example:</p>",
          "polygon": [
            [
              85.9130859375,
              623.77734375
            ],
            [
              482.90625,
              623.77734375
            ],
            [
              482.90625,
              660.0
            ],
            [
              85.9130859375,
              660.0
            ]
          ],
          "children": null,
          "section_hierarchy": {
            "1": "/page/200/SectionHeader/1",
            "3": "/page/207/SectionHeader/9"
          },
          "images": {}
        },
        {
          "id": "/page/207/Code/16",
          "block_type": "Code",
          "html": "<pre>def make_circle(event):\n    pos = ca.canvas_coords([event.x, event.y])\n    item = ca.circle(pos, 5, fill='red')</pre>",
          "polygon": [
            [
              86.0,
              666.0
            ],
            [
              327.0,
              666.0
            ],
            [
              327.0,
              701.12109375
            ],
            [
              86.0,
              701.12109375
            ]
          ],
          "children": null,
          "section_hierarchy": {
            "1": "/page/200/SectionHeader/1",
            "3": "/page/207/SectionHeader/9"
          },
          "images": {}
        }
      ],
      "section_hierarchy": {
        "1": "/page/200/SectionHeader/1",
        "3": "/page/207/SectionHeader/9"
      },
      "images": null
    },
    {
      "id": "/page/208/Page/242",
