          "children": null,
          "section_hierarchy": {
            "1": "/page/200/SectionHeader/1",
            "3": "/page/209/SectionHeader/9"
          },
          "images": {}
        },
        {
          "id": "/page/210/PageHeader/23",
          "block_type": "PageHeader",
          "html": "<p></p>",
          "polygon": [
            [
              510.3984375,
              61.43994140625
            ],
            [
              525.33984375,
              61.43994140625
            ],
            [
              525.33984375,
              70.23779296875
            ],
            [
              510.3984375,
              70.23779296875
            ]
          ],
          "children": null,
          "section_hierarchy": {
            "1": "/page/200/SectionHeader/1",
            "3": "/page/209/SectionHeader/9"
          },
          "images": {}
        },
        {
          "id": "/page/210/Text/1",
          "block_type": "Text",
          "html": "<p>As the number of widgets grows, it is increasingly difficult to imagine all possible sequences of events. One way to manage this complexity is to encapsulate the state of the system in an object and then consider:</p>",
          "polygon": [
            [
              129.392578125,
              88.2685546875
            ],
            [
              526.236328125,
              88.2685546875
            ],
            [
              526.236328125,
              123.0
            ],
            [
              129.392578125,
              123.0
            ]
          ],
          "children": null,
          "section_hierarchy": {
            "1": "/page/200/SectionHeader/1",
            "3": "/page/209/SectionHeader/9"
          },
          "images": {}
        },
        {
          "id": "/page/210/ListGroup/158",
          "block_type": "ListGroup",
          "html": "<p><ul><content-ref src='/page/210/ListItem/2'></content-ref><content-ref src='/page/210/ListItem/3'></content-ref><content-ref src='/page/210/ListItem/4'></content-ref><content-ref src='/page/210/ListItem/5'></content-ref></ul></p>",
          "polygon": [
            [
              143.0,
              133.1279296875
            ],
            [
              527.1328125,
              133.1279296875
            ],
            [
              527.1328125,
              251.0
            ],
            [
              143.0,
              251.0
            ]
          ],
          "children": [
            {
              "id": "/page/210/ListItem/2",
              "block_type": "ListItem",
              "html": "<li> What are the possible states? In the Circle example, we might consider two states: before and after the user creates the first circle.</li>",
              "polygon": [
                [
                  143.0,
                  133.1279296875
                ],
                [
                  526.833984375,
                  133.1279296875
                ],
                [
                  526.833984375,
                  156.0
                ],
                [
                  143.0,
                  156.0
                ]
              ],
              "children": null,
              "section_hierarchy": {
                "1": "/page/200/SectionHeader/1",
                "3": "/page/209/SectionHeader/9"
              },
              "images": {}
            },
            {
              "id": "/page/210/ListItem/3",
              "block_type": "ListItem",
              "html": "<li> In each state, what events can occur? In the example, the user can press either of the buttons, or quit.</li>",
              "polygon": [
                [
                  143.0,
                  164.7421875
                ],
                [
                  526.53515625,
                  164.7421875
                ],
                [
                  526.53515625,
                  188.0
                ],
                [
                  143.0,
                  188.0
                ]
              ],
              "children": null,
              "section_hierarchy": {
                "1": "/page/200/SectionHeader/1",
                "3": "/page/209/SectionHeader/9"
              },
              "images": {}
            },
            {
              "id": "/page/210/ListItem/4",
              "block_type": "ListItem",
              "html": "<li> For each state-event pair, what is the desired outcome? Since there are two states and two buttons, there are four state-event pairs to consider.</li>",
              "polygon": [
                [
                  143.0,
                  196.3564453125
                ],
                [
                  526.833984375,
                  196.3564453125
                ],
                [
                  526.833984375,
                  219.0
                ],
                [
                  143.0,
                  219.0
                ]
              ],
              "children": null,
              "section_hierarchy": {
                "1": "/page/200/SectionHeader/1",
                "3": "/page/209/SectionHeader/9"
              },
              "images": {}
            },
            {
              "id": "/page/210/ListItem/5",
              "block_type": "ListItem",
              "html": "<li> What can cause a transition from one state to another? In this case, there is a transition when the user creates the first circle.</li>",
              "polygon": [
                [
                  143.0,
                  227.77734375
                ],
                [
                  527.1328125,
                  227.77734375
                ],
                [
                  527.1328125,
                  251.0
                ],
                [
                  143.0,
                  251.0
                ]
              ],
              "children": null,
              "section_hierarchy": {
                "1": "/page/200/SectionHeader/1",
                "3": "/page/209/SectionHeader/9"
              },
              "images": {}
            }
          ],
          "section_hierarchy": {
            "1": "/page/200/SectionHeader/1",
            "3": "/page/209/SectionHeader/9"
          },
          "images": null
        },
        {
          "id": "/page/210/Text/6",
          "block_type": "Text",
          "html": "<p>You might also find it useful to define, and check, invariants that should hold regardless of the sequence of events.</p>",
          "polygon": [
            [
              129.392578125,
              261.228515625
            ],
            [
              526.236328125,
              261.228515625
            ],
            [
              526.236328125,
              284.0
            ],
            [
              129.392578125,
              284.0
            ]
          ],
          "children": null,
          "section_hierarchy": {
            "1": "/page/200/SectionHeader/1",
            "3": "/page/209/SectionHeader/9"
          },
          "images": {}
        },
        {
          "id": "/page/210/Text/7",
          "block_type": "Text",
          "html": "<p>This approach to GUI programming can help you write correct code without taking the time to test every possible sequence of user events!</p>",
          "polygon": [
            [
              129.5419921875,
              292.552734375
            ],
            [
              526.0,
              292.552734375
            ],
            [
              526.0,
              315.0
            ],
            [
              129.5419921875,
              315.0
            ]
          ],
          "children": null,
          "section_hierarchy": {
            "1": "/page/200/SectionHeader/1",
            "3": "/page/210/SectionHeader/8"
          },
          "images": {}
        },
