      ],
      "children": [
        {
          "id": "/page/214/SectionHeader/0",
          "block_type": "SectionHeader",
          "html": "<h3><b>Appendix A</b></h3>",
          "polygon": [
            [
              129.2431640625,
              164.6455078125
            ],
            [
              245.0,
              164.6455078125
            ],
            [
              245.0,
              186.4951171875
            ],
            [
              129.2431640625,
              186.4951171875
            ]
          ],
          "children": null,
          "section_hierarchy": {
            "1": "/page/214/SectionHeader/1"
          },
          "images": {}
        },
        {
          "id": "/page/214/SectionHeader/1",
          "block_type": "SectionHeader",
          "html": "<h1><b>Debugging</b></h1>",
          "polygon": [
            [
              127.8984375,
              217.916015625
            ],
            [
              258.1875,
              217.916015625
            ],
            [
              258.1875,
              246.146484375
            ],
            [
              127.8984375,
              246.146484375
            ]
          ],
          "children": null,
          "section_hierarchy": {
            "1": "/page/214/SectionHeader/1"
          },
          "images": {}
        },
        {
          "id": "/page/214/Text/2",
          "block_type": "Text",
          "html": "<p>Different kinds of errors can occur in a program, and it is useful to distinguish among them in order to track them down more quickly:</p>",
          "polygon": [
            [
              129.5419921875,
              295.83984375
            ],
            [
              527.1328125,
              295.83984375
            ],
            [
              527.1328125,
              318.26953125
            ],
            [
              129.5419921875,
              318.26953125
            ]
          ],
          "children": null,
          "section_hierarchy": {
            "1": "/page/214/SectionHeader/1"
          },
          "images": {}
        },
        {
          "id": "/page/214/ListGroup/100",
          "block_type": "ListGroup",
          "html": "<p><ul><content-ref src='/page/214/ListItem/3'></content-ref><content-ref src='/page/214/ListItem/4'></content-ref><content-ref src='/page/214/ListItem/5'></content-ref></ul></p>",
          "polygon": [
            [
              143.0,
              332.384765625
            ],
            [
              528.92578125,
              332.384765625
            ],
            [
              528.92578125,
              485.71875
            ],
            [
              143.0,
              485.71875
            ]
          ],
          "children": [
            {
              "id": "/page/214/ListItem/3",
              "block_type": "ListItem",
              "html": "<li> Syntax errors are produced by Python when it is translating the source code into byte code. They usually indicate that there is something wrong with the syntax of the program. Example: Omitting the colon at the end of a def statement yields the somewhat redundant message SyntaxError: invalid syntax.</li>",
              "polygon": [
                [
                  143.0,
                  332.384765625
                ],
                [
                  528.92578125,
                  332.384765625
                ],
                [
                  528.92578125,
                  381.0
                ],
                [
                  143.0,
                  381.0
                ]
              ],
              "children": null,
              "section_hierarchy": {
                "1": "/page/214/SectionHeader/1"
              },
              "images": {}
            },
            {
              "id": "/page/214/ListItem/4",
              "block_type": "ListItem",
              "html": "<li> Runtime errors are produced by the interpreter if something goes wrong while the program is running. Most runtime error messages include information about where the error occurred and what functions were executing. Example: An infinite recursion eventually causes the runtime error \"maximum recursion depth exceeded.\"</li>",
              "polygon": [
                [
                  143.0,
                  390.392578125
                ],
                [
                  527.73046875,
                  390.392578125
                ],
                [
                  527.73046875,
                  439.0
                ],
                [
                  143.0,
                  439.0
                ]
              ],
              "children": null,
              "section_hierarchy": {
                "1": "/page/214/SectionHeader/1"
              },
              "images": {}
            },
            {
              "id": "/page/214/ListItem/5",
              "block_type": "ListItem",
              "html": "<li> Semantic errors are problems with a program that runs without producing error messages but doesn't do the right thing. Example: An expression may not be evaluated in the order you expect, yielding an incorrect result.</li>",
              "polygon": [
                [
                  143.0,
                  450.140625
                ],
                [
                  527.1328125,
                  450.140625
                ],
                [
                  527.1328125,
                  485.71875
                ],
                [
                  143.0,
                  485.71875
                ]
              ],
              "children": null,
              "section_hierarchy": {
                "1": "/page/214/SectionHeader/1"
              },
              "images": {}
            }
          ],
          "section_hierarchy": {
            "1": "/page/214/SectionHeader/1"
          },
          "images": null
        },
        {
          "id": "/page/214/Text/6",
          "block_type": "Text",
          "html": "<p>The first step in debugging is to figure out which kind of error you are dealing with. Although the following sections are organized by error type, some techniques are applicable in more than one situation.</p>",
          "polygon": [
            [
              128.49609375,
              500.4140625
            ],
            [
              527.73046875,
              500.4140625
            ],
            [
              527.73046875,
              536.0
            ],
            [
              128.49609375,
              536.0
            ]
          ],
          "children": null,
          "section_hierarchy": {
            "1": "/page/214/SectionHeader/1",
            "3": "/page/214/SectionHeader/7"
          },
          "images": {}
        },
        {
          "id": "/page/214/SectionHeader/7",
          "block_type": "SectionHeader",
          "html": "<h3><b>A.1 Syntax errors</b></h3>",
          "polygon": [
            [
              128.49609375,
              567.31640625
            ],
            [
              253.40625,
              567.31640625
            ],
            [
              253.40625,
              583.0
            ],
            [
              128.49609375,
              583.0
            ]
          ],
          "children": null,
          "section_hierarchy": {
            "1": "/page/214/SectionHeader/1",
            "3": "/page/214/SectionHeader/7"
          },
          "images": {}
        },
        {
          "id": "/page/214/Text/8",
          "block_type": "Text",
          "html": "<p>Syntax errors are usually easy to fix once you figure out what they are. Unfortunately, the error messages are often not helpful. The most common messages are SyntaxError: invalid syntax and SyntaxError: invalid token, neither of which is very informative.</p>",
          "polygon": [
            [
              128.6455078125,
              595.93359375
            ],
            [
              527.1328125,
              595.93359375
            ],
            [
              527.1328125,
              643.11328125
            ],
            [
              128.6455078125,
              643.11328125
            ]
          ],
          "children": null,
          "section_hierarchy": {
            "1": "/page/214/SectionHeader/1",
            "3": "/page/214/SectionHeader/7"
          },
          "images": {}
        },
        {
          "id": "/page/214/Text/9",
          "block_type": "Text",
          "html": "<p>On the other hand, the message does tell you where in the program the problem occurred. Actually, it tells you where Python noticed a problem, which is not necessarily where the error is. Sometimes the error is prior to the location of the error message, often on the preceding line.</p>",
          "polygon": [
            [
              129.09375,
              653.16796875
            ],
            [
              526.53515625,
              653.16796875
            ],
            [
              526.53515625,
              701.12109375
            ],
            [
              129.09375,
              701.12109375
            ]
          ],
          "children": null,
          "section_hierarchy": {
            "1": "/page/214/SectionHeader/1",
            "3": "/page/214/SectionHeader/7"
          },
          "images": {}
        }
      ],
      "section_hierarchy": {
        "1": "/page/214/SectionHeader/1",
        "3": "/page/214/SectionHeader/7"
      },
      "images": null
    },
    {
      "id": "/page/215/Page/164",
      "block_type": "Page",
      "html": "<content-ref src='/page/215/PageHeader/0'></content-ref><content-ref src='/page/215/PageHeader/19'></content-ref><content-ref src='/page/215/Text/1'></content-ref><content-ref src='/page/215/Text/2'></content-ref><content-ref src='/page/215/Text/3'></content-ref><content-ref src='/page/215/ListGroup/163'></content-ref><content-ref src='/page/215/Text/11'></content-ref><content-ref src='/page/215/SectionHeader/12'></content-ref><content-ref src='/page/215/Text/13'></content-ref><content-ref src='/page/215/Text/14'></content-ref><content-ref src='/page/215/Text/15'></content-ref><content-ref src='/page/215/ListGroup/164'></content-ref>",
      "polygon": [
        [
          0.0,
          0.0
        ],
        [
          612.0,
          0.0
        ],
        [
          612.0,
          792.0
        ],
        [
          0.0,
          792.0
        ]
      ],
      "children": [
        {
          "id": "/page/215/PageHeader/0",
          "block_type": "PageHeader",
          "html": "<p><b>194 Appendix A. Debugging</b></p>",
          "polygon": [
            [
              86.0,
              60.76318359375
            ],
            [
              484.400390625,
              60.76318359375
            ],
            [
              484.400390625,
              71.0
            ],
            [
              86.0,
              71.0
            ]
          ],
          "children": null,
          "section_hierarchy": {
            "1": "/page/214/SectionHeader/1",
            "3": "/page/214/SectionHeader/7"
          },
          "images": {}
        },
        {
          "id": "/page/215/PageHeader/19",
          "block_type": "PageHeader",
          "html": "<p></p>",
          "polygon": [
            [
              85.166015625,
              60.2314453125
            ],
            [
              100.5556640625,
              60.2314453125
            ],
            [
              100.5556640625,
              69.802734375
            ],
            [
              85.166015625,
              69.802734375
            ]
          ],
          "children": null,
          "section_hierarchy": {
            "1": "/page/214/SectionHeader/1",
            "3": "/page/214/SectionHeader/7"
          },
          "images": {}
        },
        {
          "id": "/page/215/Text/1",
          "block_type": "Text",
          "html": "<p>If you are building the program incrementally, you should have a good idea about where the error is. It will be in the last line you added.</p>",
          "polygon": [
            [
              85.9130859375,
              86.67333984375
            ],
            [
              484.1015625,
              86.67333984375
            ],
            [
              484.1015625,
              111.0
            ],
            [
              85.9130859375,
              111.0
            ]
          ],
          "children": null,
          "section_hierarchy": {
            "1": "/page/214/SectionHeader/1",
            "3": "/page/214/SectionHeader/7"
          },
          "images": {}
        },
        {
          "id": "/page/215/Text/2",
          "block_type": "Text",
          "html": "<p>If you are copying code from a book, start by comparing your code to the book's code very carefully. Check every character. At the same time, remember that the book might be wrong, so if you see something that looks like a syntax error, it might be.</p>",
          "polygon": [
            [
              85.46484375,
              120.9462890625
            ],
            [
              484.1015625,
              120.9462890625
            ],
            [
              484.1015625,
              156.0
            ],
            [
              85.46484375,
              156.0
            ]
          ],
          "children": null,
          "section_hierarchy": {
            "1": "/page/214/SectionHeader/1",
            "3": "/page/214/SectionHeader/7"
          },
          "images": {}
        },
        {
          "id": "/page/215/Text/3",
          "block_type": "Text",
          "html": "<p>Here are some ways to avoid the most common syntax errors:</p>",
          "polygon": [
            [
              85.763671875,
              164.548828125
            ],
            [
              359.19140625,
              164.548828125
            ],
            [
              359.19140625,
              176.0
            ],
            [
              85.763671875,
              176.0
            ]
          ],
          "children": null,
          "section_hierarchy": {
            "1": "/page/214/SectionHeader/1",
            "3": "/page/214/SectionHeader/7"
          },
          "images": {}
        },
        {
          "id": "/page/215/ListGroup/163",
          "block_type": "ListGroup",
          "html": "<p><ul><content-ref src='/page/215/ListItem/4'></content-ref><content-ref src='/page/215/ListItem/5'></content-ref><content-ref src='/page/215/ListItem/6'></content-ref><content-ref src='/page/215/ListItem/7'></content-ref><content-ref src='/page/215/ListItem/8'></content-ref><content-ref src='/page/215/ListItem/9'></content-ref><content-ref src='/page/215/ListItem/10'></content-ref></ul></p>",
          "polygon": [
            [
              97.41796875,
              188.912109375
            ],
            [
              485.296875,
              188.912109375
            ],
            [
              485.296875,
              448.0
            ],
            [
              97.41796875,
              448.0
            ]
          ],
          "children": [
            {
              "id": "/page/215/ListItem/4",
              "block_type": "ListItem",
              "html": "<li>1. Make sure you are not using a Python keyword for a variable name.</li>",
              "polygon": [
                [
                  98.912109375,
                  188.912109375
                ],
                [
                  411.486328125,
                  188.912109375
                ],
                [
                  411.486328125,
                  201.0
                ],
                [
                  98.912109375,
                  201.0
                ]
              ],
              "children": null,
              "section_hierarchy": {
                "1": "/page/214/SectionHeader/1",
                "3": "/page/214/SectionHeader/7"
              },
              "images": {}
            },
            {
              "id": "/page/215/ListItem/5",
              "block_type": "ListItem",
              "html": "<li>2. Check that you have a colon at the end of the header of every compound statement, including for, while, if, and def statements.</li>",
              "polygon": [
                [
                  97.8662109375,
                  210.568359375
                ],
                [
                  484.1015625,
                  210.568359375
                ],
                [
                  484.1015625,
                  234.0
                ],
                [
                  97.8662109375,
                  234.0
                ]
              ],
              "children": null,
              "section_hierarchy": {
                "1": "/page/214/SectionHeader/1",
                "3": "/page/214/SectionHeader/7"
              },
              "images": {}
            },
            {
              "id": "/page/215/ListItem/6",
              "block_type": "ListItem",
              "html": "<li>3. Make sure that any strings in the code have matching quotation marks.</li>",
              "polygon": [
                [
                  98.1650390625,
                  243.826171875
                ],
                [
                  425.53125,
                  243.826171875
                ],
                [
                  425.53125,
                  255.0
                ],
                [
                  98.1650390625,
                  255.0
                ]
              ],
              "children": null,
              "section_hierarchy": {
                "1": "/page/214/SectionHeader/1",
                "3": "/page/214/SectionHeader/7"
              },
              "images": {}
            },
            {
              "id": "/page/215/ListItem/7",
              "block_type": "ListItem",
              "html": "<li>4. If you have multiline strings with triple quotes (single or double), make sure you have terminated the string properly. An unterminated string may cause an invalid token error at the end of your program, or it may treat the following part of the program as a string until it comes to the next string. In the second case, it might not produce an error message at all!</li>",
              "polygon": [
                [
                  98.4638671875,
                  264.515625
                ],
                [
                  485.296875,
                  264.515625
                ],
                [
                  485.296875,
                  324.84375
                ],
                [
                  98.4638671875,
                  324.84375
                ]
              ],
              "children": null,
              "section_hierarchy": {
                "1": "/page/214/SectionHeader/1",
                "3": "/page/214/SectionHeader/7"
              },
              "images": {}
            },
            {
              "id": "/page/215/ListItem/8",
              "block_type": "ListItem",
              "html": "<li>5. An unclosed opening operator—(, {, or [—makes Python continue with the next line as part of the current statement. Generally, an error occurs almost immediately in the next line.</li>",
              "polygon": [
                [
                  97.716796875,
                  334.51171875
                ],
                [
                  484.998046875,
                  332.96484375
                ],
                [
                  484.998046875,
                  369.0
                ],
                [
                  97.716796875,
                  369.703125
                ]
              ],
              "children": null,
              "section_hierarchy": {
                "1": "/page/214/SectionHeader/1",
                "3": "/page/214/SectionHeader/7"
              },
              "images": {}
            },
            {
              "id": "/page/215/ListItem/9",
              "block_type": "ListItem",
              "html": "<li>6. Check for the classic = instead of == inside a conditional.</li>",
              "polygon": [
                [
                  98.015625,
                  378.59765625
                ],
                [
                  360.38671875,
                  378.59765625
                ],
                [
                  360.38671875,
                  390.0
                ],
                [
                  98.015625,
                  390.0
                ]
              ],
              "children": null,
              "section_hierarchy": {
                "1": "/page/214/SectionHeader/1",
                "3": "/page/214/SectionHeader/7"
              },
              "images": {}
            },
            {
              "id": "/page/215/ListItem/10",
              "block_type": "ListItem",
              "html": "<li>7. Check the indentation to make sure it lines up the way it is supposed to. Python can handle space and tabs, but if you mix them it can cause problems. The best way to avoid this problem is to use a text editor that knows about Python and generates consistent indentation.</li>",
              "polygon": [
                [
                  97.41796875,
                  399.8671875
                ],
                [
                  484.69921875,
                  399.8671875
                ],
                [
                  484.69921875,
                  448.0
                ],
                [
                  97.41796875,
                  448.0
                ]
              ],
              "children": null,
              "section_hierarchy": {
                "1": "/page/214/SectionHeader/1",
                "3": "/page/214/SectionHeader/7"
              },
              "images": {}
            }
          ],
          "section_hierarchy": {
            "1": "/page/214/SectionHeader/1",
            "3": "/page/214/SectionHeader/7"
          },
          "images": null
        },
        {
          "id": "/page/215/Text/11",
          "block_type": "Text",
          "html": "<p>If nothing works, move on to the next section...</p>",
          "polygon": [
            [
              85.763671875,
              461.35546875
            ],
            [
              294.345703125,
              461.35546875
            ],
            [
              294.345703125,
              472.18359375
            ],
            [
              85.763671875,
              472.18359375
            ]
          ],
          "children": null,
          "section_hierarchy": {
            "1": "/page/214/SectionHeader/1",
            "3": "/page/214/SectionHeader/7",
            "4": "/page/215/SectionHeader/12"
          },
          "images": {}
        },
        {
          "id": "/page/215/SectionHeader/12",
          "block_type": "SectionHeader",
          "html": "<h4><b>A.1.1 I keep making changes and it makes no difference.</b></h4>",
          "polygon": [
            [
              85.763671875,
              498.09375
            ],
            [
              404.015625,
              498.09375
            ],
            [
              404.015625,
              511.2421875
            ],
            [
              85.763671875,
              511.2421875
            ]
          ],
          "children": null,
          "section_hierarchy": {
            "1": "/page/214/SectionHeader/1",
            "3": "/page/214/SectionHeader/7",
            "4": "/page/215/SectionHeader/12"
          },
          "images": {}
        },
        {
          "id": "/page/215/Text/13",
          "block_type": "Text",
          "html": "<p>If the interpreter says there is an error and you don't see it, that might be because you and the interpreter are not looking at the same code. Check your programming environment to make sure that the program you are editing is the one Python is trying to run.</p>",
          "polygon": [
            [
              85.763671875,
              521.68359375
            ],
            [
              484.1015625,
              521.68359375
            ],
            [
              484.1015625,
              557.26171875
            ],
            [
              85.763671875,
              557.26171875
            ]
          ],
          "children": null,
          "section_hierarchy": {
            "1": "/page/214/SectionHeader/1",
            "3": "/page/214/SectionHeader/7",
            "4": "/page/215/SectionHeader/12"
          },
          "images": {}
        },
        {
          "id": "/page/215/Text/14",
          "block_type": "Text",
          "html": "<p>If you are not sure, try putting an obvious and deliberate syntax error at the beginning of the program. Now run it again. If the interpreter doesn't find the new error, you are not running the new code.</p>",
          "polygon": [
            [
              85.6142578125,
              566.54296875
            ],
            [
              485.296875,
              566.54296875
            ],
            [
              485.296875,
              602.0
            ],
            [
              85.6142578125,
              602.0
            ]
          ],
          "children": null,
          "section_hierarchy": {
            "1": "/page/214/SectionHeader/1",
            "3": "/page/214/SectionHeader/7",
            "4": "/page/215/SectionHeader/12"
          },
          "images": {}
        },
        {
          "id": "/page/215/Text/15",
          "block_type": "Text",
          "html": "<p>There are a few likely culprits:</p>",
          "polygon": [
            [
              86.0,
              611.015625
            ],
            [
              220.0869140625,
              611.015625
            ],
            [
              220.0869140625,
              622.0
            ],
            [
              86.0,
              622.0
            ]
          ],
          "children": null,
          "section_hierarchy": {
            "1": "/page/214/SectionHeader/1",
            "3": "/page/214/SectionHeader/7",
            "4": "/page/215/SectionHeader/12"
          },
          "images": {}
        },
        {
          "id": "/page/215/ListGroup/164",
          "block_type": "ListGroup",
          "html": "<p><ul><content-ref src='/page/215/ListItem/16'></content-ref><content-ref src='/page/215/ListItem/17'></content-ref><content-ref src='/page/215/ListItem/18'></content-ref></ul></p>",
          "polygon": [
            [
              100.0,
              636.5390625
            ],
            [
              484.1015625,
              636.5390625
            ],
            [
              484.1015625,
              701.12109375
            ],
            [
              100.0,
              701.12109375
            ]
          ],
          "children": [
            {
              "id": "/page/215/ListItem/16",
              "block_type": "ListItem",
              "html": "<li> You edited the file and forgot to save the changes before running it again. Some programming environments do this for you, but some don't.</li>",
              "polygon": [
                [
                  100.0,
                  636.5390625
                ],
                [
                  484.1015625,
                  636.5390625
                ],
                [
                  484.1015625,
                  659.0
                ],
                [
                  100.0,
                  659.0
                ]
              ],
              "children": null,
              "section_hierarchy": {
                "1": "/page/214/SectionHeader/1",
                "3": "/page/214/SectionHeader/7",
                "4": "/page/215/SectionHeader/12"
              },
              "images": {}
            },
            {
              "id": "/page/215/ListItem/17",
              "block_type": "ListItem",
              "html": "<li> You changed the name of the file, but you are still running the old name.</li>",
              "polygon": [
                [
                  100.0,
                  669.0234375
                ],
                [
                  431.5078125,
                  669.0234375
                ],
                [
                  431.5078125,
                  680.0
                ],
                [
                  100.0,
                  680.0
                ]
              ],
              "children": null,
              "section_hierarchy": {
                "1": "/page/214/SectionHeader/1",
                "3": "/page/214/SectionHeader/7",
                "4": "/page/215/SectionHeader/12"
              },
              "images": {}
            },
            {
              "id": "/page/215/ListItem/18",
              "block_type": "ListItem",
              "html": "<li> Something in your development environment is configured incorrectly.</li>",
              "polygon": [
                [
                  100.0,
                  690.29296875
                ],
                [
                  426.12890625,
                  690.29296875
                ],
                [
                  426.12890625,
                  701.12109375
                ],
                [
                  100.0,
                  701.12109375
                ]
              ],
              "children": null,
              "section_hierarchy": {
                "1": "/page/214/SectionHeader/1",
                "3": "/page/214/SectionHeader/7",
                "4": "/page/215/SectionHeader/12"
              },
              "images": {}
            }
          ],
          "section_hierarchy": {
            "1": "/page/214/SectionHeader/1",
            "3": "/page/214/SectionHeader/7",
            "4": "/page/215/SectionHeader/12"
          },
          "images": null
        }
      ],
      "section_hierarchy": {
        "1": "/page/214/SectionHeader/1",
        "3": "/page/214/SectionHeader/7",
        "4": "/page/215/SectionHeader/12"
      },
      "images": null
    },
    {
      "id": "/page/216/Page/139",
      "block_type": "Page",
      "html": "<content-ref src='/page/216/PageHeader/0'></content-ref><content-ref src='/page/216/PageHeader/17'></content-ref><content-ref src='/page/216/ListGroup/138'></content-ref><content-ref src='/page/216/Text/3'></content-ref><content-ref src='/page/216/SectionHeader/4'></content-ref><content-ref src='/page/216/Text/5'></content-ref><content-ref src='/page/216/SectionHeader/6'></content-ref><content-ref src='/page/216/Text/7'></content-ref><content-ref src='/page/216/Text/8'></content-ref><content-ref src='/page/216/SectionHeader/9'></content-ref><content-ref src='/page/216/Text/10'></content-ref><content-ref src='/page/216/ListItem/11'></content-ref><content-ref src='/page/216/Text/12'></content-ref><content-ref src='/page/216/ListItem/13'></content-ref><content-ref src='/page/216/Text/14'></content-ref><content-ref src='/page/216/ListGroup/139'></content-ref>",
      "polygon": [
        [
          0.0,
          0.0
        ],
        [
          612.0,
          0.0
        ],
        [
          612.0,
          792.0
        ],
        [
          0.0,
          792.0
        ]
      ],
      "children": [
        {
          "id": "/page/216/PageHeader/0",
          "block_type": "PageHeader",
          "html": "<p><b>A.2. Runtime errors 195</b></p>",
          "polygon": [
            [
              128.27197265625,
              61.0
            ],
            [
              526.0,
              61.0
            ],
            [
              526.0,
              71.0
            ],
            [
              128.27197265625,
              71.0
            ]
          ],
          "children": null,
          "section_hierarchy": {
            "1": "/page/214/SectionHeader/1",
            "3": "/page/214/SectionHeader/7",
            "4": "/page/215/SectionHeader/12"
          },
          "images": {}
        },
        {
          "id": "/page/216/PageHeader/17",
          "block_type": "PageHeader",
          "html": "<p></p>",
          "polygon": [
            [
              510.697265625,
              60.56982421875
            ],
            [
              526.236328125,
              60.56982421875
            ],
            [
              526.236328125,
              70.43115234375
            ],
            [
              510.697265625,
              70.43115234375
            ]
          ],
          "children": null,
          "section_hierarchy": {
            "1": "/page/214/SectionHeader/1",
            "3": "/page/214/SectionHeader/7",
            "4": "/page/215/SectionHeader/12"
          },
          "images": {}
        },
        {
          "id": "/page/216/ListGroup/138",
          "block_type": "ListGroup",
          "html": "<p><ul><content-ref src='/page/216/ListItem/1'></content-ref><content-ref src='/page/216/ListItem/2'></content-ref></ul></p>",
          "polygon": [
            [
              142.83984375,
              87.978515625
            ],
            [
              527.73046875,
              87.978515625
            ],
            [
              527.73046875,
              156.0
            ],
            [
              142.83984375,
              156.0
            ]
          ],
          "children": [
            {
              "id": "/page/216/ListItem/1",
              "block_type": "ListItem",
              "html": "<li> If you are writing a module and using import, make sure you don't give your module the same name as one of the standard Python modules.</li>",
              "polygon": [
                [
                  142.83984375,
                  87.978515625
                ],
                [
                  527.73046875,
                  87.978515625
                ],
                [
                  527.73046875,
                  111.0
                ],
                [
                  142.83984375,
                  111.0
                ]
              ],
              "children": null,
              "section_hierarchy": {
                "1": "/page/214/SectionHeader/1",
                "3": "/page/214/SectionHeader/7",
                "4": "/page/215/SectionHeader/12"
              },
              "images": {}
            },
            {
              "id": "/page/216/ListItem/2",
              "block_type": "ListItem",
              "html": "<li> If you are using import to read a module, remember that you have to restart the interpreter or use reload to read a modified file. If you import the module again, it doesn't do anything.</li>",
              "polygon": [
                [
                  142.83984375,
                  119.7861328125
                ],
                [
                  526.53515625,
                  119.7861328125
                ],
                [
                  526.53515625,
                  156.0
                ],
                [
                  142.83984375,
                  156.0
                ]
              ],
              "children": null,
              "section_hierarchy": {
                "1": "/page/214/SectionHeader/1",
                "3": "/page/214/SectionHeader/7",
                "4": "/page/215/SectionHeader/12"
              },
              "images": {}
            }
          ],
          "section_hierarchy": {
            "1": "/page/214/SectionHeader/1",
            "3": "/page/214/SectionHeader/7",
            "4": "/page/215/SectionHeader/12"
          },
          "images": null
        },
        {
          "id": "/page/216/Text/3",
          "block_type": "Text",
          "html": "<p>If you get stuck and you can't figure out what is going on, one approach is to start again with a new program like \"Hello, World!,\" and make sure you can get a known program to run. Then gradually add the pieces of the original program to the new one.</p>",
          "polygon": [
            [
              128.794921875,
              168.3193359375
            ],
            [
              527.431640625,
              168.3193359375
            ],
            [
              527.431640625,
              204.0
            ],
            [
              128.794921875,
              204.0
            ]
          ],
          "children": null,
          "section_hierarchy": {
            "1": "/page/214/SectionHeader/1",
            "3": "/page/216/SectionHeader/4"
          },
          "images": {}
        },
        {
          "id": "/page/216/SectionHeader/4",
          "block_type": "SectionHeader",
          "html": "<h3><b>A.2 Runtime errors</b></h3>",
          "polygon": [
            [
              129.2431640625,
              233.384765625
            ],
            [
              265.2099609375,
              233.384765625
            ],
            [
              265.2099609375,
              248.0
            ],
            [
              129.2431640625,
              248.0
            ]
          ],
          "children": null,
          "section_hierarchy": {
            "1": "/page/214/SectionHeader/1",
            "3": "/page/216/SectionHeader/4"
          },
          "images": {}
        },
        {
          "id": "/page/216/Text/5",
          "block_type": "Text",
          "html": "<p>Once your program is syntactically correct, Python can compile it and at least start running it. What could possibly go wrong?</p>",
          "polygon": [
            [
              128.6455078125,
              259.681640625
            ],
            [
              527.73046875,
              259.681640625
            ],
            [
              527.73046875,
              283.0
            ],
            [
              128.6455078125,
              283.0
            ]
          ],
          "children": null,
          "section_hierarchy": {
            "1": "/page/214/SectionHeader/1",
            "3": "/page/216/SectionHeader/4",
            "4": "/page/216/SectionHeader/6"
          },
          "images": {}
        },
        {
          "id": "/page/216/SectionHeader/6",
          "block_type": "SectionHeader",
          "html": "<h4><b>A.2.1 My program does absolutely nothing.</b></h4>",
          "polygon": [
            [
              128.794921875,
              307.828125
            ],
            [
              375.029296875,
              307.828125
            ],
            [
              375.029296875,
              321.0
            ],
            [
              128.794921875,
              321.0
            ]
          ],
          "children": null,
          "section_hierarchy": {
            "1": "/page/214/SectionHeader/1",
            "3": "/page/216/SectionHeader/4",
            "4": "/page/216/SectionHeader/6"
          },
          "images": {}
        },
        {
          "id": "/page/216/Text/7",
          "block_type": "Text",
          "html": "<p>This problem is most common when your file consists of functions and classes but does not actually invoke anything to start execution. This may be intentional if you only plan to import this module to supply classes and functions.</p>",
          "polygon": [
            [
              128.49609375,
              331.224609375
            ],
            [
              527.73046875,
              331.224609375
            ],
            [
              527.73046875,
              367.0
            ],
            [
              128.49609375,
              367.0
            ]
          ],
          "children": null,
          "section_hierarchy": {
            "1": "/page/214/SectionHeader/1",
            "3": "/page/216/SectionHeader/4",
            "4": "/page/216/SectionHeader/6"
          },
          "images": {}
        },
        {
          "id": "/page/216/Text/8",
          "block_type": "Text",
          "html": "<p>If it is not intentional, make sure that you are invoking a function to start execution, or execute one from the interactive prompt. Also see the \"Flow of Execution\" section below.</p>",
          "polygon": [
            [
              128.49609375,
              375.50390625
            ],
            [
              527.73046875,
              375.50390625
            ],
            [
              527.73046875,
              399.0
            ],
            [
              128.49609375,
              399.0
            ]
          ],
          "children": null,
          "section_hierarchy": {
            "1": "/page/214/SectionHeader/1",
            "3": "/page/216/SectionHeader/4",
            "4": "/page/216/SectionHeader/9"
          },
          "images": {}
        },
        {
          "id": "/page/216/SectionHeader/9",
          "block_type": "SectionHeader",
          "html": "<h4><b>A.2.2 My program hangs.</b></h4>",
          "polygon": [
            [
              128.86962890625,
              423.45703125
            ],
            [
              277.3125,
              423.45703125
            ],
            [
              277.3125,
              437.0
            ],
            [
              128.86962890625,
              437.0
            ]
          ],
          "children": null,
          "section_hierarchy": {
            "1": "/page/214/SectionHeader/1",
            "3": "/page/216/SectionHeader/4",
            "4": "/page/216/SectionHeader/9"
          },
          "images": {}
        },
        {
          "id": "/page/216/Text/10",
          "block_type": "Text",
          "html": "<p>If a program stops and seems to be doing nothing, it is \"hanging.\" Often that means that it is caught in an infinite loop or infinite recursion.</p>",
          "polygon": [
            [
              129.8408203125,
              447.046875
            ],
            [
              527.73046875,
              447.046875
            ],
            [
              527.73046875,
              471.0
            ],
            [
              129.8408203125,
              471.0
            ]
          ],
          "children": null,
          "section_hierarchy": {
            "1": "/page/214/SectionHeader/1",
            "3": "/page/216/SectionHeader/4",
            "4": "/page/216/SectionHeader/9"
          },
          "images": {}
        },
        {
          "id": "/page/216/ListItem/11",
          "block_type": "ListItem",
          "html": "<li> If there is a particular loop that you suspect is the problem, add a print statement immediately before the loop that says \"entering the loop\" and another immediately after that says \"exiting the loop.\"</li>",
          "polygon": [
            [
              143.0,
              483.01171875
            ],
            [
              528.328125,
              483.01171875
            ],
            [
              528.328125,
              519.36328125
            ],
            [
              143.0,
              519.36328125
            ]
          ],
          "children": null,
          "section_hierarchy": {
            "1": "/page/214/SectionHeader/1",
            "3": "/page/216/SectionHeader/4",
            "4": "/page/216/SectionHeader/9"
          },
          "images": {}
        },
        {
          "id": "/page/216/Text/12",
          "block_type": "Text",
          "html": "<p>Run the program. If you get the first message and not the second, you've got an infinite loop. Go to the \"Infinite Loop\" section below.</p>",
          "polygon": [
            [
              152.2529296875,
              525.1640625
            ],
            [
              527.73046875,
              525.1640625
            ],
            [
              527.73046875,
              548.0
            ],
            [
              152.2529296875,
              548.0
            ]
          ],
          "children": null,
          "section_hierarchy": {
            "1": "/page/214/SectionHeader/1",
            "3": "/page/216/SectionHeader/4",
            "4": "/page/216/SectionHeader/9"
          },
          "images": {}
        },
        {
          "id": "/page/216/ListItem/13",
          "block_type": "ListItem",
          "html": "<li> Most of the time, an infinite recursion will cause the program to run for a while and then produce a \"RuntimeError: Maximum recursion depth exceeded\" error. If that happens, go to the \"Infinite Recursion\" section below.</li>",
          "polygon": [
            [
              143.0,
              556.48828125
            ],
            [
              527.431640625,
              556.48828125
            ],
            [
              527.431640625,
              592.06640625
            ],
            [
              143.0,
              592.06640625
            ]
          ],
          "children": null,
          "section_hierarchy": {
            "1": "/page/214/SectionHeader/1",
            "3": "/page/216/SectionHeader/4",
            "4": "/page/216/SectionHeader/9"
          },
          "images": {}
        },
        {
          "id": "/page/216/Text/14",
          "block_type": "Text",
          "html": "<p>If you are not getting this error but you suspect there is a problem with a recursive method or function, you can still use the techniques in the \"Infinite Recursion\" section.</p>",
          "polygon": [
            [
              152.8505859375,
              597.48046875
            ],
            [
              527.1328125,
              597.48046875
            ],
            [
              527.1328125,
              633.05859375
            ],
            [
              152.8505859375,
              633.05859375
            ]
          ],
          "children": null,
          "section_hierarchy": {
            "1": "/page/214/SectionHeader/1",
            "3": "/page/216/SectionHeader/4",
            "4": "/page/216/SectionHeader/9"
          },
          "images": {}
        },
        {
          "id": "/page/216/ListGroup/139",
          "block_type": "ListGroup",
          "html": "<p><ul><content-ref src='/page/216/ListItem/15'></content-ref><content-ref src='/page/216/ListItem/16'></content-ref></ul></p>",
          "polygon": [
            [
              143.0,
              641.56640625
            ],
            [
              527.1328125,
              641.56640625
            ],
            [
              527.1328125,
              698.0
            ],
            [
              143.0,
              698.0
            ]
          ],
          "children": [
            {
              "id": "/page/216/ListItem/15",
              "block_type": "ListItem",
              "html": "<li> If neither of those steps works, start testing other loops and other recursive functions and methods.</li>",
              "polygon": [
                [
                  143.0,
                  641.56640625
                ],
                [
                  527.1328125,
                  641.56640625
                ],
                [
                  527.1328125,
                  666.0
                ],
                [
                  143.0,
                  666.0
                ]
              ],
              "children": null,
              "section_hierarchy": {
                "1": "/page/214/SectionHeader/1",
                "3": "/page/216/SectionHeader/4",
                "4": "/page/216/SectionHeader/9"
              },
              "images": {}
            },
            {
              "id": "/page/216/ListItem/16",
              "block_type": "ListItem",
              "html": "<li> If that doesn't work, then it is possible that you don't understand the flow of execution in your program. Go to the \"Flow of Execution\" section below.</li>",
              "polygon": [
                [
                  143.0,
                  674.05078125
                ],
                [
                  526.236328125,
                  674.05078125
                ],
                [
                  526.236328125,
                  698.0
                ],
                [
                  143.0,
                  698.0
                ]
              ],
              "children": null,
              "section_hierarchy": {
                "1": "/page/214/SectionHeader/1",
                "3": "/page/216/SectionHeader/4",
                "4": "/page/216/SectionHeader/9"
              },
              "images": {}
            }
          ],
          "section_hierarchy": {
            "1": "/page/214/SectionHeader/1",
            "3": "/page/216/SectionHeader/4",
            "4": "/page/216/SectionHeader/9"
          },
          "images": null
        }
      ],
      "section_hierarchy": {
        "1": "/page/214/SectionHeader/1",
        "3": "/page/216/SectionHeader/4",
        "4": "/page/216/SectionHeader/9"
      },
      "images": null
    },
    {
      "id": "/page/217/Page/163",
      "block_type": "Page",
      "html": "<content-ref src='/page/217/PageHeader/0'></content-ref><content-ref src='/page/217/PageHeader/16'></content-ref><content-ref src='/page/217/Text/1'></content-ref><content-ref src='/page/217/Text/2'></content-ref><content-ref src='/page/217/Text/3'></content-ref><content-ref src='/page/217/Code/4'></content-ref><content-ref src='/page/217/Text/5'></content-ref><content-ref src='/page/217/SectionHeader/6'></content-ref><content-ref src='/page/217/Text/7'></content-ref><content-ref src='/page/217/Text/8'></content-ref><content-ref src='/page/217/Text/9'></content-ref><content-ref src='/page/217/SectionHeader/10'></content-ref><content-ref src='/page/217/Text/11'></content-ref><content-ref src='/page/217/Text/12'></content-ref><content-ref src='/page/217/SectionHeader/13'></content-ref><content-ref src='/page/217/Text/14'></content-ref><content-ref src='/page/217/Text/15'></content-ref>",
      "polygon": [
        [
          0.0,
          0.0
        ],
        [
