      ],
      "children": [
        {
          "id": "/page/217/PageHeader/0",
          "block_type": "PageHeader",
          "html": "<p><b>196 Appendix A. Debugging</b></p>",
          "polygon": [
            [
              86.0,
              60.2314453125
            ],
            [
              483.802734375,
              60.2314453125
            ],
            [
              483.802734375,
              71.0
            ],
            [
              86.0,
              71.0
            ]
          ],
          "children": null,
          "section_hierarchy": {
            "1": "/page/214/SectionHeader/1",
            "3": "/page/216/SectionHeader/4",
            "4": "/page/216/SectionHeader/9"
          },
          "images": {}
        },
        {
          "id": "/page/217/PageHeader/16",
          "block_type": "PageHeader",
          "html": "<p></p>",
          "polygon": [
            [
              85.68896484375,
              60.0380859375
            ],
            [
              101.37744140625,
              60.0380859375
            ],
            [
              101.37744140625,
              69.802734375
            ],
            [
              85.68896484375,
              69.802734375
            ]
          ],
          "children": null,
          "section_hierarchy": {
            "1": "/page/214/SectionHeader/1",
            "3": "/page/216/SectionHeader/4",
            "4": "/page/216/SectionHeader/9"
          },
          "images": {}
        },
        {
          "id": "/page/217/Text/1",
          "block_type": "Text",
          "html": "<p><b>Infinite Loop</b></p>",
          "polygon": [
            [
              86.0,
              87.4951171875
            ],
            [
              147.09814453125,
              87.4951171875
            ],
            [
              147.09814453125,
              99.0
            ],
            [
              86.0,
              99.0
            ]
          ],
          "children": null,
          "section_hierarchy": {
            "1": "/page/214/SectionHeader/1",
            "3": "/page/216/SectionHeader/4",
            "4": "/page/216/SectionHeader/9"
          },
          "images": {}
        },
        {
          "id": "/page/217/Text/2",
          "block_type": "Text",
          "html": "<p>If you think you have an infinite loop and you think you know what loop is causing the problem, add a print statement at the end of the loop that prints the values of the variables in the condition and the value of the condition.</p>",
          "polygon": [
            [
              85.3154296875,
              107.5078125
            ],
            [
              482.90625,
              107.5078125
            ],
            [
              482.90625,
              144.0
            ],
            [
              85.3154296875,
              144.0
            ]
          ],
          "children": null,
          "section_hierarchy": {
            "1": "/page/214/SectionHeader/1",
            "3": "/page/216/SectionHeader/4",
            "4": "/page/216/SectionHeader/9"
          },
          "images": {}
        },
        {
          "id": "/page/217/Text/3",
          "block_type": "Text",
          "html": "<p>For example:</p>",
          "polygon": [
            [
              85.24072265625,
              152.0771484375
            ],
            [
              144.0,
              152.0771484375
            ],
            [
              144.0,
              164.0
            ],
            [
              85.24072265625,
              164.0
            ]
          ],
          "children": null,
          "section_hierarchy": {
            "1": "/page/214/SectionHeader/1",
            "3": "/page/216/SectionHeader/4",
            "4": "/page/216/SectionHeader/9"
          },
          "images": {}
        },
        {
          "id": "/page/217/Code/4",
          "block_type": "Code",
          "html": "<pre>while x &gt; 0 and y &lt; 0 :\n    # do something to x\n    # do something to y\n    print \"x: \", x\n    print \"y: \", y\n    print \"condition: \", (x &gt; 0 and y &lt; 0)</pre>",
          "polygon": [
            [
              85.83837890625,
              170.0
            ],
            [
              306.0,
              170.0
            ],
            [
              306.0,
              253.0
            ],
            [
              85.83837890625,
              253.0
            ]
          ],
          "children": null,
          "section_hierarchy": {
            "1": "/page/214/SectionHeader/1",
            "3": "/page/216/SectionHeader/4",
            "4": "/page/216/SectionHeader/9"
          },
          "images": {}
        },
        {
          "id": "/page/217/Text/5",
          "block_type": "Text",
          "html": "<p>Now when you run the program, you will see three lines of output for each time through the loop. The last time through the loop, the condition should be false. If the loop keeps going, you will be able to see the values of x and y, and you might figure out why they are not being updated correctly.</p>",
          "polygon": [
            [
              85.3154296875,
              256.587890625
            ],
            [
              482.90625,
              256.587890625
            ],
            [
              482.90625,
              305.314453125
            ],
            [
              85.3154296875,
              305.314453125
            ]
          ],
          "children": null,
          "section_hierarchy": {
            "1": "/page/214/SectionHeader/1",
            "3": "/page/216/SectionHeader/4",
            "4": "/page/217/SectionHeader/6"
          },
          "images": {}
        },
        {
          "id": "/page/217/SectionHeader/6",
          "block_type": "SectionHeader",
          "html": "<h4><b>Infinite Recursion</b></h4>",
          "polygon": [
            [
              85.46484375,
              327.9375
            ],
            [
              169.0,
              327.9375
            ],
            [
              169.0,
              340.0
            ],
            [
              85.46484375,
              340.0
            ]
          ],
          "children": null,
          "section_hierarchy": {
            "1": "/page/214/SectionHeader/1",
            "3": "/page/216/SectionHeader/4",
            "4": "/page/217/SectionHeader/6"
          },
          "images": {}
        },
        {
          "id": "/page/217/Text/7",
          "block_type": "Text",
          "html": "<p>Most of the time, an infinite recursion will cause the program to run for a while and then produce a Maximum recursion depth exceeded error.</p>",
          "polygon": [
            [
              85.3154296875,
              349.98046875
            ],
            [
              483.50390625,
              349.98046875
            ],
            [
              483.50390625,
              374.0
            ],
            [
              85.3154296875,
              374.0
            ]
          ],
          "children": null,
          "section_hierarchy": {
            "1": "/page/214/SectionHeader/1",
            "3": "/page/216/SectionHeader/4",
            "4": "/page/217/SectionHeader/6"
          },
          "images": {}
        },
        {
          "id": "/page/217/Text/8",
          "block_type": "Text",
          "html": "<p>If you suspect that a function or method is causing an infinite recursion, start by checking to make sure that there is a base case. In other words, there should be some condition that will cause the function or method to return without making a recursive invocation. If not, then you need to rethink the algorithm and identify a base case.</p>",
          "polygon": [
            [
              85.3154296875,
              382.271484375
            ],
            [
              483.50390625,
              382.271484375
            ],
            [
              483.50390625,
              430.0
            ],
            [
              85.3154296875,
              430.0
            ]
          ],
          "children": null,
          "section_hierarchy": {
            "1": "/page/214/SectionHeader/1",
            "3": "/page/216/SectionHeader/4",
            "4": "/page/217/SectionHeader/6"
          },
          "images": {}
        },
        {
          "id": "/page/217/Text/9",
          "block_type": "Text",
          "html": "<p>If there is a base case but the program doesn't seem to be reaching it, add a print statement at the beginning of the function or method that prints the parameters. Now when you run the program, you will see a few lines of output every time the function or method is invoked, and you will see the parameters. If the parameters are not moving toward the base case, you will get some ideas about why not.</p>",
          "polygon": [
            [
              85.166015625,
              438.15234375
            ],
            [
              483.50390625,
              438.15234375
            ],
            [
              483.50390625,
              499.0
            ],
            [
              85.166015625,
              499.0
            ]
          ],
          "children": null,
          "section_hierarchy": {
            "1": "/page/214/SectionHeader/1",
            "3": "/page/216/SectionHeader/4",
            "4": "/page/217/SectionHeader/10"
          },
          "images": {}
        },
        {
          "id": "/page/217/SectionHeader/10",
          "block_type": "SectionHeader",
          "html": "<h4><b>Flow of Execution</b></h4>",
          "polygon": [
            [
              85.46484375,
              520.91015625
            ],
            [
              168.0,
              520.91015625
            ],
            [
              168.0,
              533.0
            ],
            [
              85.46484375,
              533.0
            ]
          ],
          "children": null,
          "section_hierarchy": {
            "1": "/page/214/SectionHeader/1",
            "3": "/page/216/SectionHeader/4",
            "4": "/page/217/SectionHeader/10"
          },
          "images": {}
        },
        {
          "id": "/page/217/Text/11",
          "block_type": "Text",
          "html": "<p>If you are not sure how the flow of execution is moving through your program, add print statements to the beginning of each function with a message like \"entering function foo,\" where foo is the name of the function.</p>",
          "polygon": [
            [
              85.6142578125,
              542.953125
            ],
            [
              482.90625,
              542.953125
            ],
            [
              482.90625,
              579.0
            ],
            [
              85.6142578125,
              579.0
            ]
          ],
          "children": null,
          "section_hierarchy": {
            "1": "/page/214/SectionHeader/1",
            "3": "/page/216/SectionHeader/4",
            "4": "/page/217/SectionHeader/10"
          },
          "images": {}
        },
        {
          "id": "/page/217/Text/12",
          "block_type": "Text",
          "html": "<p>Now when you run the program, it will print a trace of each function as it is invoked.</p>",
          "polygon": [
            [
              85.46484375,
              586.65234375
            ],
            [
              461.0,
              586.65234375
            ],
            [
              461.0,
              599.0
            ],
            [
              85.46484375,
              599.0
            ]
          ],
          "children": null,
          "section_hierarchy": {
            "1": "/page/214/SectionHeader/1",
            "3": "/page/216/SectionHeader/4",
            "4": "/page/217/SectionHeader/13"
          },
          "images": {}
        },
        {
          "id": "/page/217/SectionHeader/13",
          "block_type": "SectionHeader",
          "html": "<h4><b>A.2.3 When I run the program I get an exception.</b></h4>",
          "polygon": [
            [
              85.3154296875,
              623.77734375
            ],
            [
              360.0,
              623.77734375
            ],
            [
              360.0,
              636.15234375
            ],
            [
              85.3154296875,
              636.15234375
            ]
          ],
          "children": null,
          "section_hierarchy": {
            "1": "/page/214/SectionHeader/1",
            "3": "/page/216/SectionHeader/4",
            "4": "/page/217/SectionHeader/13"
          },
          "images": {}
        },
        {
          "id": "/page/217/Text/14",
          "block_type": "Text",
          "html": "<p>If something goes wrong during runtime, Python prints a message that includes the name of the exception, the line of the program where the problem occurred, and a traceback.</p>",
          "polygon": [
            [
              85.763671875,
              645.43359375
            ],
            [
              483.802734375,
              645.43359375
            ],
            [
              483.802734375,
              669.0
            ],
            [
              85.763671875,
              669.0
            ]
          ],
          "children": null,
          "section_hierarchy": {
            "1": "/page/214/SectionHeader/1",
            "3": "/page/216/SectionHeader/4",
            "4": "/page/217/SectionHeader/13"
          },
          "images": {}
        },
        {
          "id": "/page/217/Text/15",
          "block_type": "Text",
          "html": "<p class=\"has-continuation\">The traceback identifies the function that is currently running, and then the function that invoked it, and then the function that invoked <i>that</i>, and so on. In other words, it traces the</p>",
          "polygon": [
            [
              85.46484375,
              677.53125
            ],
            [
              484.69921875,
              677.53125
            ],
            [
              484.69921875,
              701.0
            ],
            [
              85.46484375,
              701.0
            ]
          ],
          "children": null,
          "section_hierarchy": {
            "1": "/page/214/SectionHeader/1",
            "3": "/page/216/SectionHeader/4",
            "4": "/page/217/SectionHeader/13"
          },
          "images": {}
        }
      ],
      "section_hierarchy": {
        "1": "/page/214/SectionHeader/1",
        "3": "/page/216/SectionHeader/4",
        "4": "/page/217/SectionHeader/13"
      },
      "images": null
    },
    {
      "id": "/page/218/Page/190",
      "block_type": "Page",
      "html": "<content-ref src='/page/218/PageHeader/0'></content-ref><content-ref src='/page/218/PageHeader/16'></content-ref><content-ref src='/page/218/Text/1'></content-ref><content-ref src='/page/218/Text/2'></content-ref><content-ref src='/page/218/ListGroup/190'></content-ref><content-ref src='/page/218/Text/10'></content-ref><content-ref src='/page/218/ListItem/11'></content-ref><content-ref src='/page/218/Text/12'></content-ref><content-ref src='/page/218/SectionHeader/13'></content-ref><content-ref src='/page/218/Text/14'></content-ref><content-ref src='/page/218/Text/15'></content-ref>",
      "polygon": [
        [
          0.0,
          0.0
        ],
        [
          612.0,
          0.0
        ],
        [
          612.0,
          792.0
        ],
        [
          0.0,
          792.0
        ]
      ],
      "children": [
        {
          "id": "/page/218/PageHeader/0",
          "block_type": "PageHeader",
          "html": "<p><b>A.2. Runtime errors 197</b></p>",
          "polygon": [
            [
              128.6455078125,
              61.0
            ],
            [
              526.0,
              61.0
            ],
            [
              526.0,
              71.01123046875
            ],
            [
              128.6455078125,
              71.01123046875
            ]
          ],
          "children": null,
          "section_hierarchy": {
            "1": "/page/214/SectionHeader/1",
            "3": "/page/216/SectionHeader/4",
            "4": "/page/217/SectionHeader/13"
          },
          "images": {}
        },
        {
          "id": "/page/218/PageHeader/16",
          "block_type": "PageHeader",
          "html": "<p></p>",
          "polygon": [
            [
              510.99609375,
              61.24658203125
            ],
            [
              525.9375,
              61.24658203125
            ],
            [
              525.9375,
              70.23779296875
            ],
            [
              510.99609375,
              70.23779296875
            ]
          ],
          "children": null,
          "section_hierarchy": {
            "1": "/page/214/SectionHeader/1",
            "3": "/page/216/SectionHeader/4",
            "4": "/page/217/SectionHeader/13"
          },
          "images": {}
        },
        {
          "id": "/page/218/Text/1",
          "block_type": "Text",
          "html": "<p>sequence of function invocations that got you to where you are. It also includes the line number in your file where each of these calls occurs.</p>",
          "polygon": [
            [
              129.09375,
              88.89697265625
            ],
            [
              526.53515625,
              88.89697265625
            ],
            [
              526.53515625,
              111.0
            ],
            [
              129.09375,
              111.0
            ]
          ],
          "children": null,
          "section_hierarchy": {
            "1": "/page/214/SectionHeader/1",
            "3": "/page/216/SectionHeader/4",
            "4": "/page/217/SectionHeader/13"
          },
          "images": {}
        },
        {
          "id": "/page/218/Text/2",
          "block_type": "Text",
          "html": "<p>The first step is to examine the place in the program where the error occurred and see if you can figure out what happened. These are some of the most common runtime errors:</p>",
          "polygon": [
            [
              129.2431640625,
              120.7529296875
            ],
            [
              526.53515625,
              120.7529296875
            ],
            [
              526.53515625,
              144.0
            ],
            [
              129.2431640625,
              144.0
            ]
          ],
          "children": null,
          "section_hierarchy": {
            "1": "/page/214/SectionHeader/1",
            "3": "/page/216/SectionHeader/4",
            "4": "/page/217/SectionHeader/13"
          },
          "images": {}
        },
        {
          "id": "/page/218/ListGroup/190",
          "block_type": "ListGroup",
          "html": "<p><ul><content-ref src='/page/218/ListItem/3'></content-ref><content-ref src='/page/218/ListItem/4'></content-ref><content-ref src='/page/218/ListItem/5'></content-ref><content-ref src='/page/218/ListItem/6'></content-ref><content-ref src='/page/218/ListItem/7'></content-ref><content-ref src='/page/218/ListItem/8'></content-ref><content-ref src='/page/218/ListItem/9'></content-ref></ul></p>",
          "polygon": [
            [
              129.2431640625,
              159.908203125
            ],
            [
              527.1328125,
              158.361328125
            ],
            [
              527.1328125,
              420.0
            ],
            [
              129.2431640625,
              420.0
            ]
          ],
          "children": [
            {
              "id": "/page/218/ListItem/3",
              "block_type": "ListItem",
              "html": "<li><b>NameError:</b> You are trying to use a variable that doesn't exist in the current environment. Remember that local variables are local. You cannot refer to them from outside the function where they are defined.</li>",
              "polygon": [
                [
                  129.2431640625,
                  159.908203125
                ],
                [
                  527.1328125,
                  158.361328125
                ],
                [
                  527.1328125,
                  194.0
                ],
                [
                  129.2431640625,
                  194.1328125
                ]
              ],
              "children": null,
              "section_hierarchy": {
                "1": "/page/214/SectionHeader/1",
                "3": "/page/216/SectionHeader/4",
                "4": "/page/217/SectionHeader/13"
              },
              "images": {}
            },
            {
              "id": "/page/218/ListItem/4",
              "block_type": "ListItem",
              "html": "<li><b>TypeError:</b> There are several possible causes:</li>",
              "polygon": [
                [
                  129.5419921875,
                  205.154296875
                ],
                [
                  330.0,
                  205.154296875
                ],
                [
                  330.0,
                  216.0
                ],
                [
                  129.5419921875,
                  216.0
                ]
              ],
              "children": null,
              "section_hierarchy": {
                "1": "/page/214/SectionHeader/1",
                "3": "/page/216/SectionHeader/4",
                "4": "/page/217/SectionHeader/13"
              },
              "images": {}
            },
            {
              "id": "/page/218/ListItem/5",
              "block_type": "ListItem",
              "html": "<li> You are trying to use a value improperly. Example: indexing a string, list, or tuple with something other than an integer.</li>",
              "polygon": [
                [
                  165.0,
                  222.943359375
                ],
                [
                  526.0,
                  222.943359375
                ],
                [
                  526.0,
                  245.0
                ],
                [
                  165.0,
                  245.0
                ]
              ],
              "children": null,
              "section_hierarchy": {
                "1": "/page/214/SectionHeader/1",
                "3": "/page/216/SectionHeader/4",
                "4": "/page/217/SectionHeader/13"
              },
              "images": {}
            },
            {
              "id": "/page/218/ListItem/6",
              "block_type": "ListItem",
              "html": "<li> There is a mismatch between the items in a format string and the items passed for conversion. This can happen if either the number of items does not match or an invalid conversion is called for.</li>",
              "polygon": [
                [
                  165.0,
                  251.947265625
                ],
                [
                  526.0,
                  251.947265625
                ],
                [
                  526.0,
                  287.0
                ],
                [
                  165.0,
                  287.0
                ]
              ],
              "children": null,
              "section_hierarchy": {
                "1": "/page/214/SectionHeader/1",
                "3": "/page/216/SectionHeader/4",
                "4": "/page/217/SectionHeader/13"
              },
              "images": {}
            },
            {
              "id": "/page/218/ListItem/7",
              "block_type": "ListItem",
              "html": "<li> You are passing the wrong number of arguments to a function or method. For methods, look at the method definition and check that the first parameter is self. Then look at the method invocation; make sure you are invoking the method on an object with the right type and providing the other arguments correctly.</li>",
              "polygon": [
                [
                  165.0,
                  293.0
                ],
                [
                  526.0,
                  293.0
                ],
                [
                  526.0,
                  352.30078125
                ],
                [
                  165.0,
                  352.30078125
                ]
              ],
              "children": null,
              "section_hierarchy": {
                "1": "/page/214/SectionHeader/1",
                "3": "/page/216/SectionHeader/4",
                "4": "/page/217/SectionHeader/13"
              },
              "images": {}
            },
            {
              "id": "/page/218/ListItem/8",
              "block_type": "ListItem",
              "html": "<li><b>KeyError:</b> You are trying to access an element of a dictionary using a key that the dictionary does not contain.</li>",
              "polygon": [
                [
                  129.8408203125,
                  363.708984375
                ],
                [
                  526.0,
                  363.708984375
                ],
                [
                  526.0,
                  386.0
                ],
                [
                  129.8408203125,
                  386.0
                ]
              ],
              "children": null,
              "section_hierarchy": {
                "1": "/page/214/SectionHeader/1",
                "3": "/page/216/SectionHeader/4",
                "4": "/page/217/SectionHeader/13"
              },
              "images": {}
            },
            {
              "id": "/page/218/ListItem/9",
              "block_type": "ListItem",
              "html": "<li><b>AttributeError:</b> You are trying to access an attribute or method that does not exist. Check the spelling! You can use dir to list the attributes that do exist.</li>",
              "polygon": [
                [
                  129.2431640625,
                  397.0
                ],
                [
                  526.0,
                  397.0
                ],
                [
                  526.0,
                  420.0
                ],
                [
                  129.2431640625,
                  420.0
                ]
              ],
              "children": null,
              "section_hierarchy": {
                "1": "/page/214/SectionHeader/1",
                "3": "/page/216/SectionHeader/4",
                "4": "/page/217/SectionHeader/13"
              },
              "images": {}
            }
          ],
          "section_hierarchy": {
            "1": "/page/214/SectionHeader/1",
            "3": "/page/216/SectionHeader/4",
            "4": "/page/217/SectionHeader/13"
          },
          "images": null
        },
        {
          "id": "/page/218/Text/10",
          "block_type": "Text",
          "html": "<p>If an AttributeError indicates that an object has NoneType, that means that it is None. One common cause is forgetting to return a value from a function; if you get to the end of a function without hitting a return statement, it returns None. Another common cause is using the result from a list method, like sort, that returns None.</p>",
          "polygon": [
            [
              154.6435546875,
              426.0
            ],
            [
              526.0,
              426.0
            ],
            [
              526.0,
              473.0
            ],
            [
              154.6435546875,
              473.0
            ]
          ],
          "children": null,
          "section_hierarchy": {
            "1": "/page/214/SectionHeader/1",
            "3": "/page/216/SectionHeader/4",
            "4": "/page/217/SectionHeader/13"
          },
          "images": {}
        },
        {
          "id": "/page/218/ListItem/11",
          "block_type": "ListItem",
          "html": "<li><b>IndexError:</b> The index you are using to access a list, string, or tuple is greater than its length minus one. Immediately before the site of the error, add a print statement to display the value of the index and the length of the array. Is the array the right size? Is the index the right value?</li>",
          "polygon": [
            [
              129.392578125,
              484.0
            ],
            [
              526.833984375,
              484.0
            ],
            [
              526.833984375,
              531.0
            ],
            [
              129.392578125,
              531.0
            ]
          ],
          "children": null,
          "section_hierarchy": {
            "1": "/page/214/SectionHeader/1",
            "3": "/page/216/SectionHeader/4",
            "4": "/page/217/SectionHeader/13"
          },
          "images": {}
        },
        {
          "id": "/page/218/Text/12",
          "block_type": "Text",
          "html": "<p>The Python debugger (pdb) is useful for tracking down Exceptions because it allows you to examine the state of the program immediately before the error. You can read about pdb at http://docs.python.org/2/library/pdb.html.</p>",
          "polygon": [
            [
              128.9443359375,
              546.8203125
            ],
            [
              526.0,
              546.8203125
            ],
            [
              526.0,
              581.0
            ],
            [
              128.9443359375,
              581.0
            ]
          ],
          "children": null,
          "section_hierarchy": {
            "1": "/page/214/SectionHeader/1",
            "3": "/page/216/SectionHeader/4",
            "4": "/page/218/SectionHeader/13"
          },
          "images": {}
        },
        {
          "id": "/page/218/SectionHeader/13",
          "block_type": "SectionHeader",
          "html": "<h4><b>A.2.4 I added so many</b> print <b>statements I get inundated with output.</b></h4>",
          "polygon": [
            [
              129.09375,
              609.0
            ],
            [
              511.59375,
              609.0
            ],
            [
              511.59375,
              621.0
            ],
            [
              129.09375,
              621.0
            ]
          ],
          "children": null,
          "section_hierarchy": {
            "1": "/page/214/SectionHeader/1",
            "3": "/page/216/SectionHeader/4",
            "4": "/page/218/SectionHeader/13"
          },
          "images": {}
        },
        {
          "id": "/page/218/Text/14",
          "block_type": "Text",
          "html": "<p>One of the problems with using print statements for debugging is that you can end up buried in output. There are two ways to proceed: simplify the output or simplify the program.</p>",
          "polygon": [
            [
              128.6455078125,
              633.0
            ],
            [
              527.1328125,
              633.0
            ],
            [
              527.1328125,
              668.0
            ],
            [
              128.6455078125,
              668.0
            ]
          ],
          "children": null,
          "section_hierarchy": {
            "1": "/page/214/SectionHeader/1",
            "3": "/page/216/SectionHeader/4",
            "4": "/page/218/SectionHeader/13"
          },
          "images": {}
        },
        {
          "id": "/page/218/Text/15",
          "block_type": "Text",
          "html": "<p>To simplify the output, you can remove or comment out print statements that aren't helping, or combine them, or format the output so it is easier to understand.</p>",
          "polygon": [
            [
              128.3466796875,
              678.3046875
            ],
            [
              526.0,
              678.3046875
            ],
            [
              526.0,
              701.0
            ],
            [
              128.3466796875,
              701.0
            ]
          ],
          "children": null,
          "section_hierarchy": {
            "1": "/page/214/SectionHeader/1",
            "3": "/page/216/SectionHeader/4",
            "4": "/page/218/SectionHeader/13"
          },
          "images": {}
        }
      ],
      "section_hierarchy": {
        "1": "/page/214/SectionHeader/1",
        "3": "/page/216/SectionHeader/4",
        "4": "/page/218/SectionHeader/13"
      },
      "images": null
    },
    {
      "id": "/page/219/Page/134",
      "block_type": "Page",
      "html": "<content-ref src='/page/219/PageHeader/0'></content-ref><content-ref src='/page/219/PageHeader/15'></content-ref><content-ref src='/page/219/Text/1'></content-ref><content-ref src='/page/219/Text/2'></content-ref><content-ref src='/page/219/Text/3'></content-ref><content-ref src='/page/219/Text/4'></content-ref><content-ref src='/page/219/SectionHeader/5'></content-ref><content-ref src='/page/219/Text/6'></content-ref><content-ref src='/page/219/Text/7'></content-ref><content-ref src='/page/219/Text/8'></content-ref><content-ref src='/page/219/SectionHeader/9'></content-ref><content-ref src='/page/219/Text/10'></content-ref><content-ref src='/page/219/ListGroup/134'></content-ref><content-ref src='/page/219/Text/14'></content-ref>",
      "polygon": [
        [
          0.0,
          0.0
        ],
        [
          612.0,
          0.0
        ],
        [
          612.0,
          792.0
        ],
        [
          0.0,
          792.0
        ]
      ],
      "children": [
        {
          "id": "/page/219/PageHeader/0",
          "block_type": "PageHeader",
          "html": "<p><b>198 Appendix A. Debugging</b></p>",
          "polygon": [
            [
              86.0,
              60.521484375
            ],
            [
              484.400390625,
              60.521484375
            ],
            [
              484.400390625,
              71.0
            ],
            [
              86.0,
              71.0
            ]
          ],
          "children": null,
          "section_hierarchy": {
            "1": "/page/214/SectionHeader/1",
            "3": "/page/216/SectionHeader/4",
            "4": "/page/218/SectionHeader/13"
          },
          "images": {}
        },
        {
          "id": "/page/219/PageHeader/15",
          "block_type": "PageHeader",
          "html": "<p></p>",
          "polygon": [
            [
              85.6142578125,
              59.89306640625
            ],
            [
              101.4521484375,
              59.89306640625
            ],
            [
              101.4521484375,
              70.14111328125
            ],
            [
              85.6142578125,
              70.14111328125
            ]
          ],
          "children": null,
          "section_hierarchy": {
            "1": "/page/214/SectionHeader/1",
            "3": "/page/216/SectionHeader/4",
            "4": "/page/218/SectionHeader/13"
          },
          "images": {}
        },
        {
          "id": "/page/219/Text/1",
          "block_type": "Text",
          "html": "<p>To simplify the program, there are several things you can do. First, scale down the problem the program is working on. For example, if you are searching a list, search a <i>small</i> list. If the program takes input from the user, give it the simplest input that causes the problem.</p>",
          "polygon": [
            [
              85.9130859375,
              87.15673828125
            ],
            [
              482.90625,
              87.15673828125
            ],
            [
              482.90625,
              123.0
            ],
            [
              85.9130859375,
              123.0
            ]
          ],
          "children": null,
          "section_hierarchy": {
            "1": "/page/214/SectionHeader/1",
            "3": "/page/216/SectionHeader/4",
            "4": "/page/218/SectionHeader/13"
          },
          "images": {}
        },
        {
          "id": "/page/219/Text/2",
          "block_type": "Text",
          "html": "<p>Second, clean up the program. Remove dead code and reorganize the program to make it as easy to read as possible. For example, if you suspect that the problem is in a deeply nested part of the program, try rewriting that part with simpler structure. If you suspect a large function, try splitting it into smaller functions and testing them separately.</p>",
          "polygon": [
            [
              85.3154296875,
              133.03125
            ],
            [
              483.50390625,
              133.03125
            ],
            [
              483.50390625,
              181.0
            ],
            [
              85.3154296875,
              181.0
            ]
          ],
          "children": null,
          "section_hierarchy": {
            "1": "/page/214/SectionHeader/1",
            "3": "/page/216/SectionHeader/4",
            "4": "/page/218/SectionHeader/13"
          },
          "images": {}
        },
        {
          "id": "/page/219/Text/3",
          "block_type": "Text",
          "html": "<p>Often the process of finding the minimal test case leads you to the bug. If you find that a program works in one situation but not in another, that gives you a clue about what is going on.</p>",
          "polygon": [
            [
              85.46484375,
              190.3623046875
            ],
            [
              483.50390625,
              190.3623046875
            ],
            [
              483.50390625,
              226.6171875
            ],
            [
              85.46484375,
              226.6171875
            ]
          ],
          "children": null,
          "section_hierarchy": {
            "1": "/page/214/SectionHeader/1",
            "3": "/page/216/SectionHeader/4",
            "4": "/page/218/SectionHeader/13"
          },
          "images": {}
        },
        {
          "id": "/page/219/Text/4",
          "block_type": "Text",
          "html": "<p>Similarly, rewriting a piece of code can help you find subtle bugs. If you make a change that you think shouldn't affect the program, and it does, that can tip you off.</p>",
          "polygon": [
            [
              84.8671875,
              235.8984375
            ],
            [
              484.1015625,
              235.8984375
            ],
            [
              484.1015625,
              260.0
            ],
            [
              84.8671875,
              260.0
            ]
          ],
          "children": null,
          "section_hierarchy": {
            "1": "/page/214/SectionHeader/1",
            "3": "/page/219/SectionHeader/5"
          },
          "images": {}
        },
        {
          "id": "/page/219/SectionHeader/5",
          "block_type": "SectionHeader",
          "html": "<h3><b>A.3 Semantic errors</b></h3>",
          "polygon": [
            [
              86.0,
              289.458984375
            ],
            [
              226.212890625,
              289.458984375
            ],
            [
              226.212890625,
              306.0
            ],
            [
              86.0,
              306.0
            ]
          ],
          "children": null,
          "section_hierarchy": {
            "1": "/page/214/SectionHeader/1",
            "3": "/page/219/SectionHeader/5"
          },
          "images": {}
        },
        {
          "id": "/page/219/Text/6",
          "block_type": "Text",
          "html": "<p>In some ways, semantic errors are the hardest to debug, because the interpreter provides no information about what is wrong. Only you know what the program is supposed to do.</p>",
          "polygon": [
            [
              85.763671875,
              318.65625
            ],
            [
              484.1015625,
              318.65625
            ],
            [
              484.1015625,
              342.0
            ],
            [
              85.763671875,
              342.0
            ]
          ],
          "children": null,
          "section_hierarchy": {
            "1": "/page/214/SectionHeader/1",
            "3": "/page/219/SectionHeader/5"
          },
          "images": {}
        },
        {
          "id": "/page/219/Text/7",
          "block_type": "Text",
          "html": "<p>The first step is to make a connection between the program text and the behavior you are seeing. You need a hypothesis about what the program is actually doing. One of the things that makes that hard is that computers run so fast.</p>",
          "polygon": [
            [
              85.3154296875,
              351.9140625
            ],
            [
              484.69921875,
              351.9140625
            ],
            [
              484.69921875,
              387.87890625
            ],
            [
              85.3154296875,
              387.87890625
            ]
          ],
          "children": null,
          "section_hierarchy": {
            "1": "/page/214/SectionHeader/1",
            "3": "/page/219/SectionHeader/5"
          },
          "images": {}
        },
        {
          "id": "/page/219/Text/8",
          "block_type": "Text",
          "html": "<p>You will often wish that you could slow the program down to human speed, and with some debuggers you can. But the time it takes to insert a few well-placed print statements is often short compared to setting up the debugger, inserting and removing breakpoints, and \"stepping\" the program to where the error is occurring.</p>",
          "polygon": [
            [
              85.6142578125,
              397.16015625
            ],
            [
              485.296875,
              397.16015625
            ],
            [
              485.296875,
              445.0
            ],
            [
              85.6142578125,
              445.0
            ]
          ],
          "children": null,
          "section_hierarchy": {
            "1": "/page/214/SectionHeader/1",
            "3": "/page/219/SectionHeader/9"
          },
          "images": {}
        },
        {
          "id": "/page/219/SectionHeader/9",
          "block_type": "SectionHeader",
          "html": "<h3><b>A.3.1 My program doesn't work.</b></h3>",
          "polygon": [
            [
              86.0,
              472.18359375
            ],
            [
              271.93359375,
              472.18359375
            ],
            [
              271.93359375,
              486.10546875
            ],
            [
              86.0,
              486.10546875
            ]
          ],
          "children": null,
          "section_hierarchy": {
            "1": "/page/214/SectionHeader/1",
            "3": "/page/219/SectionHeader/9"
          },
          "images": {}
        },
        {
          "id": "/page/219/Text/10",
          "block_type": "Text",
          "html": "<p>You should ask yourself these questions:</p>",
          "polygon": [
            [
              86.0,
              496.93359375
            ],
            [
              266.1064453125,
              496.93359375
            ],
            [
              266.1064453125,
              508.53515625
            ],
            [
              86.0,
              508.53515625
            ]
          ],
          "children": null,
          "section_hierarchy": {
            "1": "/page/214/SectionHeader/1",
            "3": "/page/219/SectionHeader/9"
          },
          "images": {}
        },
        {
          "id": "/page/219/ListGroup/134",
          "block_type": "ListGroup",
          "html": "<p><ul><content-ref src='/page/219/ListItem/11'></content-ref><content-ref src='/page/219/ListItem/12'></content-ref><content-ref src='/page/219/ListItem/13'></content-ref></ul></p>",
          "polygon": [
            [
              99.9580078125,
              522.0703125
            ],
            [
              484.1015625,
              522.0703125
            ],
            [
              484.1015625,
              651.0
            ],
            [
              99.9580078125,
              651.0
            ]
          ],
          "children": [
            {
              "id": "/page/219/ListItem/11",
              "block_type": "ListItem",
              "html": "<li> Is there something the program was supposed to do but which doesn't seem to be happening? Find the section of the code that performs that function and make sure it is executing when you think it should.</li>",
              "polygon": [
                [
                  100.0,
                  522.0703125
                ],
                [
                  484.1015625,
                  522.0703125
                ],
                [
                  484.1015625,
                  558.421875
                ],
                [
                  100.0,
                  558.421875
                ]
              ],
              "children": null,
              "section_hierarchy": {
                "1": "/page/214/SectionHeader/1",
                "3": "/page/219/SectionHeader/9"
              },
              "images": {}
            },
            {
              "id": "/page/219/ListItem/12",
              "block_type": "ListItem",
              "html": "<li> Is something happening that shouldn't? Find code in your program that performs that function and see if it is executing when it shouldn't.</li>",
              "polygon": [
                [
                  100.0,
                  569.25
                ],
                [
                  484.1015625,
                  569.25
                ],
                [
                  484.1015625,
                  592.453125
                ],
                [
                  100.0,
                  592.453125
                ]
              ],
              "children": null,
              "section_hierarchy": {
                "1": "/page/214/SectionHeader/1",
                "3": "/page/219/SectionHeader/9"
              },
              "images": {}
            },
            {
              "id": "/page/219/ListItem/13",
              "block_type": "ListItem",
              "html": "<li> Is a section of code producing an effect that is not what you expected? Make sure that you understand the code in question, especially if it involves invocations to functions or methods in other Python modules. Read the documentation for the functions you invoke. Try them out by writing simple test cases and checking the results.</li>",
              "polygon": [
                [
                  99.9580078125,
                  603.28125
                ],
                [
                  483.50390625,
                  603.28125
                ],
                [
                  483.50390625,
                  651.0
                ],
                [
                  99.9580078125,
                  651.0
                ]
              ],
              "children": null,
              "section_hierarchy": {
                "1": "/page/214/SectionHeader/1",
                "3": "/page/219/SectionHeader/9"
              },
              "images": {}
            }
          ],
          "section_hierarchy": {
            "1": "/page/214/SectionHeader/1",
            "3": "/page/219/SectionHeader/9"
          },
          "images": null
        },
        {
          "id": "/page/219/Text/14",
          "block_type": "Text",
          "html": "<p>In order to program, you need to have a mental model of how programs work. If you write a program that doesn't do what you expect, very often the problem is not in the program; it's in your mental model.</p>",
          "polygon": [
            [
              85.763671875,
              665.15625
            ],
            [
              484.1015625,
              665.15625
            ],
            [
              484.1015625,
              701.0
            ],
            [
              85.763671875,
              701.0
            ]
          ],
          "children": null,
          "section_hierarchy": {
            "1": "/page/214/SectionHeader/1",
            "3": "/page/219/SectionHeader/9"
          },
          "images": {}
        }
      ],
      "section_hierarchy": {
        "1": "/page/214/SectionHeader/1",
        "3": "/page/219/SectionHeader/9"
      },
      "images": null
    },
    {
      "id": "/page/220/Page/169",
      "block_type": "Page",
      "html": "<content-ref src='/page/220/PageHeader/0'></content-ref><content-ref src='/page/220/PageHeader/23'></content-ref><content-ref src='/page/220/Text/1'></content-ref><content-ref src='/page/220/Text/2'></content-ref><content-ref src='/page/220/SectionHeader/3'></content-ref><content-ref src='/page/220/Text/4'></content-ref><content-ref src='/page/220/Text/5'></content-ref><content-ref src='/page/220/Text/6'></content-ref><content-ref src='/page/220/Text/7'></content-ref><content-ref src='/page/220/Code/8'></content-ref><content-ref src='/page/220/Text/9'></content-ref><content-ref src='/page/220/Text/10'></content-ref><content-ref src='/page/220/Text/11'></content-ref><content-ref src='/page/220/Text/12'></content-ref><content-ref src='/page/220/Text/13'></content-ref><content-ref src='/page/220/Text/14'></content-ref><content-ref src='/page/220/Text/15'></content-ref><content-ref src='/page/220/SectionHeader/16'></content-ref><content-ref src='/page/220/Text/17'></content-ref><content-ref src='/page/220/Code/18'></content-ref><content-ref src='/page/220/Text/19'></content-ref><content-ref src='/page/220/Text/20'></content-ref><content-ref src='/page/220/Text/21'></content-ref><content-ref src='/page/220/Text/22'></content-ref>",
      "polygon": [
        [
          0.0,
