        ]
      ],
      "children": [
        {
          "id": "/page/220/PageHeader/0",
          "block_type": "PageHeader",
          "html": "<p><b>A.3. Semantic errors 199</b></p>",
          "polygon": [
            [
              128.794921875,
              61.0
            ],
            [
              526.0,
              61.0
            ],
            [
              526.0,
              71.0
            ],
            [
              128.794921875,
              71.0
            ]
          ],
          "children": null,
          "section_hierarchy": {
            "1": "/page/214/SectionHeader/1",
            "3": "/page/219/SectionHeader/9"
          },
          "images": {}
        },
        {
          "id": "/page/220/PageHeader/23",
          "block_type": "PageHeader",
          "html": "<p></p>",
          "polygon": [
            [
              510.697265625,
              60.521484375
            ],
            [
              525.638671875,
              60.521484375
            ],
            [
              525.638671875,
              69.99609375
            ],
            [
              510.697265625,
              69.99609375
            ]
          ],
          "children": null,
          "section_hierarchy": {
            "1": "/page/214/SectionHeader/1",
            "3": "/page/219/SectionHeader/9"
          },
          "images": {}
        },
        {
          "id": "/page/220/Text/1",
          "block_type": "Text",
          "html": "<p>The best way to correct your mental model is to break the program into its components (usually the functions and methods) and test each component independently. Once you find the discrepancy between your model and reality, you can solve the problem.</p>",
          "polygon": [
            [
              128.6455078125,
              87.3017578125
            ],
            [
              526.0,
              87.3017578125
            ],
            [
              526.0,
              123.0
            ],
            [
              128.6455078125,
              123.0
            ]
          ],
          "children": null,
          "section_hierarchy": {
            "1": "/page/214/SectionHeader/1",
            "3": "/page/219/SectionHeader/9"
          },
          "images": {}
        },
        {
          "id": "/page/220/Text/2",
          "block_type": "Text",
          "html": "<p>Of course, you should be building and testing components as you develop the program. If you encounter a problem, there should be only a small amount of new code that is not known to be correct.</p>",
          "polygon": [
            [
              128.3466796875,
              132.0
            ],
            [
              526.53515625,
              132.0
            ],
            [
              526.53515625,
              167.0
            ],
            [
              128.3466796875,
              167.0
            ]
          ],
          "children": null,
          "section_hierarchy": {
            "1": "/page/214/SectionHeader/1",
            "3": "/page/219/SectionHeader/9",
            "4": "/page/220/SectionHeader/3"
          },
          "images": {}
        },
        {
          "id": "/page/220/SectionHeader/3",
          "block_type": "SectionHeader",
          "html": "<h4><b>A.3.2 I've got a big hairy expression and it doesn't do what I expect.</b></h4>",
          "polygon": [
            [
              128.0478515625,
              191.0
            ],
            [
              505.01953125,
              191.0
            ],
            [
              505.01953125,
              203.220703125
            ],
            [
              128.0478515625,
              203.220703125
            ]
          ],
          "children": null,
          "section_hierarchy": {
            "1": "/page/214/SectionHeader/1",
            "3": "/page/219/SectionHeader/9",
            "4": "/page/220/SectionHeader/3"
          },
          "images": {}
        },
        {
          "id": "/page/220/Text/4",
          "block_type": "Text",
          "html": "<p>Writing complex expressions is fine as long as they are readable, but they can be hard to debug. It is often a good idea to break a complex expression into a series of assignments to temporary variables.</p>",
          "polygon": [
            [
              128.6455078125,
              212.888671875
            ],
            [
              526.0,
              212.888671875
            ],
            [
              526.0,
              247.0
            ],
            [
              128.6455078125,
              247.0
            ]
          ],
          "children": null,
          "section_hierarchy": {
            "1": "/page/214/SectionHeader/1",
            "3": "/page/219/SectionHeader/9",
            "4": "/page/220/SectionHeader/3"
          },
          "images": {}
        },
        {
          "id": "/page/220/Text/5",
          "block_type": "Text",
          "html": "<p>For example:</p>",
          "polygon": [
            [
              127.599609375,
              255.814453125
            ],
            [
              187.0,
              255.814453125
            ],
            [
              187.0,
              266.0
            ],
            [
              127.599609375,
              266.0
            ]
          ],
          "children": null,
          "section_hierarchy": {
            "1": "/page/214/SectionHeader/1",
            "3": "/page/219/SectionHeader/9",
            "4": "/page/220/SectionHeader/3"
          },
          "images": {}
        },
        {
          "id": "/page/220/Text/6",
          "block_type": "Text",
          "html": "<p>self.hands[i].addCard(self.hands[self.findNeighbor(i)].popCard())</p>",
          "polygon": [
            [
              128.794921875,
              271.0
            ],
            [
              470.35546875,
              271.0
            ],
            [
              470.35546875,
              281.14453125
            ],
            [
              128.794921875,
              281.14453125
            ]
          ],
          "children": null,
          "section_hierarchy": {
            "1": "/page/214/SectionHeader/1",
            "3": "/page/219/SectionHeader/9",
            "4": "/page/220/SectionHeader/3"
          },
          "images": {}
        },
        {
          "id": "/page/220/Text/7",
          "block_type": "Text",
          "html": "<p>This can be rewritten as:</p>",
          "polygon": [
            [
              129.69140625,
              285.591796875
            ],
            [
              237.0,
              285.591796875
            ],
            [
              237.0,
              297.0
            ],
            [
              129.69140625,
              297.0
            ]
          ],
          "children": null,
          "section_hierarchy": {
            "1": "/page/214/SectionHeader/1",
            "3": "/page/219/SectionHeader/9",
            "4": "/page/220/SectionHeader/3"
          },
          "images": {}
        },
        {
          "id": "/page/220/Code/8",
          "block_type": "Code",
          "html": "<pre>neighbor = self.findNeighbor(i)\npickedCard = self.hands[neighbor].popCard()\nself.hands[i].addCard(pickedCard)</pre>",
          "polygon": [
            [
              129.61669921875,
              300.8671875
            ],
            [
              355.306640625,
              300.8671875
            ],
            [
              355.0,
              336.0
            ],
            [
              128.42138671875,
              336.0
            ]
          ],
          "children": null,
          "section_hierarchy": {
            "1": "/page/214/SectionHeader/1",
            "3": "/page/219/SectionHeader/9",
            "4": "/page/220/SectionHeader/3"
          },
          "images": {}
        },
        {
          "id": "/page/220/Text/9",
          "block_type": "Text",
          "html": "<p>The explicit version is easier to read because the variable names provide additional documentation, and it is easier to debug because you can check the types of the intermediate variables and display their values.</p>",
          "polygon": [
            [
              128.6455078125,
              341.0
            ],
            [
              526.53515625,
              341.0
            ],
            [
              526.53515625,
              376.0
            ],
            [
              128.6455078125,
              376.0
            ]
          ],
          "children": null,
          "section_hierarchy": {
            "1": "/page/214/SectionHeader/1",
            "3": "/page/219/SectionHeader/9",
            "4": "/page/220/SectionHeader/3"
          },
          "images": {}
        },
        {
          "id": "/page/220/Text/10",
          "block_type": "Text",
          "html": "<p>Another problem that can occur with big expressions is that the order of evaluation may not be what you expect. For example, if you are translating the expression x 2π into Python, you might write:</p>",
          "polygon": [
            [
              129.09375,
              384.01171875
            ],
            [
              527.1328125,
              384.01171875
            ],
            [
              527.1328125,
              419.0
            ],
            [
              129.09375,
              419.0
            ]
          ],
          "children": null,
          "section_hierarchy": {
            "1": "/page/214/SectionHeader/1",
            "3": "/page/219/SectionHeader/9",
            "4": "/page/220/SectionHeader/3"
          },
          "images": {}
        },
        {
          "id": "/page/220/Text/11",
          "block_type": "Text",
          "html": "<p>y = x / 2 * math.pi</p>",
          "polygon": [
            [
              129.16845703125,
              423.0703125
            ],
            [
              229.0,
              423.0703125
            ],
            [
              229.0,
              434.0
            ],
            [
              129.16845703125,
              434.0
            ]
          ],
          "children": null,
          "section_hierarchy": {
            "1": "/page/214/SectionHeader/1",
            "3": "/page/219/SectionHeader/9",
            "4": "/page/220/SectionHeader/3"
          },
          "images": {}
        },
        {
          "id": "/page/220/Text/12",
          "block_type": "Text",
          "html": "<p>That is not correct because multiplication and division have the same precedence and are evaluated from left to right. So this expression computes xπ/2.</p>",
          "polygon": [
            [
              128.49609375,
              438.15234375
            ],
            [
              526.53515625,
              438.15234375
            ],
            [
              526.53515625,
              462.0
            ],
            [
              128.49609375,
              462.0
            ]
          ],
          "children": null,
          "section_hierarchy": {
            "1": "/page/214/SectionHeader/1",
            "3": "/page/219/SectionHeader/9",
            "4": "/page/220/SectionHeader/3"
          },
          "images": {}
        },
        {
          "id": "/page/220/Text/13",
          "block_type": "Text",
          "html": "<p>A good way to debug expressions is to add parentheses to make the order of evaluation explicit:</p>",
          "polygon": [
            [
              128.6455078125,
              470.25
            ],
            [
              526.53515625,
              470.25
            ],
            [
              526.53515625,
              493.0
            ],
            [
              128.6455078125,
              493.0
            ]
          ],
          "children": null,
          "section_hierarchy": {
            "1": "/page/214/SectionHeader/1",
            "3": "/page/219/SectionHeader/9",
            "4": "/page/220/SectionHeader/3"
          },
          "images": {}
        },
        {
          "id": "/page/220/Text/14",
          "block_type": "Text",
          "html": "<p>y = x / (2 * math.pi)</p>",
          "polygon": [
            [
              132.30615234375,
              498.0
            ],
            [
              245.0,
              498.0
            ],
            [
              245.0,
              508.1484375
            ],
            [
              132.30615234375,
              508.1484375
            ]
          ],
          "children": null,
          "section_hierarchy": {
            "1": "/page/214/SectionHeader/1",
            "3": "/page/219/SectionHeader/9",
            "4": "/page/220/SectionHeader/3"
          },
          "images": {}
        },
        {
          "id": "/page/220/Text/15",
          "block_type": "Text",
          "html": "<p>Whenever you are not sure of the order of evaluation, use parentheses. Not only will the program be correct (in the sense of doing what you intended), it will also be more readable for other people who haven't memorized the rules of precedence.</p>",
          "polygon": [
            [
              128.9443359375,
              512.40234375
            ],
            [
              526.53515625,
              512.40234375
            ],
            [
              526.53515625,
              547.0
            ],
            [
              128.9443359375,
              547.0
            ]
          ],
          "children": null,
          "section_hierarchy": {
            "1": "/page/214/SectionHeader/1",
            "3": "/page/219/SectionHeader/9",
            "4": "/page/220/SectionHeader/16"
          },
          "images": {}
        },
        {
          "id": "/page/220/SectionHeader/16",
          "block_type": "SectionHeader",
          "html": "<h4><b>A.3.3 I've got a function or method that doesn't return what I expect.</b></h4>",
          "polygon": [
            [
              128.794921875,
              571.5703125
            ],
            [
              509.501953125,
              571.5703125
            ],
            [
              509.501953125,
              584.0
            ],
            [
              128.794921875,
              584.0
            ]
          ],
          "children": null,
          "section_hierarchy": {
            "1": "/page/214/SectionHeader/1",
            "3": "/page/219/SectionHeader/9",
            "4": "/page/220/SectionHeader/16"
          },
          "images": {}
        },
        {
          "id": "/page/220/Text/17",
          "block_type": "Text",
          "html": "<p>If you have a return statement with a complex expression, you don't have a chance to print the return value before returning. Again, you can use a temporary variable. For example, instead of:</p>",
          "polygon": [
            [
              128.6455078125,
              592.83984375
            ],
            [
              527.1328125,
              592.83984375
            ],
            [
              527.1328125,
              628.41796875
            ],
            [
              128.6455078125,
              628.41796875
            ]
          ],
          "children": null,
          "section_hierarchy": {
            "1": "/page/214/SectionHeader/1",
            "3": "/page/219/SectionHeader/9",
            "4": "/page/220/SectionHeader/16"
          },
          "images": {}
        },
        {
          "id": "/page/220/Code/18",
          "block_type": "Code",
          "html": "<pre>return self.hands[i].removeMatches()</pre>",
          "polygon": [
            [
              127.82373046875,
              632.28515625
            ],
            [
              318.251953125,
              632.28515625
            ],
            [
              318.251953125,
              643.11328125
            ],
            [
              127.82373046875,
              643.11328125
            ]
          ],
          "children": null,
          "section_hierarchy": {
            "1": "/page/214/SectionHeader/1",
            "3": "/page/219/SectionHeader/9",
            "4": "/page/220/SectionHeader/16"
          },
          "images": {}
        },
        {
          "id": "/page/220/Text/19",
          "block_type": "Text",
          "html": "<p>you could write:</p>",
          "polygon": [
            [
              127.8984375,
              648.0
            ],
            [
              202.0,
              648.0
            ],
            [
              202.0,
              658.96875
            ],
            [
              127.8984375,
              658.96875
            ]
          ],
          "children": null,
          "section_hierarchy": {
            "1": "/page/214/SectionHeader/1",
            "3": "/page/219/SectionHeader/9",
            "4": "/page/220/SectionHeader/16"
          },
          "images": {}
        },
        {
          "id": "/page/220/Text/20",
          "block_type": "Text",
          "html": "<p>count = self.hands[i].removeMatches()</p>",
          "polygon": [
            [
              129.16845703125,
              663.0
            ],
            [
              323.0,
              663.0
            ],
            [
              323.0,
              673.27734375
            ],
            [
              129.16845703125,
              673.27734375
            ]
          ],
          "children": null,
          "section_hierarchy": {
            "1": "/page/214/SectionHeader/1",
            "3": "/page/219/SectionHeader/9",
            "4": "/page/220/SectionHeader/16"
          },
          "images": {}
        },
        {
          "id": "/page/220/Text/21",
          "block_type": "Text",
          "html": "<p>return count</p>",
          "polygon": [
            [
              128.794921875,
              676.0
            ],
            [
              192.146484375,
              676.0
            ],
            [
              192.0,
              686.42578125
            ],
            [
              127.599609375,
              686.42578125
            ]
          ],
          "children": null,
          "section_hierarchy": {
            "1": "/page/214/SectionHeader/1",
            "3": "/page/219/SectionHeader/9",
            "4": "/page/220/SectionHeader/16"
          },
          "images": {}
        },
        {
          "id": "/page/220/Text/22",
          "block_type": "Text",
          "html": "<p>Now you have the opportunity to display the value of count before returning.</p>",
          "polygon": [
            [
