        {
          "id": "/page/236/Text/8",
          "block_type": "Text",
          "html": "<p>Figure C.5 shows the result. copy.copy make a shallow copy, so box and box2 have their own width and height, but they share the same embedded Point object. This kind of sharing is usually fine with immutable objects, but with mutable types, it is highly errorprone.</p>",
