            "3": "/page/236/SectionHeader/9",
            "4": "/page/237/SectionHeader/5"
          },
          "images": {}
        },
        {
          "id": "/page/237/Text/8",
          "block_type": "Text",
          "html": "<p>This diagram might clarify two points of common confusion: (1) the difference between the class object, Point, and the instance of Point, obj, and (2) the difference between the function object created when instantiate is defined, and the frame created with it is called.</p>",
          "polygon": [
